return {
  ["magicitem.libram-of-souls-and-flesh.tce2014"]={title="Libram of Souls and Flesh",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 129\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWith covers made of skin and fittings of bone, this tome is cold to the touch, and it whispers faintly. When found, the book contains the following spells, which are wizard spells for you while you are attuned to the book: animate dead, circle of death, false life, finger of death, speak with dead, TCE, and vampiric touch. It functions as a spellbook for you.\n\nWhile you are holding the book, you can use it as a spellcasting focus for your wizard spells.\n\nThe book has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. You can use the charges in the following ways while holding it:\n\n• If you spend 1 minute studying the book, you can expend 1 charge to replace one of your prepared wizard spells with a different spell in the book. The new spell must be of the necromancy school.\n\n• As an action, you can expend 1 charge to take on a semblance of undeath for 10 minutes. For the duration, you take on a deathly appearance, and undead creatures are indifferent to you, unless you have damaged them. You also appear undead to all outward inspection and to spells used to determine the target's status. The effect ends if you deal damage or force a creature to make a saving throw."},
  ["creature.lich.mm2014"]={title="Lich",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 202\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 135 (18d8 + 54)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 16 | INT 20 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus up to five other languages\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the lich fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nIf it has a phylactery, a destroyed lich gains a new body in 1d10 days, regaining all its hit points and becoming active again. The new body appears within 5 feet of the phylactery.\n\nTurn Resistance\n\nThe lich has advantage on saving throws against any effect that turns undead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nParalyzing Touch\n\nms 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h10 (3d6) cold damage. The target must succeed on a 18 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCantrip\n\nThe lich casts a cantrip.\n\nParalyzing Touch (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe lich uses its Paralyzing Touch.\n\nFrightening Gaze (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe lich fixes its gaze on one creature it can see within 10 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 18 Wisdom saving throw against this magic or become frightened for 1 minute. The frightened target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a target's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the target is immune to the lich's gaze for the next 24 hours.\n\nDisrupt Life (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nEach non-undead creature within 20 feet of the lich must make a 18 Constitution saving throw against this magic, taking 21 (6d6) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.lich.xmm2024"]={title="Lich",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 196\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 315 (42d8 + 126)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 16 | INT 21 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the lich fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpirit Jar\n\nIf destroyed, the lich reforms in 1d10 days if it has a spirit jar, reviving with all its XPHB. The new body appears in an unoccupied space within the lich's lair.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nProtective Magic\n\nFrightening Gaze\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe lich makes three attacks, using Eldritch Burst or Paralyzing Touch in any combination.\n\nEldritch Burst\n\nm,r 12, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h31 (4d12 + 5) Force damage.\n\nParalyzing Touch\n\nm 12, reach 5 ft. h15 (3d6 + 5) Cold damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the lich's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDeathly Teleport\n\nThe lich teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see, and each creature within 10 feet of the space it left takes 11 (2d10) Necrotic damage.\n\nDisrupt Life\n\ncon 20, each creature that isn't an Undead in a 20-foot XPHB originating from the lich. actSaveFail 31 (9d6) Necrotic damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage. actSaveSuccessOrFail The lich can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.lichen-lich.cm2014"]={title="Lichen Lich",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 225 (30d8 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 20 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Druidic, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the lich fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nIf it has a phylactery, a destroyed lich gains a new body in 1d10 days, regaining all its hit points and becoming active again. The new body appears within 5 feet of the phylactery.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe lich makes four attacks.\n\nPoisonous Touch\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h17 (5d6) poison damage, and the target must succeed on a 19 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nWither\n\nrs 9 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h14 (4d6) necrotic damage.\n\nFire Storm (7th-Level Spell; 1/Day)\n\nThe lich fills up to ten 10-foot cubes with fire. Every cube must be within 150 feet of the lich and occupy a space the lich can see, and each cube must have at least one face adjacent to the face of another cube. Each creature in the area must make a 19 Dexterity saving throw, taking 38 (7d10) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The fire ignites flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried. If the lich chooses, plant life in the area is unaffected by the spell.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe lich makes an attack.\n\nPoison Prick (Cost 2 Actions)\n\nThe lich targets one poisoned creature it can see within 30 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 19 Constitution saving throw or fall unconscious until the poisoned condition ends on it.\n\nSap Life (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe lich targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 19 Constitution saving throw or take 11 (2d10) necrotic damage. The lich regains a number of hit points equal to the amount of damage that the creature takes."},
  ["creature.lief-lipsiege.cos2014"]={title="Lief Lipsiege",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["subclass.life-domain.phb2014.cleric.life.0"]={title="Life Domain",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Bonus Proficiency\n\nPagina: 60\n\nWhen you choose this domain at 1st level, you gain proficiency with heavy armor.\n\nNivel 1 - Bonus Proficiency\n\nNivel 1 - Disciple of Life\n\nPagina: 60\n\nAlso starting at 1st level, your healing spells are more effective. Whenever you use a spell of 1st level or higher to restore hit points to a creature, the creature regains additional hit points equal to 2 + the spell's level.\n\nNivel 1 - Disciple of Life\n\nNivel 1 - Life Domain\n\nPagina: 60\n\nThe Life domain focuses on the vibrant positive energy—one of the fundamental forces of the universe—that sustains all life. The gods of life promote vitality and health through healing the sick and wounded, caring for those in need, and driving away the forces of death and undeath. Almost any non-evil deity can claim influence over this domain, particularly agricultural deities (such as Chauntea, Eberron, and Greek), sun gods (such as Lathander, Greyhawk, and Egyptian), gods of healing or endurance (such as Ilmater, Dragonlance, Greek, and Celtic), and gods of home and community (such as Greek, Egyptian, and Eberron).\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, you add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | bless, cure wounds\n\n3rd | lesser restoration, spiritual weapon\n\n5th | beacon of hope, revivify\n\n7th | death ward, guardian of faith\n\n9th | mass cure wounds, raise dead\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Preserve Life\n\nPagina: 60\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to heal the badly injured.\n\nAs an action, you present your holy symbol and evoke healing energy that can restore a number of hit points equal to five times your cleric level. Choose any creatures within 30 feet of you, and divide those hit points among them. This feature can restore a creature to no more than half of its hit point maximum. You can't use this feature on an undead or a construct.\n\nNivel 3 - Channel Divinity: Preserve Life\n\nNivel 3 - Disciple of Life\n\nPagina: 73\n\nWhen a spell you cast with a spell slot restores XPHB to a creature, that creature regains additional XPHB on the turn you cast the spell. The additional XPHB equal 2 plus the spell slot's level.\n\nNivel 3 - Disciple of Life\n\nNivel 3 - Life Domain\n\nNivel 3 - Life Domain\n\nPagina: 73\n\nSoothe the Hurts of the World\n\nThe Life Domain focuses on the positive energy that helps sustain all life in the multiverse. Clerics who tap into this domain are masters of healing, using that life force to cure many hurts.\n\nExistence itself relies on the positive energy associated with this domain, so a Cleric of almost any religious tradition might choose it. This domain is particularly associated with agricultural deities, gods of healing or endurance, and gods of home and community. Religious orders of healing also seek the magic of this domain.\n\nNivel 3 - Life Domain Spells\n\nPagina: 73\n\nYour connection to this divine domain ensures you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Life Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Prepared Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Preserve Life\n\nPagina: 73\n\nAs a XPHB action, you present your XPHB and expend a use of your Channel Divinity to evoke healing energy that can restore a number of XPHB equal to five times your Cleric level. Choose XPHB creatures within 30 feet of yourself (which can include you), and divide those XPHB among them. This feature can restore a creature to no more than half its XPHB maximum.\n\nNivel 3 - Preserve Life\n\nNivel 6 - Blessed Healer\n\nPagina: 60\n\nBeginning at 6th level, the healing spells you cast on others heal you as well. When you cast a spell of 1st level or higher that restores hit points to a creature other than you, you regain hit points equal to 2 + the spell's level.\n\nNivel 6 - Blessed Healer\n\nPagina: 74\n\nThe healing spells you cast on others heal you as well. Immediately after you cast a spell with a spell slot that restores XPHB to one or more creatures other than yourself, you regain XPHB equal to 2 plus the spell slot's level.\n\nNivel 6 - Blessed Healer\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Divine Strike feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Divine Strike\n\nPagina: 60\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 radiant damage to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8.\n\nNivel 17 - Supreme Healing\n\nPagina: 60\n\nStarting at 17th level, when you would normally roll one or more dice to restore hit points with a spell, you instead use the highest number possible for each die. For example, instead of restoring 2d6 hit points to a creature, you restore 12.\n\nNivel 17 - Supreme Healing\n\nPagina: 74\n\nWhen you would normally roll one or more dice to restore XPHB to a creature with a spell or Channel Divinity, don't roll those dice for the healing; instead use the highest number possible for each die. For example, instead of restoring 2d6 XPHB to a creature with a spell, you restore 12."},
  ["feature.life-domain.phb2014.cleric.life.1"]={title="Life Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\nThe Life domain focuses on the vibrant positive energy—one of the fundamental forces of the universe—that sustains all life. The gods of life promote vitality and health through healing the sick and wounded, caring for those in need, and driving away the forces of death and undeath. Almost any non-evil deity can claim influence over this domain, particularly agricultural deities (such as Chauntea, Eberron, and Greek), sun gods (such as Lathander, Greyhawk, and Egyptian), gods of healing or endurance (such as Ilmater, Dragonlance, Greek, and Celtic), and gods of home and community (such as Greek, Egyptian, and Eberron).\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, you add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | bless, cure wounds\n\n3rd | lesser restoration, spiritual weapon\n\n5th | beacon of hope, revivify\n\n7th | death ward, guardian of faith\n\n9th | mass cure wounds, raise dead"},
  ["feature.life-domain.phb2014.cleric.life.3"]={title="Life Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
