ou cast a spell of 1st level or higher that restores hit points to a creature other than you, you regain hit points equal to 2 + the spell's level.\n\nNivel 6 - Blessed Healer\n\nPagina: 74\n\nThe healing spells you cast on others heal you as well. Immediately after you cast a spell with a spell slot that restores XPHB to one or more creatures other than yourself, you regain XPHB equal to 2 plus the spell slot's level.\n\nNivel 6 - Blessed Healer\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Divine Strike feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Divine Strike\n\nPagina: 60\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 radiant damage to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8.\n\nNivel 17 - Supreme Healing\n\nPagina: 60\n\nStarting at 17th level, when you would normally roll one or more dice to restore hit points with a spell, you instead use the highest number possible for each die. For example, instead of restoring 2d6 hit points to a creature, you restore 12.\n\nNivel 17 - Supreme Healing\n\nPagina: 74\n\nWhen you would normally roll one or more dice to restore XPHB to a creature with a spell or Channel Divinity, don't roll those dice for the healing; instead use the highest number possible for each die. For example, instead of restoring 2d6 XPHB to a creature with a spell, you restore 12."},
  ["feature.life-domain.xphb2024.cleric.life.3"]={title="Life Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 73\n\nSoothe the Hurts of the World\n\nThe Life Domain focuses on the positive energy that helps sustain all life in the multiverse. Clerics who tap into this domain are masters of healing, using that life force to cure many hurts.\n\nExistence itself relies on the positive energy associated with this domain, so a Cleric of almost any religious tradition might choose it. This domain is particularly associated with agricultural deities, gods of healing or endurance, and gods of home and community. Religious orders of healing also seek the magic of this domain."},
  ["feature.life-domain-spells.xphb2024.cleric.life.3"]={title="Life Domain Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 73\n\nYour connection to this divine domain ensures you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Life Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Prepared Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["spell.life-transference.xge2024"]={title="Life Transference",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 160\n\nYou sacrifice some of your health to mend another creature's injuries. You take 4d8 necrotic damage, which can't be reduced in any way, and one creature of your choice that you can see within range regains a number of hit points equal to twice the necrotic damage you take."},
  ["creature.lifecraft-elephant.psk2014"]={title="Lifecraft Elephant",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned"},
  ["optionalfeature.lifedrinker.phb2014"]={title="Lifedrinker",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nWhen you hit a creature with your pact weapon, the creature takes extra necrotic damage equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1)."},
  ["optionalfeature.lifedrinker.xphb2024"]={title="Lifedrinker",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 156\n\nOnce per turn when you hit a creature with your pact weapon, you can deal an extra 1d6 Necrotic, Psychic, or Radiant damage (your choice) to the creature, and you can expend one of your XPHB to roll it and regain a number of XPHB equal to the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum of 1 XPHB)."},
  ["charoption.lifelong-companion.mot2014"]={title="Lifelong Companion",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nBehind many heroes is another hero whose greatness comes from the support and love they offer. Haktos had his beloved Perynes, Renata was accompanied by her servant Karados, and Siona sailed with her devoted crew. Like these partners, you are great and make others great. Consider the Companion Relationships table when determining your legendary connection. Any relationship with another player's character requires that player's consent. Additionally, you gain the following traits.\n\nBoon Aura\n\nYour allies within 5 feet of you have advantage on saving throws against being frightened or charmed, provided you aren't incapacitated.\n\nCompanion's Protection\n\nWhen a creature you can see within 5 feet of you is hit by an attack roll, you can use your reaction to cause the attack to hit you instead. Once you use this trait, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest.\n\nd6 | Relationship\n\n1 | Another character is my lover or dearest friend.\n\n2 | Another character is my sibling.\n\n3 | Another character is my parent or child.\n\n4 | Another character is a champion of my god.\n\n5 | After admiring another character from afar, I've finally won a position by their side.\n\n6 | I want nothing more than for another character to recognize my devotion and love me in return."},
  ["magicitem.lifewell-tattoo.tce2014"]={title="Lifewell Tattoo",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 129\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nProduced by a special needle, this magic tattoo features symbols of life and rebirth.\n\nTattoo Attunement\n\nTo attune to this item, you hold the needle to your skin where you want the tattoo to appear, pressing the needle there throughout the attunement process. When the attunement is complete, the needle turns into the ink that becomes the tattoo, which appears on the skin.\n\nIf your attunement to the tattoo ends, the tattoo vanishes, and the needle reappears in your space.\n\nNecrotic Resistance\n\nYou have resistance to necrotic damage.\n\nLife Ward\n\nWhen you would be reduced to 0 hit points, you drop to 1 hit point instead. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.lifferlas.skt2014"]={title="Lifferlas",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 250\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / H\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 59 (7d12 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 6 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile Lifferlas remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal tree.\n\nRoleplaying Information\n\nA druid of the Emerald Enclave awakened the tree Lifferlas with a spell. Goldenfields is his home, its people his friends. Children like to carve their name and initials into his body and hang from his boughs, and he's happy with that.\n\nIdeal: \"I exist to protect the people and plants of Goldenfields.\"\n\nBond: \"Children are wonderful. I would do anything to make them feel happy and safe.\"\n\nFlaw: \"I can't remember people's names and often get them mixed up.\"\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nLifferlas makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (3d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["spell.light.phb2014"]={title="Light",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 255\n\nYou touch one object that is no larger than 10 feet in any dimension. Until the spell ends, the object sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for an additional 20 feet. The light can be colored as you like. Completely covering the object with something opaque blocks the light. The spell ends if you cast it again or dismiss it as an action.\n\nIf you target an object held or worn by a hostile creature, that creature must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw to avoid the spell."},
  ["spell.light.xphb2024"]={title="Light",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 292\n\nYou touch one Large or smaller object that isn't being worn or carried by someone else. Until the spell ends, the object sheds XPHB in a 20-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 20 feet. The light can be colored as you like.\n\nCovering the object with something opaque blocks the light. The spell ends if you cast it again."},
  ["feat.light-bringer.abh2014"]={title="Light Bringer",subtitle="Feat - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nSacred Magic\n\nYou learn the XPHB spell and can cast it without Material components. If you already know that cantrip, you learn a different Cleric cantrip of your choice. The spell's spellcasting ability is the ability increased by this feat.\n\nSolar Luminance\n\nWhen you cast XPHB, you can have the light from the spell be sunlight. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nSun's Healing\n\nAs a XPHB while within sunlight, you can expend one of your XPHB, roll the die, and regain a number of XPHB equal to the roll. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB."},
  ["item.light-crossbow.phb2014"]={title="Light Crossbow",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.light-crossbow.xphb2024"]={title="Light Crossbow",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.light-devourer.crcotn2014"]={title="Light Devourer",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 119 (14d8 + 56)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, swim: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 18 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: radiant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLight Absorption\n\nIf the light devourer spends any part of its turn in an area of bright light or is subjected to radiant damage, it radiates dim light in a 10-foot radius for 1 hour.\n\nWater Breathing\n\nThe light devourer can breathe only underwater.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe light devourer makes two Bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h21 (5d6 + 4) piercing damage, or radiant damage if the light devourer is radiating light (see Light Absorption).\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRadiant Discharge\n\nIf the light devourer is radiating light (see Light Absorption), it releases the light stored in its body in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on itself, then ceases to radiate light. Each creature in the sphere must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 24 (7d6) radiant damage on a failed saving throw, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["subclass.light-domain.phb2014.cleric.light.0"]={title="Light Domain",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Bonus Cantrip\n\nPagina: 60\n\nWhen you choose this domain at 1st level, you gain the light cantrip if you don't already know it. This cantrip doesn't count against the number of cleric cantrips you know.\n\nNivel 1 - Light Domain\n\nPagina: 60\n\nGods of light—including Helm, Lathander, Greyhawk, Dragonlance, Eberron, Celtic, Greek, and Egyptian—promote the ideals of rebirth and renewal, truth, vigilance, and beauty, often using the symbol of the sun. Some of these gods are portrayed as the sun itself or as a charioteer who guides the sun across the sky. Others are tireless sentinels whose eyes pierce every shadow and see through every deception. Some are deities of beauty and artistry, who teach that art is a vehicle for the soul's improvement. Clerics of a god of light are enlightened souls infused with radiance and the power of their gods' discerning vision, charged with chasing away lies and burning away darkness.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, you add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | burning hands, faerie fire\n\n3rd | flaming sphere, scorching ray\n\n5th | daylight, fireball\n\n7th | guardian of faith, wall of fire\n\n9th | flame strike, scrying\n\nNivel 1 - Warding Flare\n\nPagina: 60\n\nAlso at 1st level, you can interpose divine light between yourself and an attacking enemy. When you are attacked by a creature within 30 feet of you that you can see, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on the attack roll, causing light to flare before the attacker before it hits or misses. An attacker that can't be blinded is immune to this feature.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Radiance of the Dawn\n\nPagina: 60\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to harness sunlight, banishing darkness and dealing radiant damage to your foes.\n\nAs an action, you present your holy symbol, and any magical darkness within 30 feet of you is dispelled. Additionally, each hostile creature within 30 feet of you must make a Constitution saving throw. A creature takes radiant damage equal to 2d10 + your cleric level on a failed saving throw, and half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that has Cover from you is not affected.\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Radiance of the Dawn\n\nNivel 3 - Channel Divinity: Radiance of the Dawn\n\nNivel 3 - Light Domain\n\nNivel 3 - Light Domain\n\nPagina: 74\n\nBring Light to Banish Darkness\n\nThe Light Domain emphasizes the divine power to bring about blazing fire and revelation. Clerics who wield this power are enlightened souls infused with radiance and the power of their deities' discerning vision, charged with chasing away lies and burning away darkness.\n\nThe Light Domain is associated with gods of truth, vigilance, beauty, insight, and renewal. Some of these gods are identified with the sun or as charioteers who guide the sun across the sky. Others are sentinels who pierce deception. Some are deities of beauty and artistry who teach that art is a vehicle for the soul's improvement.\n\nNivel 3 - Light Domain Spells\n\nPagina: 74\n\nYour connection to this divine domain ensures you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Light Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Prepared Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Radiance of the Dawn\n\nPagina: 74\n\nAs a XPHB action, you present your XPHB and expend a use of your Channel Divinity to emit a flash of light in a 30-foot XPHB originating from yourself. Any magical XPHB—such as that created by the XPHB spell—in that area is dispelled. Additionally, each creature of your choice in that area must make a Constitution saving throw, taking Radiant damage equal to 2d10 plus your Cleric level on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nNivel 3 - Radiance of the Dawn\n\nNivel 3 - Warding Flare\n\nPagina: 74\n\nWhen a creature that you can see within 30 feet of yourself makes an attack roll, you can take a XPHB to impose XPHB on the attack roll, causing light to flare before it hits or misses.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Warding Flare\n\nNivel 6 - Improved Flare\n\nPagina: 60\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can also use your Warding Flare feature when a creature that you can see within 30 feet of you attacks a creature other than you.\n\nNivel 6 - Improved Warding Flare\n\nPagina: 75\n\nYou regain all expended uses of your Warding Flare when you finish a XPHB or XPHB.\n\nIn addition, whenever you use Warding Flare, you can give the target of the triggering attack a number of XPHB equal to 2d6 plus your Wisdom modifier.\n\nNivel 6 - Improved Warding Flare\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Potent Spellcasting feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Potent Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 60\n\nStarting at 8th level, you add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any cleric cantrip.\n\nNivel 17 - Corona of Light\n\nPagina: 60\n\nStarting at 17th level, you can use your action to activate an aura of sunlight that lasts for 1 minute or until you dismiss it using another action. You emit bright light in a 60-foot radius and dim light 30 feet beyond that. Your enemies in the bright light have disadvantage on saving throws against any spell that deals fire or radiant damage.\n\nNivel 17 - Corona of Light\n\nPagina: 75\n\nAs a XPHB action, you cause yourself to emit an aura of sunlight that lasts for 1 minute or until you dismiss it (no action required). You emit XPHB in a 60-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 30 feet. Your enemies in the XPHB have XPHB on saving throws against your Radiance of the Dawn and any spell that deals Fire or Radiant damage.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 17 - Corona of Light\n\nNivel 17 - Corona of Light"},
  ["feature.light-domain.phb2014.cleric.light.1"]={title="Light Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\nGods of light—including Helm, Lathander, Greyhawk, Dragonlance, Eberron, Celtic, Greek, and Egyptian—promote the ideals of rebirth and renewal, truth, vigilance, and beauty, often using the symbol of the sun. Some of these gods are portrayed as the sun itself or as a charioteer who guides the sun across the sky. Others are tireless sentinels whose eyes pierce every shadow and see through every deception. Some are deities of beauty and artistry, who teach that art is a vehicle for the soul's improvement. Clerics of a god of light are enlightened souls infused with radiance and the power of their gods' discerning vision, charged with chasing away lies and burning away darkness.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, you add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | burning hands, faerie fire\n\n3rd | flaming sphere, scorching ray\n\n5th | daylight, fireball\n\n7th | guardian of faith, wall of fire\n\n9th | flame strike, scrying"},
  ["feature.light-domain.phb2014.cleric.light.3"]={title="Light Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
