  ["creature.lord-soth.dsotdq2014"]={title="Lord Soth",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 19\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 228 (24d8 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 11 | CON 20 | INT 12 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal, Solamnic\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Soth fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSoth has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMarshal Undead\n\nUnless Soth is incapacitated, he and Undead creatures of his choice within 60 feet of him are immune to features that turn Undead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nSoth doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSoth makes three Forsaken Brand attacks.\n\nForsaken Brand\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) necrotic damage, and if the target is a creature, it can't regain hit points until the start of Soth's next turn.\n\nCataclysmic Fire (1/Day)\n\nSoth hurls a magical ball of fire that explodes at a point he can see within 120 feet of himself. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 19 Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 35 (10d6) fire damage and 35 (10d6) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nAdditionally, any Medium or smaller Humanoid killed by this damage, as well as every corpse of such a creature within the sphere, becomes a skeleton (see the Monster Manual) under Soth's control. The skeleton acts on Soth's initiative but immediately after his turn. Absent any other command, the skeleton tries to kill any non-Undead creature it encounters.\n\nWord of Death (1/Day)\n\nSoth points at a creature he can see within 60 feet of himself and magically commands it to die. The target must make a 19 Constitution saving throw, taking 100 necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If this damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target dies.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nImplacable Maneuver\n\nSoth moves up to his speed or commands a mount he is riding to move up to its speed. The movement from this action doesn't provoke opportunity attacks. If he or his mount moves within 5 feet of a creature during this movement, he can force the creature to make a 20 Strength saving throw. The creature is knocked prone unless it succeeds on the saving throw.\n\nStrike (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nSoth makes one Forsaken Brand attack.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nSoth uses Spellcasting."},
  ["creature.lord-soth-of-sithicus.rhw2014"]={title="Lord Soth of Sithicus",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 158\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 19\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 228 (24d8 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 11 | CON 20 | INT 12 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDarklord Restoration\n\nIf Lord Soth dies, he revives with all his XPHB in 1d10 weeks somewhere in Sithicus.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Domain)\n\nIf Lord Soth fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nLord Soth has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMarshal Undead\n\nUndead creatures of Lord Soth's choice (excluding himself) in a 60-foot XPHB originating from him have XPHB on attack rolls and saving throws. Lord Soth can't use this trait if he has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nCommanding Magic (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nLord Soth makes three Forsaken Brand attacks.\n\nForsaken Brand\n\nm 12, reach 5 ft. h10 (1d8 + 6) Slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) Necrotic damage.\n\nCataclysmic Fire {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 19, each creature in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point Lord Soth can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 24 (7d6) Fire damage plus 24 (7d6) Necrotic damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nFace of Death (1/Day)\n\ncha 19, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB originating from Lord Soth. actSaveFail 22 (4d10) Psychic damage, and the creature has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail If this damage reduces the target to 0 XPHB, the target dies.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPunish\n\nLord Soth moves up to half his XPHB, and he makes one Forsaken Brand attack.\n\nSoth's Command\n\nLord Soth casts XPHB (level 3 version), using the same spellcasting ability as Commanding Magic. Lord Soth can't take this action again until the start of his next turn."},
  ["magicitem.lord-s-ensemble.wdh2014"]={title="Lord's Ensemble",subtitle="Item Magico - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 191\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThe Masked Lords of Waterdeep don this ensemble when meeting with one another. This raiment renders each lord indistinguishable from the others. The ensemble consists of three pieces—a helm, an amulet, and a robe—that function as a single magic item when worn together, but only within the city of Waterdeep and its sewers. You become attuned to the ensemble as a single item.\n\nLord's Helm\n\nThis bucket helm covers your head and conceals your face. Screens over the eyes help to shroud your identity without blinding you. While you wear the helm, your voice is magically altered to sound genderless, and you are immune to magic that allows other creatures to read your thoughts, to determine whether you are lying, to know your alignment, or to know your creature type. Creatures can communicate telepathically with you only if you allow it.\n\nLord's Amulet\n\nThis amulet bears the crest of Waterdeep. It functions as an amulet of proof against detection and location.\n\nLord's Robe\n\nThis elegant robe functions as a ring of free action, and it creates the illusion that you have a nondescript, androgynous humanoid build and stand 6 feet tall."},
  ["feat.lordly-resolve.frhof2014"]={title="Lordly Resolve",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nStandard Bearer\n\nAs a XPHB, choose up to three creatures within 60 feet of yourself that can see you. Each target can immediately take a XPHB to right itself and end the XPHB condition, provided its XPHB isn't 0. Additionally, you bolster the targets' resolve, which lasts for 1 minute or until you have the XPHB condition. While bolstered, a target can't be possessed or gain the XPHB or XPHB condition; if a target is already possessed, XPHB, or XPHB, the target has XPHB on any new saving throw against the relevant effect.\n\nOnce you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feat.lords-alliance-agent.frhof2014"]={title="Lords' Alliance Agent",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nInspiring Strike\n\nOnce per turn when you score a XPHB against a creature, you can choose an ally within 30 feet of yourself who can see or hear you and who lacks XPHB. That ally gains XPHB.\n\nReassert Honor\n\nWhen an enemy you can see deals damage to an ally of yours that is within 5 feet of you, you have XPHB on your next attack roll against that enemy before the end of your next turn."},
  ["creature.lords-alliance-guard.oota2014"]={title="Lords' Alliance Guard",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 131\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDwarven Resilience\n\nThe guard has advantage on saving throws against poison.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHalberd\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.lords-alliance-spy.oota2014"]={title="Lords' Alliance Spy",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 131\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCunning Action\n\nOn each of its turns, the spy can use a bonus action to take the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action.\n\nSneak Attack (1/Turn)\n\nThe spy deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage when it hits a target with a weapon attack and has advantage on the attack roll, or when the target is within 5 feet of an ally of the spy that isn't incapacitated and the spy doesn't have disadvantage on the attack roll.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe spy makes two melee attacks.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nHand Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["item.lords-alliance-trinket.frhof2014"]={title="Lords' Alliance Trinket",subtitle="Item - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 164\n\nRaridade: none\n\n1d6 | Trinket\n\n1 | A scrap from a defeated army's banner\n\n2 | A bit and bridle engraved with the name of a famous steed\n\n3 | The broken blade of a sword used in a famous battle\n\n4 | The left glove of a lord who went mysteriously missing\n\n5 | An articulated toy horse and knight\n\n6 | A spaulder emblazoned with the insignia of an unidentified lord"},
  ["background.lords-alliance-vassal.frhof2014"]={title="Lords' Alliance Vassal",subtitle="Background - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["creature.lorehold-apprentice.scc2014"]={title="Lorehold Apprentice",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 15 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any two languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nScroll Bash\n\nms 4 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) thunder damage.\n\nReduce to Memory {@recharge}\n\nThundering golden energy erupts around a creature the apprentice can see within 90 feet of it. The creature must make a 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 33 (6d10) thunder damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A Construct has disadvantage on the saving throw.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nLearn from the Past (2/Day)\n\nWhen another creature within 60 feet of the apprentice misses a target with an attack roll, the apprentice magically enables the attacker to reroll the attack roll. It must use the new roll."},
  ["creature.lorehold-pledgemage.scc2014"]={title="Lorehold Pledgemage",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 60 (11d8 + 11)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any two languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe pledgemage makes two Scroll Bash attacks.\n\nScroll Bash\n\nms 5 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) thunder damage.\n\nReduce to Memory {@recharge 5}\n\nThundering golden energy erupts around a creature the pledgemage can see within 90 feet of it. The creature must make a 13 Constitution saving throw, taking 44 (8d10) thunder damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A Construct has disadvantage on the saving throw.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChronal Break (1/Day)\n\nThe pledgemage chooses a point within 30 feet of itself, shunting the minds of nearby creatures out of this moment in time. Each creature in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or be incapacitated until the end of the pledgemage's next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nLearn from the Past (2/Day)\n\nWhen another creature within 60 feet of the pledgemage misses a target with an attack roll, the pledgemage magically enables the attacker to reroll the attack roll. It must use the new roll."},
  ["magicitem.lorehold-primer.scc2014"]={title="Lorehold Primer",subtitle="Item Magico - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThe Lorehold Primer is a magic textbook created at Strixhaven's Lorehold College. The primer has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you make an Intelligence (History) or Intelligence (Religion) check while holding the primer, you can expend 1 charge to give yourself 1d4 bonus to the check, immediately after you roll the d20.\n\nIn addition, if you study the primer at the end of a long rest, you can choose one 1st-level spell from the cleric or wizard spell list. Before you finish your next long rest, you can cast the chosen spell once without a spell slot if you are holding the primer. Your spellcasting ability for this spell is your choice of Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma."},
  ["creature.lorehold-professor-of-chaos.scc2014"]={title="Lorehold Professor of Chaos",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 110 (17d8 + 34)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 19 | WIS 15 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any four languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nVoice from the Past (1/Day)\n\nThe professor can cast the contact other plane spell to contact a long-dead spirit, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe professor makes two Spectral Scroll attacks. It can also use Weight of History, if available.\n\nSpectral Scroll\n\nms 7 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) force damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nWeight of History {@recharge 5}\n\nThe professor magically compresses time around up to six creatures of its choice that it can see within 30 feet of itself. Each target must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or be restrained for 1 minute, but the restrained target's speed is halved instead of being reduced to 0. At the start of each of its turns, the restrained target takes 4 (1d8) force damage. A restrained target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.lorehold-professor-of-order.scc2014"]={title="Lorehold Professor of Order",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 104 (16d8 + 32)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 19 | WIS 15 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any four languages\n\nResistencias: force\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nVoice from the Past (1/Day)\n\nThe professor can cast the contact other plane spell to contact a long-dead spirit, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe professor makes two Repelling Burst attacks. It can also use Force Barrier, if available.\n\nRepelling Burst\n\nms 7 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) force damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 10 feet directly away from the professor and become restrained until the start of professor's next turn.\n\nForce Barrier {@recharge 5}\n\nThe professor magically creates a wall of translucent, golden force within 90 feet of itself. The wall lasts for 1 minute or until the professor uses this action again. The barrier can be a vertical or horizontal plane up to 30 feet on a side or a 10-foot-radius hemispherical dome with a floor. The wall provides Cover. It has AC 17, 30 hit points, and immunity to poison and psychic damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nArcane Stasis (2/Day)\n\nWhen a creature the professor can see within 60 feet of it casts a spell, the professor can magically lock the casting in the moment before completion. The spellcaster must succeed on a 15 saving throw using the spell's spellcasting ability, or the spell fails and is wasted."},
  ["background.lorehold-student.scc2014"]={title="Lorehold Student",subtitle="Background - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Lorehold Initiate\n\nYou gain the SCC feat and must choose Lorehold within it.\n\nIn addition, if you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic feature, the spells on the Lorehold Spells table are added to the spell list of your spellcasting class. (If you are a multiclass character with multiple spell lists, these spells are added to all of them.)\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1st | Comprehend Languages, Identify\n\n2nd | SCC, Locate Object\n\n3rd | Speak with Dead, Spirit Guardians\n\n4th | Arcane Eye, Stone Shape\n\n5th | Flame Strike, Legend Lore\n\nConsider customizing how your spells look when you cast them. Your Lorehold spells might create displays of golden light. You might use a tome or a scroll as a spellcasting focus, and your spell effects might reflect the appearance of the reference books you study.\n\nBuilding a Lorehold Character\n\nAny class or subclass that deals with knowledge of the past can be a good fit in Lorehold. Bards thrive in Lorehold, and wizards (particularly those of the PHB) are numerous among its students. Clerics (often with the PHB or PHB domains) are also quite common.\n\nFor a more unusual take on a Lorehold student, you could consider playing a barbarian with a primal connection to the past (perhaps adopting the PHB from XGE) or a paladin whose PHB gives a concrete link to history.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nMethodical historians and daring adventurers alike can be found among the ranks of Lorehold college. The Lorehold Personality Traits table suggests a variety of traits you might adopt for your character.\n\nd6 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I thrive on esoteric lore. The more obscure the historical references I can include in everyday conversation, the better.\n\n2 | By searching for these lost artifacts, I hope to find who I really am along the way.\n\n3 | I can barely go a minute without talking about my research. I have so much knowledge in my head, and it needs to be let out somewhere!\n\n4 | The spirits of the dead are so much more interesting to talk with than living classmates.\n\n5 | I can speak eloquently about the historical ramifications of an ancient war. But ask me to add two-digit numbers together, and I'm a mess.\n\n6 | In the end, it's all just entropy. Everything falls apart someday.\n\nLorehold Trinkets\n\nWhen you make your character, you may roll once on the SCC table, instead of on the phb in the PHB, for your starting trinket."},
  ["item.lorehold-trinket.scc2014"]={title="Lorehold Trinket",subtitle="Item - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWhen you make your character, you may roll once on the Lorehold Trinkets table, instead of on the phb in the PHB, for your starting trinket.\n\nd6 | Trinket\n\n1 | A map made of concentric circles that can be rotated around the page\n\n2 | A puzzle box bedecked with amber\n\n3 | A dented brass compass with a red needle\n\n4 | The head of a broken statue that houses the consciousness of a snarky sage\n\n5 | A sheet of parchment embossed with tactile lettering, glowing red\n\n6 | A broken dagger with a wavy blade and a serpentine hilt"},
  ["language.loross.idrotf2014"]={title="Loross",subtitle="Idioma - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\nLoross, a language spoken by the Netherese, is a dead tongue. Very few creatures in the world today would recognize it, much less speak it. Loross used the Draconic alphabet in its written form, while the spoken language had many similarities with Elvish, due to the cultural influence the elves had on Netherese civilization. A character who speaks Elvish can understand what a creature speaking Loross is saying, and vice versa. A character who has the Cloistered Scholar or Sage background, or a warlock who knows the Eyes of the Rune Keeper invocation, can translate written Loross without an ability check."},
  ["creature.lorry-wanwillow.dsotdq2014"]={title="Lorry Wanwillow",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 177\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead"},
  ["creature.lorthuun.oota2014"]={title="Lorthuun",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 9"},
  ["species.lorwyn-changeling.lfl2014"]={title="Lorwyn Changeling",subtitle="Especie - LFL - 2014",body="Shape Self\n\nAs an action, you can reshape your body to a two-legged Humanoid shape or to a four-legged Beast shape. While you have a Humanoid shape, you can wear clothing and armor made for a Humanoid of your size.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 120 feet.\n\nDelightful Imitator\n\nYou have proficiency in the XPHB or XPHB skill.\n\nUnpredictable Movement\n\nWhen you roll XPHB, you can immediately move up to half your XPHB, provided you don't have XPHB on the XPHB roll."},
  ["background.lorwyn-expert.lfl2014"]={title="Lorwyn Expert",subtitle="Background - LFL - 2014",body="• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiency:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["creature.lorwyn-giant.lfl2014"]={title="Lorwyn Giant",subtitle="Criatura - LFL - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / H\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 115 (11d12 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 13 | CON 18 | INT 9 | WIS 16 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe giant makes two attacks, using Stone Sword or Boulder in any combination.\n\nStone Sword\n\nm 8, reach 15 ft. h21 (3d10 + 5) Slashing damage.\n\nBoulder\n\nr 8, range 60/240 ft. h14 (2d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nName Sleep {@recharge 5}\n\nThe giant falls into a deep, restorative slumber. The giant gains 20 XPHB and has the XPHB condition until it takes damage or the end of its next turn. The giant has XPHB on ability checks and saving throws for 1 minute."},
  ["creature.losser-mirklav.wdh2014"]={title="Losser Mirklav",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 85\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 31 (9d6)"},
  ["magicitem.lost-crown-of-besilmer.pota2014"]={title="Lost Crown of Besilmer",subtitle="Item Magico - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis dwarven battle-helm consists of a sturdy open-faced steel helmet, decorated with a golden circlet above the brow from which seven small gold spikes project upward. You gain the following benefits while wearing the crown:\n\n• You have resistance to psychic damage.\n\n• You have advantage on saving throws against effects that would charm you.\n\n• You can use a bonus action to inspire one creature you can see that is within 60 feet of you and that can see or hear you. Once before the end of your next turn, the inspired creature can roll a d6 and add the number rolled to one ability check, attack roll, or saving throw it makes. This uses 1 charge from the crown. It has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."},
  ["creature.lost-sorrowsworn.mpmm2014"]={title="Lost Sorrowsworn",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 6 | WIS 7 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sorrowsworn makes two Arm Spike attacks.\n\nArm Spike\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (2d10 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nEmbrace {@recharge 4}\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h25 (4d10 + 3) piercing damage, and the target is grappled (escape 14) if it is a Medium or smaller creature. Until the grapple ends, the target is frightened, and it takes 27 (6d8) psychic damage at the end of each of its turns. The sorrowsworn can grapple only one creature at a time.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nTightening Embrace\n\nIf the sorrowsworn takes damage, the creature grappled by Embrace takes 18 (4d8) psychic damage."},
  ["creature.lothar.mabjov2014"]={title="Lothar",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 80\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 210 (28d8 + 84)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 50\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Orc\n\nImunidades: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMimicry\n\nLothar can mimic simple sounds he has heard, such as a person whispering, a baby crying, or an animal chittering. A creature that hears the sounds can tell they are imitations with a successful 15 Wisdom (Insight) check.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nLothar makes three Greataxe attacks.\n\nGreataxe (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d12 + 4) slashing damage, 14 (1d12 + 8) while in a rage.\n\nBeak (Raven or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1 piercing damage in raven form, or 6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage in hybrid form. If the target is Humanoid, it must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with wereraven MM.\n\nChange Shape\n\nLothar can use his action to polymorph into a raven-humanoid hybrid, or into a Small raven, or back into his true form, which is Humanoid. His statistics, other than his size, are the same in each form. Any equipment he is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. Lothar reverts to his true form if he dies.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRage\n\nLothar rages for 1 minute. During his rage he has advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. He gains a +4 bonus to damage while he is in a rage. He has resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage while in a rage. Lothar can't cast spells while in a rage."},
  ["creature.loup-garou.rhw2014"]={title="Loup Garou",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 252\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S/M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 187 (22d8 + 88)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 18 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common (can't speak in dire wolf form)\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the loup garou fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe loup garou makes two attacks, using Longsword or Rend in any combination. It can replace one attack with a Bite attack.\n\nBite (Dire Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nm 12, reach 5 ft. h16 (2d8 + 7) Piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) Necrotic damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it is subjected to the following effect. con 18. actSaveFail The target is cursed. If the cursed target drops to 0 XPHB, it instead becomes a Werewolf under the DM's control and has 10 XPHB. The curse can't be removed until this loup garou dies. actSaveSuccess The target is immune to this loup garou's curse for 24 hours.\n\nLongsword (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nm 12, reach 5 ft. h18 (2d10 + 7) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage.\n\nRend (Dire Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nm 12, reach 5 ft. h16 (2d8 + 7) Slashing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe loup garou shape-shifts into a Large dire wolf-humanoid hybrid or a Large dire wolf, or it returns to its true humanoid form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nMauling Charge\n\nThe loup garou moves up to half its XPHB without provoking XPHB and makes one Longsword or Rend attack.\n\nSurprise Bite\n\nThe loup garou uses Shape-Shift, turning into its hybrid or dire wolf form, then makes one Bite attack. The loup garou can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.loup-garou.vrgr2014"]={title="Loup Garou",subtitle="Criatura - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 170 (20d8 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 18 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common (can't speak in wolf form)\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe loup garou has advantage on attack rolls against a creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nWhen the loup garou fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe loup garou regains 10 hit points at the start of each of its turns. If the loup garou takes damage from a silver weapon, this trait doesn't function at the start of the loup garou's next turn. The loup garou dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe loup garou makes two attacks: two with its Longsword (humanoid form) or one with its Bite and one with its Claws (dire wolf or hybrid form).\n\nBite (Dire Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) necrotic damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with loup garou MM.\n\nClaws (Dire Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 17 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nLongsword (Humanoid Form Only)\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage, or 15 (2d10 + 4) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe loup garou polymorphs into a Large wolf-humanoid hybrid or into a Large dire wolf, or back into its true form, which appears humanoid. Its statistics, other than its size and speed, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nSwipe\n\nThe loup garou makes one Claws attack (dire wolf or hybrid form only) or one Longsword attack (humanoid form only).\n\nMauling Pounce (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe loup garou moves up to its speed without provoking opportunity attacks, and it can make one Claws attack (dire wolf or hybrid form only) or one Longsword attack (humanoid form only) against each creature it moves past.\n\nBite (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe loup garou changes into hybrid or dire wolf form and then makes one Bite attack."},
  ["feat.love-bites.abh2014"]={title="Love Bites",subtitle="Feat - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nEndearing Pain\n\nImmediately after you damage a creature with a Melee weapon or an XPHB, you can take a XPHB to give the target the XPHB condition until the start of your next turn or until you or your allies damage it. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB."},
  ["deity.loviatar.frhof2014"]={title="Loviatar",subtitle="Divindade - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 114\n\nLoviatar is a god of agony, the mistress of physical and psychological suffering. Coldhearted and calculatingly cruel, Loviatar is an aggressive and domineering despot, and she deeply enjoys her divine remit. Pain isn't a means to an end for Loviatar, but an end unto itself. That quality endears her to the tyrant god Bane.\n\nLoviatar takes the form of a slender woman, like a whip in her movement and aspect. She speaks to her followers during extended sessions of enduring or inflicting pain, intruding on their perceptions in the delirium of agony or ecstasy. When she dispatches an emissary, she usually sends a XMM, an XMM, or a XMM.\n\nTo the followers of Loviatar, nothing is as transcendent as suffering. All pain is holy, from the crudest brutality to the emotional suffering of the heartbroken or the betrayed, and is proof of Loviatar's attention. Pain—the ability both to inflict it and to endure it—is a path to power. Loviatar's followers consider a cold, cruel demeanor ideal because that best emulates Loviatar herself, and for the same reason her faithful appreciate beauty, cultural refinement, and skill at manipulation.\n\nThough temples to Loviatar are rare, her faithful are numerous. Loviatar is a preferred deity of those who inflict pain as a matter of course, including torturers and others who need to break the will of their victims. Her followers form cells of secret adherents led by someone who takes pleasure in administering pain and dominating others, supported and bolstered by submissive sycophants.\n\nWorshipers of Loviatar rarely gather in numbers except in populous cities, and never openly. When small cadres of the faithful operate quietly, few citizens take notice or raise a fuss when they witness cult activity. Loviatar's cults sometimes kidnap and keep prisoners, which can draw the attention of the authorities.\n\nThe Chosen of Loviatar are paragons of inflicting and receiving pain. They delight in insinuating themselves into the fabric of society and then tearing through it like a barbed whip."},
  ["deity.loviatar.phb2014"]={title="Loviatar",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 294"},
  ["deity.loviatar.scag2014"]={title="Loviatar",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nPain isn't a means to an end for Loviatar's faithful, but an end unto itself. To them, nothing is as transcendent as suffering, and all pain is holy, from the crudest barbarism, to the most sublime torture, to the emotional suffering of the heartbroken or the betrayed.\n\nThe pain that one feels is proof of the Lady's attention, and so her faithful are notorious self-flagellants. Pain is also a path to power, in terms of both one's ability to inflict it and one's ability to endure it. A cold, cruel demeanor is considered ideal because it best emulates the Scourge Mistress, and for the same reason her faithful appreciate beauty, cultural refinement, and a certain adeptness at manipulation.\n\nThough temples to Loviatar are rare, her faithful are more numerous than might be expected. Loviatar is the chosen deity of those who inflict pain as a matter of course, including torturers and others who need to break the will of their victims. She is favored by sadists and masochists, and some of her followers form cultish cells of secret adherents. Each of these groups is led by someone who takes pleasure in administering pain and dominating others, supported and backed up by a number of submissive sycophants.\n\nWorshipers of Loviatar rarely gather in numbers except in the more populous cities. When small cadres of faithful operate quietly in such places, few citizens take notice or raise a fuss if they do witness cult activity. The sufferers who endure the lash, however, aren't always willing participants, and Lovatar's cults sometimes operate secret slavery rings, which can draw the attention of the authorities. The open worship of Loviatar and temples clearly dedicated to her are rarely seen except in lands where slavery is an accepted practice."},
  ["creature.lowarnizel.pabtso2014"]={title="Lowarnizel",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 181\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 168 (16d10 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: force, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nLowarnizel can breathe both air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nLowarnizel makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nSingularity Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nLowarnizel creates a shining bead of gravitational force, then releases the energy in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 17 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 36 (8d8) force damage, and its speed becomes 0 until the start of the dragon's next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nLowarnizel magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining his game statistics (other than his size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it."},
  ["language.loxodon.ggr2014"]={title="Loxodon",subtitle="Idioma - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["species.loxodon.ggr2014"]={title="Loxodon",subtitle="Especie - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nAge\n\nLoxodons physically mature at the same rate as humans, but they live about 450 years. They highly value the weight of wisdom and experience and are considered young until they reach the age of 60.\n\nAlignment\n\nMost loxodons are lawful, believing in the value of a peaceful, ordered life. They also tend toward good.\n\nSize\n\nLoxodons stand between 7 and 8 feet tall. Their massive bodies weigh between 300 and 400 pounds. Your size is Medium.\n\nPowerful Build\n\nYou count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity and the weight you can push, drag, or lift.\n\nLoxodon Serenity\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened.\n\nNatural Armor\n\nYou have thick, leathery skin. When you aren't wearing armor, your AC is 12 + your Constitution modifier. You can use your natural armor to determine your AC if the armor you wear would leave you with a lower AC. A shield's benefits apply as normal while you use your natural armor.\n\nTip: AC Calculations Don't Stack\n\nWhen the game gives you more than one way to calculate your Armor Class, you can use only one of them. You choose the one to use. For example, if you have the loxodon's Natural Armor trait and the monk's Unarmored Defense feature, you don't mix them together. Instead, you choose which one determines your AC.\n\nTrunk\n\nYou can grasp things with your trunk, and you can use it as a snorkel. It has a reach of 5 feet, and it can lift a number of pounds equal to five times your Strength score. You can use it to do the following simple tasks: lift, drop, hold, push, or pull an object or a creature; open or close a door or a container; grapple someone; or make an unarmed strike. Your DM might allow other simple tasks to be added to that list of options.\n\nYour trunk can't wield weapons or shields or do anything that requires manual precision, such as using tools or magic items or performing the somatic components of a spell.\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThanks to your sensitive trunk, you have advantage on Wisdom (Perception), Wisdom (Survival), and Intelligence (Investigation) checks that involve smell.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Loxodon."},
  ["creature.lu-zhong-yin.jttrc2014"]={title="Lu Zhong Yin",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["magicitem.luba-s-tarokka-of-souls.tce2014"]={title="Luba's Tarokka of Souls",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 129\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nNot all lingering spirits are tragic souls, lost on their way to the hereafter. Some languish as prisoners, souls so wicked mortals dare not free them upon an unsuspecting afterlife.\n\nCreated by a figure of Vistani legend, Luba's Tarokka of Souls shaped the destiny of countless heroes. The prophecies of this deck of cards also revealed great evils and guided its creator into the path of nefarious forces. Untold times the deck's creator, Mother Luba, narrowly escaped doom, spared only by her keen insights. But even for her, not all wickedness could be escaped. In the most dire cases, Mother Luba managed to ensnare beings of pure evil amid the strands of fate, imprisoning them within her CoS. There these foul spirits dwell still, trapped within a nether-realm hidden amid shuffling cards, waiting for fate to turn foul—as it inevitably will.\n\nLike all CoS, the Tarokka of Souls is a lavishly illustrated collection of fifty-four cards, comprising the fourteen cards of the high deck and forty other cards divided into four suits: coins, glyphs, stars, and swords.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe artifact has the following random properties, which you can determine by rolling on the tables in the \"Artifacts\" section of the DMG:\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\nSpells\n\nWhile holding the deck, you can use an action to cast one of the following spells (save 18) from it: comprehend languages, detect evil and good, detect magic, detect poison and disease, locate object, or scrying. Once you use the deck to cast a spell, you can't cast that spell again from it until the next dawn.\n\nEnduring Vision\n\nWhile holding the deck, you automatically succeed on Constitution saving throws made to maintain your concentration on divination spells.\n\nTwist of Fate\n\nAs an action, you can draw a card from the deck and twist the fortune of another creature you can see within 15 feet of you. Choose one of the following effects:\n\n• Weal\n\n• Woe\n\nThe deck can be used in this way twice, and you regain all expended uses at the next dawn.\n\nPrisoners of Fate\n\nWhenever you use the Twist of Fate property, there is a chance that one of the souls trapped in the deck escapes. Roll d100 and consult the Souls of the Tarokka table. If you roll one of the high cards, the soul associated with it escapes. You can find its statistics in the MM. If you roll a soul that has already escaped, roll again.\n\nd100 | Card | Soul\n\n1 | Artifact | Flameskull\n\n2 | Beast | Wraith\n\n3 | Broken | Banshee\n\n4 | Darklord | Vampire\n\n5 | Donjon | Mummy\n\n6 | Executioner | Death knight\n\n7 | Ghost | Ghost\n\n8 | Horseman | Mummy lord\n\n9 | Innocent | Ghost\n\n10 | Marionette | Mummy\n\n11 | Mists | Wraith\n\n12 | Raven | Vampire spawn\n\n13 | Seer | Vampire\n\n14 | Tempter | Vampire spawn\n\n15-100 | — | —\n\nThe released soul appears at a random location within 10d10 miles of you and terrorizes the living. Until the released soul is destroyed, it gains the benefit of a weal from the deck's Twist of Fate property, and both you and the original target of Twist of Fate suffer the effect of woe.\n\nShuffling Fate\n\nIf you go 7 days without using the Twist of Fate property, your attunement to Luba's Tarokka of Souls ends, and you can't attune to it again until after another creature uses Twist of Fate on you.\n\nDestroying the Deck\n\nLuba's Tarokka of Souls can be destroyed only if all fourteen souls within are released and destroyed. This reveals a fifteenth soul, a lich, that inhabits the Nether card, which appears only when the fourteen souls are defeated. If this ancient entity is destroyed, the Nether card vanishes and the deck becomes a normal CoS, with no special properties, but it includes a new card of the DM's design.\n\nMother Luba and the Vistani\n\nThe creator of the Tarokka of Souls, Mother Luba was one of the most influential leaders of the Vistani. For untold generations, the Vistani have wandered the Shadowfell, which includes terrifying demiplanes like the vampire-haunted realm of Barovia. These travelers have learned many secrets of these domains and encountered countless others wandering amid the Shadowfell's horrors. Most Vistani bands accept well-intentioned wayfarers from diverse walks and of disparate origins, embracing any who seek to find a home amid the endless roads and vistas hidden amid the mists.\n\nA halfling Vistani, Mother Luba led one of the largest groups of Vistani in the Shadowfell. She hailed from the same world that Count Strahd von Zarovich and Madam Eva came from, and she created a community of kindness and resilience-ever rare to find in the Plane of Shadow. She led her people in welcoming strangers, feeding the hungry, and defying the cruel. She and Madam Eva were once friends, until Madam Eva began bargaining with the creatures of the night. \"We may wander amid the shadows,\" Mother Luba said. \"But we must ever serve as a light to our fellow travelers.\"\n\nSome years ago, Mother Luba disappeared into the mists, leaving behind only the Tarokka of Souls. It is said that if you draw the Mists card from it, you can hear the whispers of her kind voice."},
  ["magicitem.lucent-destroyer.bgg2014"]={title="Lucent Destroyer",subtitle="Item Magico - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 113\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis magic weapon is a triple-barreled bronze musket. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. It requires no ammunition, its damage is radiant instead of piercing, and it doesn't have the loading property. The base of the weapon is emblazoned with the light rune.\n\nAdditionally, while attuned to the weapon, you can cast dancing lights from the musket at will.\n\nInvoking the Rune\n\nAs an action, you can invoke the weapon's rune to cast the sunbeam spell (save 17) with it. Once the rune has been invoked, it can't be invoked again until the next dawn."},
  ["feat.lucky.phb2014"]={title="Lucky",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\nYou have inexplicable luck that seems to kick in at just the right moment.\n\nYou have 3 luck points. Whenever you make an attack roll, an ability check, or a saving throw, you can spend one luck point to roll an additional d20. You can choose to spend one of your luck points after you roll the die, but before the outcome is determined. You choose which of the d20s is used for the attack roll, ability check, or saving throw.\n\nYou can also spend one luck point when an attack roll is made against you. Roll a d20, and then choose whether the attack uses the attacker's roll or yours. If more than one creature spends a luck point to influence the outcome of a roll, the points cancel each other out; no additional dice are rolled.\n\nYou regain your expended luck points when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feat.lucky.xphb2024"]={title="Lucky",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 201\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nLuck Points\n\nYou have a number of Luck Points equal to your XPHB and can spend the points on the benefits below. You regain your expended Luck Points when you finish a XPHB.\n\nAdvantage\n\nWhen you roll a d20 for a XPHB, you can spend 1 Luck Point to give yourself XPHB on the roll.\n\nDisadvantage\n\nWhen a creature rolls a d20 for an attack roll against you, you can spend 1 Luck Point to impose XPHB on that roll."},
  ["magicitem.lucky-foot.au2014"]={title="Lucky Foot",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhen you roll a 1 on a saving throw or ability check, you can use this preserved rabbit foot's magic to reroll the die. You must use the new roll, and the foot disintegrates."},
  ["creature.ludmilla-vilisevic.cos2014"]={title="Ludmilla Vilisevic",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 93\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["deity.lugh.phb2014"]={title="Lugh",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["creature.lulu.bgdia2014"]={title="Lulu",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 5\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.lumalia.tftyp2014"]={title="Lumalia",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["magicitem.luminous-war-pick.pabtso2014"]={title="Luminous War Pick",subtitle="Item Magico - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThe haft of this war pick is inlaid with crushed pearlescent stones that imbue the weapon with a faint luminescence. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this war pick.\n\nWhile wielding the war pick, you can use a bonus action to cast the daylight spell, choosing a point on the war pick. Once you use this bonus action, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["feature.lunar-boons.dsotdq2014.sorcerer.lunar.6"]={title="Lunar Boons",subtitle="Caracteristica - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n6th-Level Lunar Sorcery Feature\n\nThe current phase of your Lunar Embodiment can affect your Metamagic feature. Each Lunar Embodiment phase is associated with certain schools of magic, as shown here:\n\n• Full Moon spells\n\n• New Moon spells\n\n• Crescent Moon spells\n\nWhenever you use Metamagic on a spell of a school of magic associated with your current Lunar Embodiment phase, you can reduce the sorcery points spent by 1 (minimum 0). You can reduce the sorcery points spent for your Metamagic a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["creature.lunar-dragon-wyrmling.bam2014"]={title="Lunar Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 37 (5d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 10, fly: 40\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 5-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) cold damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a blast of frost in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the cone must make a 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 13 (3d8) cold damage, and its speed is halved until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and its speed isn't reduced.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nPhase (2/Day)\n\nThe dragon becomes partially incorporeal for as long as it maintains concentration on the effect (as if concentration on a spell). While partially incorporeal, the dragon has resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage."},
  ["feature.lunar-embodiment.dsotdq2014.sorcerer.lunar.1"]={title="Lunar Embodiment",subtitle="Caracteristica - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n1st-Level Lunar Sorcery Feature\n\nYou learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the Lunar Spells table. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.\n\nSorcerer Level | Full Moon Spell | New Moon Spell | Crescent Moon Spell\n\n1st | shield | ray of sickness | color spray\n\n3rd | lesser restoration | blindness/deafness | alter self\n\n5th | dispel magic | vampiric touch | phantom steed\n\n7th | death ward | confusion | hallucinatory terrain\n\n9th | Rary's telepathic bond | hold monster | mislead\n\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can choose what lunar phase manifests its power through your magic: Full Moon, New Moon, or Crescent Moon. While in the chosen phase, you can cast one 1st-level spell of the associated phase in the Lunar Spells table once without expending a spell slot. Once you cast a spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.lunar-empowerment.dsotdq2014.sorcerer.lunar.14"]={title="Lunar Empowerment",subtitle="Caracteristica - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n14th-Level Lunar Sorcery Feature\n\nThe power of a lunar phase saturates your being. While you are in a Lunar Embodiment phase, you also gain the following benefit associated with that phase:\n\n• Full Moon You can use a bonus action to shed bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet or to douse the light. In addition, you and creatures of your choice have advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) and Wisdom (Perception) checks while within the bright light you shed.\n\n• New Moon You have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. In addition, while you are entirely in darkness, attack rolls have disadvantage against you.\n\n• Crescent Moon You have resistance to necrotic and radiant damage."},
  ["feature.lunar-form.xphb2024.druid.moon.14"]={title="Lunar Form",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.lunar-phenomenon.dsotdq2014.sorcerer.lunar.18"]={title="Lunar Phenomenon",subtitle="Caracteristica - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n18th-Level Lunar Sorcery feature\n\nAs a bonus action, you can tap into a special power of your current Lunar Embodiment phase. Alternatively, as part of the bonus action you take to change your lunar phase using the Waxing and Waning feature, you can immediately use the power of the lunar phase you are entering:\n\n• Full Moon You radiate moonlight for a moment. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or be blinded until the end of its next turn. In addition, one creature of your choice in that area regains 3d8 hit points.\n\n• New Moon You momentarily emanate gloom. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC or take 3d10 necrotic damage and have its speed reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. In addition, you become invisible until the end of your next turn, or until immediately after you make an attack roll or cast a spell.\n\n• Crescent Moon You can magically teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 60 feet of yourself. You can bring along one willing creature you can see within 5 feet of yourself. That creature teleports to an unoccupied space of your choice that you can see within 5 feet of your destination space. In addition, you and that creature gain resistance to all damage until the start of your next turn.\n\nOnce you use one of these bonus action benefits, you can't use that benefit again until you finish a long rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again."},
  ["subclass.lunar-sorcery.dsotdq2014.sorcerer.lunar.0"]={title="Lunar Sorcery",subtitle="Subclasse - DSotDQ - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Lunar Embodiment\n\nPagina: 34\n\n1st-Level Lunar Sorcery Feature\n\nYou learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the Lunar Spells table. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.\n\nSorcerer Level | Full Moon Spell | New Moon Spell | Crescent Moon Spell\n\n1st | shield | ray of sickness | color spray\n\n3rd | lesser restoration | blindness/deafness | alter self\n\n5th | dispel magic | vampiric touch | phantom steed\n\n7th | death ward | confusion | hallucinatory terrain\n\n9th | Rary's telepathic bond | hold monster | mislead\n\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can choose what lunar phase manifests its power through your magic: Full Moon, New Moon, or Crescent Moon. While in the chosen phase, you can cast one 1st-level spell of the associated phase in the Lunar Spells table once without expending a spell slot. Once you cast a spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 1 - Lunar Sorcery\n\nPagina: 34\n\nOn many worlds, the moon is a revered celestial body with magical properties. On Krynn, the gods of magic are associated with the world's three moons. On the world of Toril, the god Selûne uses the light of the moon to battle darkness. On Eberron, scholars of the Draconic Prophecy decipher ancient secrets from the waxing and waning of that world's twelve moons.\n\nYou or someone from your lineage has been exposed to the concentrated magic of the moon (or moons) of your world, imbuing you with lunar magic. Perhaps your ancestor was involved in a druidic ritual involving an eclipse, or maybe a mystical fragment of a moon crashed near you. However you came to have your magic, your connection to the moon is obvious when you cast sorcerer spells—perhaps making your pupils glow with the color of a moon from your world, causing spectral manifestations of lunar phases to orbit you, or some other effect.\n\nNivel 1 - Moon Fire\n\nPagina: 34\n\n1st-Level Lunar Sorcery Feature\n\nYou can call down the radiant light of the moon on command. You learn the sacred flame spell, which doesn't count against the number of sorcerer cantrips you know. When you cast the spell, you can target one creature as normal or target two creatures within range that are within 5 feet of each other.\n\nNivel 3 - Lunar Sorcery\n\nNivel 6 - Lunar Boons\n\nPagina: 34\n\n6th-Level Lunar Sorcery Feature\n\nThe current phase of your Lunar Embodiment can affect your Metamagic feature. Each Lunar Embodiment phase is associated with certain schools of magic, as shown here:\n\n• Full Moon spells\n\n• New Moon spells\n\n• Crescent Moon spells\n\nWhenever you use Metamagic on a spell of a school of magic associated with your current Lunar Embodiment phase, you can reduce the sorcery points spent by 1 (minimum 0). You can reduce the sorcery points spent for your Metamagic a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 6 - Waxing and Waning\n\nPagina: 35\n\n6th-Level Lunar Sorcery Feature\n\nYou gain greater control over the phases of your lunar magic. As a bonus action, you can spend 1 sorcery point to change your current Lunar Embodiment phase to a different one.\n\nYou can now cast one 1st-level spell from each lunar phase of the Lunar Spells table once without expending a spell slot, provided your current phase is the same as the lunar phase spell. Once you cast a lunar phase spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 14 - Lunar Empowerment\n\nPagina: 35\n\n14th-Level Lunar Sorcery Feature\n\nThe power of a lunar phase saturates your being. While you are in a Lunar Embodiment phase, you also gain the following benefit associated with that phase:\n\n• Full Moon You can use a bonus action to shed bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet or to douse the light. In addition, you and creatures of your choice have advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) and Wisdom (Perception) checks while within the bright light you shed.\n\n• New Moon You have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. In addition, while you are entirely in darkness, attack rolls have disadvantage against you.\n\n• Crescent Moon You have resistance to necrotic and radiant damage.\n\nNivel 18 - Lunar Phenomenon\n\nPagina: 35\n\n18th-Level Lunar Sorcery feature\n\nAs a bonus action, you can tap into a special power of your current Lunar Embodiment phase. Alternatively, as part of the bonus action you take to change your lunar phase using the Waxing and Waning feature, you can immediately use the power of the lunar phase you are entering:\n\n• Full Moon You radiate moonlight for a moment. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or be blinded until the end of its next turn. In addition, one creature of your choice in that area regains 3d8 hit points.\n\n• New Moon You momentarily emanate gloom. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC or take 3d10 necrotic damage and have its speed reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. In addition, you become invisible until the end of your next turn, or until immediately after you make an attack roll or cast a spell.\n\n• Crescent Moon You can magically teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 60 feet of yourself. You can bring along one willing creature you can see within 5 feet of yourself. That creature teleports to an unoccupied space of your choice that you can see within 5 feet of your destination space. In addition, you and that creature gain resistance to all damage until the start of your next turn.\n\nOnce you use one of these bonus action benefits, you can't use that benefit again until you finish a long rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again."},
  ["feature.lunar-sorcery.dsotdq2014.sorcerer.lunar.1"]={title="Lunar Sorcery",subtitle="Caracteristica - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\nOn many worlds, the moon is a revered celestial body with magical properties. On Krynn, the gods of magic are associated with the world's three moons. On the world of Toril, the god Selûne uses the light of the moon to battle darkness. On Eberron, scholars of the Draconic Prophecy decipher ancient secrets from the waxing and waning of that world's twelve moons.\n\nYou or someone from your lineage has been exposed to the concentrated magic of the moon (or moons) of your world, imbuing you with lunar magic. Perhaps your ancestor was involved in a druidic ritual involving an eclipse, or maybe a mystical fragment of a moon crashed near you. However you came to have your magic, your connection to the moon is obvious when you cast sorcerer spells—perhaps making your pupils glow with the color of a moon from your world, causing spectral manifestations of lunar phases to orbit you, or some other effect."},
  ["feature.lunar-sorcery.dsotdq2014.sorcerer.lunar.3"]={title="Lunar Sorcery",subtitle="Caracteristica - DSotDQ - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.lunar-wand-of-celestial-prowess.au2014"]={title="Lunar Wand of Celestial Prowess",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 133\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias"},
  ["optionalfeature.lunging-attack.phb2014"]={title="Lunging Attack",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 74\n\nWhen you make a melee weapon attack on your turn, you can expend one superiority die to increase your reach for that attack by 5 feet. If you hit, you add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll."},
  ["optionalfeature.lunging-attack.xphb2024"]={title="Lunging Attack",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 95\n\nAs a XPHB, you can expend one Superiority Die and take the XPHB action. If you move at least 5 feet in a straight line immediately before hitting with a melee attack as part of the XPHB action on this turn, you can add the Superiority Die to the attack's damage roll."},
  ["creature.lungtian.jttrc2014"]={title="Lungtian",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 136\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["deity.lunitari.dsotdq2014"]={title="Lunitari",subtitle="Divindade - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nLunitari, the god of neutral magic and illusions, is patron of the Mages of High Sorcery's Order of the Red Robes and other neutral mages. With her cousins Solinari and Nuitari, she watches over the people of Krynn from the heavens, conveying her power through the red moon that shares her name. She appears as a trickster figure in mythology, using her mastery of illusions to fool gods and heroes alike."},
  ["deity.lunitari.phb2014"]={title="Lunitari",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["species.lupin.rhw2014"]={title="Lupin",subtitle="Especie - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 60 feet.\n\nFeral Pounce\n\nYour XPHB deal Slashing damage instead of Bludgeoning damage. In addition, when you hit a creature with an XPHB as part of the XPHB action on your turn, you can use both the XPHB and the Shove options. You can use this benefit only once per turn.\n\nHowl\n\nAs a XPHB, you let out an unearthly howl. Each creature of your choice within 15 feet of you must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 plus your Constitution modifier and XPHB) or have XPHB on attack rolls and saving throws until the start of your next turn.\n\nYou can use this trait a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nWerewolf Instincts\n\nYou have proficiency in the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB skill."},
  ["item.lute.phb2014"]={title="Lute",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.lute.xphb2024"]={title="Lute",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Charisma\n\n• Utilize: Play a known tune (10), or improvise a song (15)"},
  ["item.lute-crafted-of-exotic-wood-with-mother-of-pearl-inlay-and-zircon-gems-brazen-coalition.psx2014"]={title="Lute crafted of exotic wood with mother-of-pearl inlay and zircon gems (Brazen Coalition)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.lute-of-thunderous-thumping.xdmg2024"]={title="Lute of Thunderous Thumping",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 275\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis reinforced XPHB can be wielded as a magic Club that deals an extra 2d8 Thunder damage on a hit.\n\nSing and Swing\n\nIf you're a Bard, you can use your Charisma modifier instead of your Strength modifier when making a melee attack roll with the XPHB, provided you sing or hum while making the attack."},
  ["deity.luthic.scag2014"]={title="Luthic",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 24"},
  ["deity.luthic.vgm2014"]={title="Luthic",subtitle="Divindade - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 84\n\nWhile Gruumsh is the external force that pushes the orcs to victory over their enemies, it is the influence of Luthic, his wife, that binds them together and makes the orcs internally cohesive. She is the force that keeps the explosive rage of Gruumsh from bursting the orcs apart. If it was not for the followers of Luthic, it is possible that the race of orcs would be no more than small bands of warrior-nomads, scratching out a meager existence, rather than a force capable of great destruction.\n\nFar from the den's war hearth, within the protective depths of the caves, the followers of Luthic tend the orc brood, raising them to be strong and cruel like their progenitors. By invoking the power of superstitions, omens, and traditions, these claws of Luthic hold the tribe together through ritual, fear and, if necessary, force.\n\nTalons of the Bear\n\nLuthic is often thought to take the guise of an enormous cave bear. Her followers honor this aspect of her by keeping cave bears as pets to guard the whelping pens that are filled with squabbling young. Luthic's devoted also grow their claws long and paint them black to mimic the fearsome talons of their goddess. Luthic rewards them by making their claws as strong and tough as iron.\n\nHolding the Fort\n\nAlong with protecting the young and the tribe's food stores, the worshipers of Luthic also serve as the crafters, engineers, and builders of an orc tribe. They fashion crude weapons, armor, and the few manufactured items that the orcs need for daily life. When the tribe is away on raids, they are expected to dig deeper into the caverns of the den to create more living space for the ever-increasing population."},
  ["creature.luvash.cos2014"]={title="Luvash",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 121\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["magicitem.luxon-beacon.egw2014"]={title="Luxon Beacon",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis dodecahedron of faintly glowing crystal is heavier than it appears. A set of handles are affixed to its sides, and it pulsates and thrums when touched.\n\nFragment of Possibility\n\nA creature that touches the beacon and concentrates for 1 minute receives a Fragment of Possibility, which looks like a Tiny, grayish bead of energy that follows the creature around, staying within 1 foot of it at all times. The fragment lasts for 8 hours or until used. Once the beacon grants a Fragment of Possibility, it can't grant another until the next dawn. A creature with a Fragment of Possibility from a Luxon Beacon can't gain another Fragment of Possibility from any source.\n\nWhen a creature with a Fragment of Possibility makes an attack roll, an ability check, or a saving throw, it can expend its fragment to roll an additional d20 and choose which of the d20s to use. Alternatively, when an attack roll is made against the creature, it can expend its fragment to roll a d20 and choose which of the d20s to use, the one it rolled or the one the attacker rolled.\n\nIf the original d20 roll has advantage or disadvantage, the creature rolls its d20 after advantage or disadvantage has been applied to the original roll.\n\nSoul Snare\n\nIf a follower of the Luxon who has undergone a ritual of consecution dies within 100 miles of a Luxon Beacon, their soul is ensnared by it. This soul will be reincarnated within the body of a random humanoid baby developing within 100 miles of the beacon."},
  ["background.luxonborn-acolyte.egw2014"]={title="Luxonborn (Acolyte)",subtitle="Background - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 203"},
  ["creature.lycanthropickle.rmbre2014"]={title="Lycanthropickle",subtitle="Criatura - RMBRE - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the lycanthropickle remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a pickle."},
  ["creature.lynx-creatlach.imr2014"]={title="Lynx Creatlach",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 54\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 136 (16d8 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal\n\nResistencias: necrotic, psychic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nLynx's crystal eye is a magically shrunken crystal ball of true seeing. One of her teeth is a refashioned ring of mind shielding, while another has been magicked to place her under a permanent Nystul's magic aura spell, concealing the magic of these items and hiding her true nature from magic or features that can detect undead.\n\nAversion of Fire\n\nIf Lynx takes fire damage, she has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of her next turn.\n\nImmutable Form\n\nLynx is immune to any spell or effect that would alter her form.\n\nLightning Absorption\n\nWhenever Lynx is subjected to lightning damage, she takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the lightning damage dealt.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nLynx has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegeneration\n\nLynx regains 10 hit points at the start of her turn. If she takes fire or radiant damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of her next turn. Lynx's body is destroyed only if she starts her turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nTurn Immunity\n\nLynx is immune to effects that turn undead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nLynx makes two shortsword attacks.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.lyra.psd2014"]={title="Lyra",subtitle="Criatura - PSD - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["vehicle.lyrandar-air-cruiser.efa2014"]={title="Lyrandar Air Cruiser",subtitle="Veiculo - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 106"},
  ["creature.lyrandar-scion.efa2014"]={title="Lyrandar Scion",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 60 (11d8 + 11)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nJump (2/Day)\n\nFeather Fall (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes two Thunderbolt attacks and uses Spellcasting.\n\nThunderbolt\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Lightning damage plus 9 (2d8) Thunder damage. Critical hThe creature also has the XPHB condition for 1 minute."},
  ["vehicle.lyrandar-skyskiff.efa2014"]={title="Lyrandar Skyskiff",subtitle="Veiculo - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 107"},
  ["item.lyre.phb2014"]={title="Lyre",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.lyre.xphb2024"]={title="Lyre",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Charisma\n\n• Utilize: Play a known tune (10), or improvise a song (15)"},
  ["magicitem.lyre-of-building.tce2014"]={title="Lyre of Building",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 131\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile holding this PHB, you can cast mending as an action. You can also play the PHB as a reaction when an object or a structure you can see within 300 feet of you takes damage, causing it to be immune to that damage and any further damage of the same type until the start of your next turn.\n\nIn addition, you can play the PHB as an action to cast fabricate, move earth, passwall, or TCE, and that spell can't be cast from it again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.lysan.veor2014"]={title="Lysan",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.lyzandra-lyzzie-calderos.pota2014"]={title="Lyzandra \"Lyzzie\" Calderos",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting"},
  ["feature.macabre-modifications.rhw2014.artificer.reanimator.9"]={title="Macabre Modifications",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nYou experiment and alter your companion further. Whenever you create a RHW, the companion now gains two options for Strange Modifications, instead of one. Additionally, when picking options for Strange Modifications, you can also choose from the following options.\n\nBloated\n\nThe companion becomes Large. Whenever it hits a Large or smaller creature with its Dreadful Swipe action, that creature is pushed up to 10 feet away from the companion. Additionally, you can add your Intelligence modifier to the damage dealt by the companion's Death Burst.\n\nGaunt\n\nThe companion's XPHB increases to 45 feet, and it gains a XPHB equal to its XPHB. It can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check. In addition, whenever a creature of your choice starts its turn within a 10-foot XPHB originating from your companion, the creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or have the XPHB condition until the start of its next turn.\n\nMoist\n\nThe companion gains a XPHB equal to its XPHB, and it can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra movement to do so. In addition, whenever the companion is hit by an attack roll from a creature within 10 feet of itself, the attacker takes Acid damage equal to your Intelligence modifier."},
  ["creature.macaw.psx2014"]={title="Macaw",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.maccath-the-crimson.rot2014"]={title="Maccath the Crimson",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.mace.phb2014"]={title="Mace",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.mace.xphb2024"]={title="Mace",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.mace-of-disruption.dmg2014"]={title="Mace of Disruption",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 179\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhen you hit a fiend or an undead with this magic weapon, that creature takes an extra 2d6 radiant damage. If the target has 25 hit points or fewer after taking this damage, it must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or be destroyed. On a successful save, the creature becomes frightened of you until the end of your next turn.\n\nWhile you hold this weapon, it sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for an additional 20 feet."},
  ["magicitem.mace-of-disruption.xdmg2024"]={title="Mace of Disruption",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 276\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhen you hit a Fiend or an Undead with this magic weapon, that creature takes an extra 2d6 Radiant damage. If the target has 25 XPHB or fewer after taking this damage, it must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or be destroyed. On a successful save, the creature has the XPHB condition until the end of your next turn.\n\nLight\n\nWhile you hold this weapon, it sheds XPHB in a 20-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 20 feet."},
  ["magicitem.mace-of-smiting.dmg2014"]={title="Mace of Smiting",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 179\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. The bonus increases to +3 when you use the mace to attack a construct.\n\nWhen you roll a 20 on an attack roll made with this weapon, the target takes an extra 7 bludgeoning damage, or an extra 14 bludgeoning damage if it's a construct. If a construct has 25 hit points or fewer after taking this damage, it is destroyed.\n\n{@note Note: According to the SRD, it is an extra 2d6 and 4d6 bludgeoning damage, although https://rpg.stackexchange.com/a/174522/53884."},
  ["magicitem.mace-of-smiting.xdmg2024"]={title="Mace of Smiting",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 276\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. The bonus increases to +3 when you use the weapon to attack a Construct.\n\nWhen you roll a 20 on an attack roll made with this weapon, the target takes an extra 7 Bludgeoning damage, or 14 Bludgeoning damage if it's a Construct. If a Construct has 25 XPHB or fewer after taking this damage, it is destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.mace-of-terror.dmg2014"]={title="Mace of Terror",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis magic weapon has 3 charges. While holding it, you can use an action and expend 1 charge to release a wave of terror. Each creature of your choice in a 30-foot radius extending from you must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of you for 1 minute. While it is frightened in this way, a creature must spend its turns trying to move as far away from you as it can, and it can't willingly move to a space within 30 feet of you. It also can't take reactions. For its action it can use only the Dash action or try to escape from an effect that prevents it from moving. If it has nowhere it can move, the creature can use the Dodge action. At the end of each of its turns, a creature can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nThe mace regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."},
  ["magicitem.mace-of-terror.xdmg2024"]={title="Mace of Terror",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 276\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis magic weapon has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding the weapon, you can take a XPHB action and expend 1 charge to release a wave of terror from it. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition for 1 minute. While XPHB in this way, a creature must spend its turns trying to move as far away from you as it can, and it can't make XPHB. For its action, it can use only the XPHB action or try to escape from an effect that prevents it from moving. If it has nowhere it can move, the creature can take the XPHB action. At the end of each of its turns, a creature repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["item.mace-of-the-black-crown-awakened.egw2014"]={title="Mace of the Black Crown (Awakened)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.mace-of-the-black-crown-dormant.egw2014"]={title="Mace of the Black Crown (Dormant)",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThis mace has a haft of black iron and a ruby head with a fiendish countenance. Carrying the boon of Asmodeus, it is fit for the most powerful servants of the Nine Hells.\n\nSentience\n\nThe Mace of the Black Crown is a sentient lawful evil weapon with an Intelligence of 20, a Wisdom of 12, and a Charisma of 18. It has hearing and darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.\n\nThe weapon communicates telepathically with its wielder and can speak, read, and understand Common and Infernal.\n\nPersonality\n\nA greedy erinyes named Xartaza lives within the Mace of the Black Crown. Xartaza wants to recruit more souls for Asmodeus, so the weapon pushes its wielder toward lawful evil actions by manipulating the wielder's dreams. A former Blood War general, Xartaza hates demons and relishes crafting sound battle plans in any conflict.\n\nDormant\n\nThe mace grants the following benefits in its dormant state:\n\n• You can speak, read, and write Infernal.\n\n• You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.\n\n• While holding the mace, you can use a bonus action to speak its Infernal command word, causing flames to erupt from the head. These flames shed bright light in a 40-foot radius and dim light for an additional 40 feet. While the mace is ablaze, it deals an extra 1d6 fire damage to any target it hits. The flames last until you use a bonus action to speak the command word again or until you are no longer holding the mace.\n\n• While holding the mace, you can use an action to summon an imp. Any devil you summon with this mace is friendly to you and your companions for the duration. The imp obeys any verbal commands that you issue to it and returns to the Nine Hells 10 minutes after you summoned it. This property can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nBetrayer Artifact Properties\n\nThe Arms of the Betrayers advance in power in the same manner as the Vestiges of Divergence. In its dormant state, each of these artifacts has one dmg property and one dmg property. When the artifact attains an awakened state, it gains an additional dmg property and an additional dmg property. When the item reaches its exalted state, it gains a dmg property. See \"Artifact Properties\" in chapter 7 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for more information."},
  ["item.mace-of-the-black-crown-exalted.egw2014"]={title="Mace of the Black Crown (Exalted)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.macuahuitl.tftyp2014"]={title="Macuahuitl",subtitle="Item Magico - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 70\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nYou have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this longsword, which is made of laminated wood, and inset with jagged teeth of obsidian. It deals an extra 2d6 damage to any creature of the plant type."},
  ["creature.mad-golem.wdmm2014"]={title="Mad Golem",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 254\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: H\n\nCR: 12\n\nPV: 264 (23d12 + 115)\n\nINT 9 | CHA 9\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal, Celestial, Common, Draconic, Dwarvish, Elvish, Infernal, and Undercommon but can't speak"},
  ["creature.mad-maggie.bgdia2014"]={title="Mad Maggie",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 74\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.mad-mary.cos2014"]={title="Mad Mary",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.madam-eva.cos2014"]={title="Madam Eva",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 233\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 88 (16d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 17 | WIS 20 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Elvish, Infernal\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) piercing damage.\n\nCurse (Recharges after a Long Rest)\n\nMadam Eva targets one creature that she can see within 30 feet of her. The target must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or be cursed. While cursed, the target is blinded and deafened. The curse lasts until ended with a greater restoration spell, a remove curse spell, or similar magic. When the curse ends, Madam Eva takes 5d6 psychic damage.\n\nEvil Eye (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nMadam Eva targets one creature that she can see within 10 feet of her and casts one of the following spells on the target (save 17), requiring neither somatic nor material components to do so: animal friendship, charm person, or hold person. If the target succeeds on the initial saving throw, Madam Eva is blinded until the end of her next turn. Once a target succeeds on a saving throw against this effect, it is immune to the Evil Eye power of all Vistani for 24 hours."},
  ["creature.madam-eva.rhw2014"]={title="Madam Eva",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 253\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 117 (18d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 17 | WIS 20 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Elvish, Infernal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nMadam Eva has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nEvil Eye (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMadam Eva makes three attacks, using Cursed Dagger or Radiant Flame in any combination.\n\nCursed Dagger\n\nm 9, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d4 + 5) Piercing damage plus 21 (6d6) Necrotic damage.\n\nRadiant Flame\n\nr 9, range 60 ft. h21 (3d10 + 5) Radiant damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of Madam Eva's next turn.\n\nApocalyptic Visions {@recharge 5}\n\nwis 17, each creature in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point Madam Eva can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 24 (7d6) Necrotic damage plus 24 (7d6) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of Madam Eva's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["creature.madam-kulp.jttrc2014"]={title="Madam Kulp",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["spell.maddening-darkness.xge2024"]={title="Maddening Darkness",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 160\n\nMagical darkness spreads from a point you choose within range to fill a 60-foot-radius sphere until the spell ends. The darkness spreads around corners. A creature with darkvision can't see through this darkness. Non-magical light, as well as light created by spells of 8th level or lower, can't illuminate the area.\n\nShrieks, gibbering, and mad laughter can be heard within the sphere. Whenever a creature starts its turn in the sphere, it must make a Wisdom saving throw, taking 8d8 psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["optionalfeature.maddening-hex.xge2024"]={title="Maddening Hex",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 57\n\nAs a bonus action, you cause a psychic disturbance around the target cursed by your hex spell or by a warlock feature of yours, such as Hexblade's Curse or Sign of Ill Omen. When you do so, you deal psychic damage to the cursed target and each creature of your choice that you can see within 5 feet of it. The psychic damage equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1 damage). To use this invocation, you must be able to see the cursed target, and it must be within 30 feet of you."},
  ["magicitem.maddgoth-s-helm.wdmm2014"]={title="Maddgoth's Helm",subtitle="Item Magico - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 103\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile you wear this helm and are inside Maddgoth's castle, on its roof, or in its courtyard, you have immunity to all damage. If the helm is taken from the castle, it turns to dust and is destroyed."},
  ["creature.maddgoth-s-homunculus.wdmm2014"]={title="Maddgoth's Homunculus",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 96\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: L\n\nCR: 2\n\nPV: 55 (10d10)\n\nSTR 15\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic, Gnomish but can't speak"},
  ["creature.maegera-the-dawn-titan.skt2014"]={title="Maegera the Dawn Titan",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 241\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 341 (22d20 + 110)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 22 | CON 20 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Ignan\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEmpowered Attacks\n\nMaegera's slam attacks are treated as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance and immunity to damage from nonmagical attacks.\n\nFire Aura\n\nAt the start of each of Maegera's turns, each creature within 30 feet of it takes 35 (10d6) fire damage, and flammable objects in the aura that aren't being worn or carried ignite. A creature also takes 35 (10d6) fire damage from touching Maegera or from hitting it with a melee attack while within 10 feet of it, and a creature takes that damage the first time on a turn that Maegera moves into its space. Nonmagical weapons that hit Maegera are destroyed by fire immediately after dealing damage to it.\n\nFire Form\n\nMaegera can enter a hostile creature's space and stop there. It can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing if fire could pass through that space.\n\nIllumination\n\nMaegera sheds bright light in a 120-foot radius and dim light in an additional 120 ft..\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nMaegera has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMaegera makes three slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 35 (10d6) fire damage,\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nQuench Magic\n\nMaegera targets one creature that it can see within 60 feet of it. Any resistance or immunity to fire damage that the target gains from a spell or magic item is suppressed. The effect lasts until the end of Maegera's next turn.\n\nSmoke Cloud (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nMaegera exhales a billowing cloud of hot smoke and embers that fills a 60 feet cube. Each creature in the area takes 11 (2d10) fire damage. The cloud lasts until the end of Maegera's next turn. Creatures completely in the cloud are blinded and can't be seen.\n\nCreate Fire Elemental (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nMaegera's hit points are reduced by 50 as part of it separates and becomes a fire elemental with 102 hit points. The fire element appears in an unoccupied space within 15 feet of Maegera and acts on Maegera's initiative count. Maegera can't use this action if it has 50 hit points or fewer. The fire element obeys Maegera's commands and fights until destroyed."},
  ["creature.maegla-tarnlar.pota2014"]={title="Maegla Tarnlar",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.maelephant.mpp2014"]={title="Maelephant",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 161 (17d10 + 68)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 10 | WIS 16 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Infernal\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe maelephant has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe maelephant makes one Barbed Trunk attack and two Glaive attacks.\n\nBarbed Trunk\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage plus 13 (2d12) poison damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the grappled condition (escape 14). Until this grapple ends, the target has the restrained condition. While it is grappling a creature, the maelephant can't use its barbed trunk to attack other creatures.\n\nGlaive\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nMind Poison {@recharge 5}\n\nThe maelephant expels poisonous gas from its trunk in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 16 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 39 (6d12) poison damage and has the poisoned condition. While poisoned in this way, the creature loses all weapon and skill proficiencies, it can't cast spells, it can't understand language, and it has disadvantage on Intelligence saving throws. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only and is immune to this maelephant's Mind Poison for 24 hours."},
  ["creature.maelephant-nomad.coa2014"]={title="Maelephant Nomad",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 190 (20d10 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 14 | WIS 17 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal, Maelephant\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe maelephant has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegenerative\n\nAt the start of its turn, if the maelephant has less than half its hit points, it regenerates 20 hit points. This trait doesn't function if the maelephant starts its turn with less than 1 hit point.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe maelephant makes two attacks using its Claw, Trunk, or a combination of the two.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTrunk\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (3d6 + 6) piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the grappled condition (escape 18). Until this grapple ends, the target has the restrained condition. While it is grappling a creature, the maelephant can't use its Trunk attack against other creatures.\n\nNoxious Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe maelephant releases a cloud of noxious gas. All creatures in a 30-foot cone in front of the maelephant must make a 16 Constitution saving throw. Targets take 42 (12d6) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. In addition, on a failed save, the creature's Intelligence and Charisma scores become 1. The creature can't cast spells, activate magic items, understand language, or communicate in any intelligible way. The creature can, however, identify its friends, follow them, and even protect them. A feebled creature can repeat the save every minute, ending the effect on a success.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nReckless Charge\n\nThe maelephant moves up to 40 feet towards a creature it can see and if it moves at least 20 feet in a straight line, it may make a Claw attack. On a hit, the target takes an additional 14 (4d6) force damage and has the prone condition.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDefensive Stance\n\nAs a reaction to taking damage, the maelephant enters a defensive stance until the end of its next turn. While in a defensive stance, the maelephant moves at half speed and can't take bonus actions, but its AC increases by 5."},
  ["spell.maelstrom.xge2024"]={title="Maelstrom",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 160\n\nA swirling mass of 5-foot-deep water appears in a 30-foot radius centered on a point you can see within range. The point must be on the ground or in a body of water. Until the spell ends, that area is difficult terrain, and any creature that starts its turn there must succeed on a Strength saving throw or take 6d6 bludgeoning damage and be pulled 10 feet toward the center."},
  ["creature.mage.mm2014"]={title="Mage",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 347\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any four languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.mage.xmm2024"]={title="Mage",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 199\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 81 (18d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus three other languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nMisty Step (3/Day)\n\nProtective Magic (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe mage makes three Arcane Burst attacks.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h16 (3d8 + 3) Force damage."},
  ["creature.mage-apprentice.xmm2024"]={title="Mage Apprentice",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 198\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 49 (9d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nArcane Burst\n\nm,r 5, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h14 (2d10 + 3) Force damage."},
  ["spell.mage-armor.phb2014"]={title="Mage Armor",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 256\n\nYou touch a willing creature who isn't wearing armor, and a protective magical force surrounds it until the spell ends. The target's base AC becomes 13 + its Dexterity modifier. The spell ends if the target dons armor or if you dismiss the spell as an action."},
  ["spell.mage-armor.xphb2024"]={title="Mage Armor",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 293\n\nYou touch a willing creature who isn't wearing armor. Until the spell ends, the target's base AC becomes 13 plus its Dexterity modifier. The spell ends early if the target dons armor."},
  ["magicitem.mage-breaker.au2014"]={title="Mage Breaker",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 120\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.\n\nWhen you hit a XPHB creature with an attack roll using this weapon and deal damage, the creature has XPHB on the saving throw it makes to maintain XPHB."},
  ["spell.mage-hand.phb2014"]={title="Mage Hand",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 256\n\nA spectral, floating hand appears at a point you choose within range. The hand lasts for the duration or until you dismiss it as an action. The hand vanishes if it is ever more than 30 feet away from you or if you cast this spell again.\n\nYou can use your action to control the hand. You can use the hand to manipulate an object, open an unlocked door or container, stow or retrieve an item from an open container, or pour the contents out of a vial. You can move the hand up to 30 feet each time you use it.\n\nThe hand can't attack, activate magic items, or carry more than 10 pounds."},
  ["spell.mage-hand.xphb2024"]={title="Mage Hand",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 293\n\nA spectral, floating hand appears at a point you choose within range. The hand lasts for the duration. The hand vanishes if it is ever more than 30 feet away from you or if you cast this spell again.\n\nWhen you cast the spell, you can use the hand to manipulate an object, open an unlocked door or container, stow or retrieve an item from an open container, or pour the contents out of a vial.\n\nAs a XPHB action on your later turns, you can control the hand thus again. As part of that action, you can move the hand up to 30 feet.\n\nThe hand can't attack, activate magic items, or carry more than 10 pounds."},
  ["feature.mage-hand-legerdemain.phb2014.rogue.arcane-trickster.3"]={title="Mage Hand Legerdemain",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\nStarting at 3rd level, when you cast mage hand, you can make the spectral hand invisible, and you can perform the following additional tasks with it:\n\n• You can stow one object the hand is holding in a container worn or carried by another creature.\n\n• You can retrieve an object in a container worn or carried by another creature.\n\n• You can use phb to pick locks and disarm traps at range.\n\nYou can perform one of these tasks without being noticed by a creature if you succeed on a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check contested by the creature's Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nIn addition, you can use the bonus action granted by your Cunning Action to control the hand."},
  ["feature.mage-hand-legerdemain.xphb2024.rogue.arcane-trickster.3"]={title="Mage Hand Legerdemain",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.mage-hunter.scc2014"]={title="Mage Hunter",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 199\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 85 (10d10 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 10\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 17 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Sense\n\nThe hunter knows the location of every spellcaster, active spell, and magic item within 120 feet of itself.\n\nSpider Climb (Hunter Form Only)\n\nThe hunter can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Hunter Form Only)\n\nThe hunter makes two Claw attacks.\n\nClaw (Hunter Form Only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (4d8 + 4) piercing damage, and the target is grappled (escape 15). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the hunter can't make a Tail attack against another target.\n\nMage Tracker (Sentry Form Only)\n\nThe hunter emits a pulse of energy that helps it better locate its magical quarry. Each creature within 120 feet of the hunter that has the ability to cast spells must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or be mystically marked by the hunter for 1 hour.\n\nWhile marked, a creature can't become hidden from the hunter and gains no benefit from the invisible condition against the hunter. Additionally, while a marked creature is on the same plane of existence as the hunter, the hunter always knows the distance and direction to the creature.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShift Form\n\nThe hunter folds into its drone-like sentry form or unfolds into its hunter form. Its game statistics are the same in each form.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nConsume and Destroy\n\nWhen the hunter takes damage from a spell, it takes only half the triggering damage (rounded down). If the creature that cast the spell is within 60 feet of the hunter, that creature must succeed on a 14 Dexterity saving throw or take the other half of the damage."},
  ["background.mage-of-high-sorcery.dsotdq2014"]={title="Mage of High Sorcery",subtitle="Background - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Initiate of High Sorcery\n\nYou gain the DSotDQ feat.\n\nIn addition, the Mages of High Sorcery provide you with free, modest lodging and food indefinitely at any occupied Tower of High Sorcery and for one night at the home of an organization member.\n\nBuilding a Mage of High Sorcery Character\n\nMages of High Sorcery are typically sorcerers, warlocks, or wizards and might have any subclass. Spellcasters who gain their magic through devotion are less likely to be welcomed among the traditionalist mages. Nevertheless, the Mages of High Sorcery are shrewd, and they rarely let unique opportunities or individuals pass them by. Even members of martial classes who train in magic might find a rare place among the group's three orders.\n\nMage of High Sorcery Trinkets\n\nWhen you make your character, roll once on the Mage of High Sorcery Trinkets table instead of on the phb in the Player's Handbook for your starting trinket.\n\nd6 | Trinket\n\n1 | An unopened letter from your first teacher\n\n2 | A broken wand made of black, red, or white wood\n\n3 | A scroll bearing an incomprehensible formula\n\n4 | A purposeless device covered in colored stones that can fold into various enigmatic shapes\n\n5 | A pouch or spellbook emblazoned with the triple moon symbol of the Mages of High Sorcery\n\n6 | A lens through which you can see Krynn's invisible black moon, Nuitari"},
  ["creature.mage-of-usamigaras.qftis2014"]={title="Mage of Usamigaras",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 10 | INT 15 | WIS 10 | CHA 13\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) force damage."},
  ["feat.mage-slayer.phb2014"]={title="Mage Slayer",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\nYou have practiced techniques useful in melee combat against spellcasters, gaining the following benefits:\n\n• When a creature within 5 feet of you casts a spell, you can use your reaction to make a melee weapon attack against that creature.\n\n• When you damage a creature that is concentration on a spell, that creature has disadvantage on the saving throw it makes to maintain its concentration.\n\n• You have advantage on saving throws against spells cast by creatures within 5 feet of you."},
  ["feat.mage-slayer.xphb2024"]={title="Mage Slayer",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 205\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nConcentration Breaker\n\nWhen you damage a creature that is XPHB, it has XPHB on the saving throw it makes to maintain XPHB.\n\nGuarded Mind\n\nIf you fail an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma saving throw, you can cause yourself to succeed instead. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.mage-s-manacle.au2014"]={title="Mage's Manacle",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 120\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nAs a XPHB action while wearing this bracelet, you can target a Large or smaller creature within 5 feet of yourself that has the XPHB or XPHB condition. The target must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or become magically bound to you by a spectral chain and manacle that spring from the bracelet.\n\nWhile bound in this way, the creature has the XPHB condition. When you move, the creature moves with you.\n\nA creature remains bound for 8 hours or until you release it (no action required). If the manacle takes damage from a XPHB spell, it is destroyed; nothing else can break or harm it. Once the manacle has bound a creature, it can't be used again this way until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.magen-handbell.nf2014"]={title="Magen Handbell",subtitle="Item Magico - NF - 2014",body="Raridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile holding this brass handbell, you can take a XPHB action to ring it and summon a NF (see appendix B). The magen appears in an unoccupied space you choose within 30 feet of yourself, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. The magen disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a XPHB. The bell can't be used this way again for 1d6 days.\n\nBerserk Magen\n\nWhenever the magen summoned by this item starts its turn Bloodied, roll 1d6. On a 6, the magen goes berserk.\n\nWhile berserk, the magen no longer obeys your commands, and you can't dismiss it as a XPHB. On each of its turns, the berserk magen attacks the nearest creature it can see. If no creature is near enough for the magen to move to and attack, the magen attacks an object. The magen remains berserk until it disappears, or until a creature holding the handbell takes an XPHB action and succeeds on a DC 15 Charisma (XPHB) check to regain control of the magen."},
  ["creature.magewright.erlw2014"]={title="Magewright",subtitle="Criatura - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 318\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 13 | CON 10 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any two languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["magicitem.magewright-s-gloves.au2014"]={title="Magewright's Gloves",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 120\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile you wear these gloves, you work as efficiently as two characters when determining how much time it takes to craft nonmagical items using any of the following tools: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB."},
  ["creature.maggie-keeneyes-tier-1.crcotn2014"]={title="Maggie Keeneyes (Tier 1)",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 85 (10d10 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTactical Readiness\n\nMaggie and allies within 30 feet of her have advantage on initiative rolls, as long as Maggie isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGiant Maul\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a creature, Maggie can force it to make a 14 Strength saving throw; on a failed save, the target is pushed 5 feet away from Maggie and knocked prone.\n\nHammer Toss\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h9 (2d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a creature, Maggie can force it to make a 14 Strength saving throw; on a failed save, the target is pushed 5 feet away from Maggie and knocked prone."},
  ["creature.maggie-keeneyes-tier-2.crcotn2014"]={title="Maggie Keeneyes (Tier 2)",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 191\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 114 (12d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPush\n\nOnce during each of her turns, after hitting a creature with an attack, Maggie can force the target to make a 15 Strength saving throw; on a failed save, the target is pushed up to 10 feet horizontally away from Maggie and knocked prone.\n\nTactical Readiness\n\nMaggie and allies within 30 feet of her have advantage on initiative rolls, as long as Maggie isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMaggie makes two Giant Maul or Hammer Toss attacks.\n\nGiant Maul\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nHammer Toss\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h9 (2d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRally (1/Day)\n\nMaggie targets one creature she can see within 30 feet of herself and bolsters it with words of encouragement. The target gains 15 temporary hit points if it can see or hear Maggie."},
  ["creature.maggie-keeneyes-tier-3.crcotn2014"]={title="Maggie Keeneyes (Tier 3)",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 194\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 142 (15d10 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPush\n\nOnce during each of her turns, after hitting a creature with an attack, Maggie can force the target to make a 16 Strength saving throw; on a failed save, the target is pushed up to 15 feet horizontally away from Maggie and knocked prone.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nMaggie wears a suit of ruidium armor (plate; see appendix B). If Maggie rolls a 1 on a saving throw while wearing the armor, she must succeed on a 20 Charisma saving throw or gain 1 level of exhaustion.\n\nTactical Readiness\n\nMaggie and allies within 30 feet of her have advantage on initiative rolls, as long as Maggie isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMaggie makes two Heavy Greataxe or Hammer Toss attacks.\n\nHeavy Greataxe\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d12 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nHammer Toss\n\nrw 8 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h15 (4d4 + 5) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRally (1/Day)\n\nMaggie targets one creature she can see within 60 feet of herself and bolsters it with words of encouragement. The target gains 30 temporary hit points if it can see or hear Maggie."},
  ["actionref.magic.xphb2024"]={title="Magic",subtitle="Acao - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 371\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action, you cast a spell that has a casting time of an action or use a feature or magic item that requires a XPHB action to be activated.\n\nIf you cast a spell that has a casting time of 1 minute or longer, you must take the XPHB action on each turn of that casting, and you must maintain XPHB while you do so. If your XPHB is broken, the spell fails, but you don't expend a spell slot."},
  ["feature.magic-arrow.xge2024.fighter.arcane-archer.7"]={title="Magic Arrow",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 28\n\nAt 7th level, you gain the ability to infuse arrows with magic. Whenever you fire a nonmagical arrow from a shortbow or longbow, you can make it magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage. The magic fades from the arrow immediately after it hits or misses its target."},
  ["feature.magic-awareness.tce2014.barbarian.wild-magic.3"]={title="Magic Awareness",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["spell.magic-circle.phb2014"]={title="Magic Circle",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 256\n\nYou create a 10-foot-radius, 20-foot-tall cylinder of magical energy centered on a point on the ground that you can see within range. Glowing runes appear wherever the cylinder intersects with the floor or other surface.\n\nChoose one or more of the following types of creatures: celestials, elementals, fey, fiends, or undead. The circle affects a creature of the chosen type in the following ways:\n\n• The creature can't willingly enter the cylinder by nonmagical means. If the creature tries to use teleportation or interplanar travel to do so, it must first succeed on a Charisma saving throw.\n\n• The creature has disadvantage on attack rolls against targets within the cylinder.\n\n• Targets within the cylinder can't be charmed, frightened, or possessed by the creature.\n\nWhen you cast this spell, you can elect to cause its magic to operate in the reverse direction, preventing a creature of the specified type from leaving the cylinder and protecting targets outside it."},
  ["spell.magic-circle.xphb2024"]={title="Magic Circle",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 293\n\nYou create a 10-foot-radius, 20-foot-tall XPHB of magical energy centered on a point on the ground that you can see within range. Glowing runes appear wherever the XPHB intersects with the floor or other surface.\n\nChoose one or more of the following types of creatures: Celestials, Elementals, Fey, Fiends, or Undead. The circle affects a creature of the chosen type in the following ways:\n\n• The creature can't willingly enter the XPHB by nonmagical means. If the creature tries to use teleportation or interplanar travel to do so, it must first succeed on a Charisma saving throw.\n\n• The creature has XPHB on attack rolls against targets within the XPHB.\n\n• Targets within the XPHB can't be possessed by or gain the XPHB or XPHB condition from the creature.\n\nEach time you cast this spell, you can cause its magic to operate in the reverse direction, preventing a creature of the specified type from leaving the XPHB and protecting targets outside it."},
  ["feat.magic-connoisseur.au2014"]={title="Magic Connoisseur",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAdditional Spells\n\nChoose a level 1 and a level 2 spell from the same list you selected for the Magic Initiate feat's cantrips. You always have those spells prepared. You can cast each spell once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast those spells using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. The spellcasting ability for these spells is the same as the spellcasting ability chosen for your Magic Initiate feat's spells.\n\nSpell Change\n\nWhenever you gain a new level, you can replace one of the spells you chose for this feat with a different spell of the same level from the chosen spell list."},
  ["feat.magic-initiate.phb2014"]={title="Magic Initiate",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\nChoose a class: spells, spells, spells, spells, spells, or spells. You learn two cantrips of your choice from that class's spell list.\n\nIn addition, choose one 1st-level spell to learn from that same list. Using this feat, you can cast the spell once at its lowest level, and you must finish a long rest before you can cast it in this way again.\n\nYour spellcasting ability for these spells depends on the class you chose: Charisma for spells, spells, or spells; Wisdom for spells or spells; or Intelligence for spells."},
  ["feat.magic-initiate.xphb2024"]={title="Magic Initiate",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 201\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nTwo Cantrips\n\nYou learn two cantrips of your choice from the spells, spells, or spells spell list. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this feat's spells (choose when you select this feat).\n\nLevel 1 Spell\n\nChoose a level 1 spell from the same list you selected for this feat's cantrips. You always have that spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast the spell using any spell slots you have.\n\nSpell Change\n\nWhenever you gain a new level, you can replace one of the spells you chose for this feat with a different spell of the same level from the chosen spell list.\n\nRepeatable\n\nYou can take this feat more than once, but you must choose a different spell list each time."},
  ["feature.magic-item-adept.efa2014.artificer.base.10"]={title="Magic Item Adept",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou can now attune to up to four magic items at once."},
  ["feature.magic-item-adept.tce2014.artificer.base.10"]={title="Magic Item Adept",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n10th-level artificer feature\n\nYou've achieved a profound understanding of how to use and make magic items:\n\n• You can attune to up to four magic items at once.\n\n• If you craft a magic item with a rarity of common or uncommon, it takes you a quarter of the normal time, and it costs you half as much of the usual gold."},
  ["feature.magic-item-master.efa2014.artificer.base.18"]={title="Magic Item Master",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\nYou can now attune to up to six magic items at once."},
  ["feature.magic-item-master.tce2014.artificer.base.18"]={title="Magic Item Master",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n18th-level artificer feature\n\nYou can now attune to up to six magic items at once."},
  ["feature.magic-item-savant.tce2014.artificer.base.14"]={title="Magic Item Savant",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n14th-level artificer feature\n\nYour skill with magic items deepens:\n\n• You can attune to up to five magic items at once.\n\n• You ignore all class, race, spell, and level requirements on attuning to or using a magic item."},
  ["feature.magic-item-tinker.efa2014.artificer.base.6"]={title="Magic Item Tinker",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYour Artificer feature gains the following options.\n\nCharge Magic Item\n\nAs a XPHB, you can touch a magic item within 5 feet of yourself that you created with Replicate Magic Item and that uses charges. You expend a level 1+ spell slot and recharge the item. The number of charges the item regains is equal to the level of spell slot expended.\n\nDrain Magic Item\n\nAs a XPHB, you can touch a magic item within 5 feet of yourself that you created with Replicate Magic Item and cause the item to vanish, converting its magical energy into a spell slot. The slot is level 1 if the item is Common or level 2 if the item is Uncommon or Rare. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB. Any spell slot you create with this feature vanishes when you finish a XPHB.\n\nTransmute Magic Item\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can touch one magic item within 5 feet of yourself that you created with Replicate Magic Item and transform it into a different magic item. The resulting item must be based on a magic item plan you know. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["spell.magic-jar.phb2014"]={title="Magic Jar",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 257\n\nYour body falls into a catatonic state as your soul leaves it and enters the container you used for the spell's material component. While your soul inhabits the container, you are aware of your surroundings as if you were in the container's space. You can't move or use reactions. The only action you can take is to project your soul up to 100 feet out of the container, either returning to your living body (and ending the spell) or attempting to possess a humanoid's body.\n\nYou can attempt to possess any humanoid within 100 feet of you that you can see (creatures warded by a protection from evil and good or magic circle spell can't be possessed). The target must make a Charisma saving throw. On a failure, your soul moves into the target's body, and the target's soul becomes trapped in the container. On a success, the target resists your efforts to possess it, and you can't attempt to possess it again for 24 hours.\n\nOnce you possess a creature's body, you control it. Your game statistics are replaced by the statistics of the creature, though you retain your alignment and your Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. You retain the benefit of your own class features. If the target has any class levels, you can't use any of its class features.\n\nMeanwhile, the possessed creature's soul can perceive from the container using its own senses, but it can't move or take actions at all.\n\nWhile possessing a body, you can use your action to return from the host body to the container if it is within 100 feet of you, returning the host creature's soul to its body. If the host body dies while you're in it, the creature dies, and you must make a Charisma saving throw against your own spellcasting DC. On a success, you return to the container if it is within 100 feet of you. Otherwise, you die.\n\nIf the container is destroyed or the spell ends, your soul immediately returns to your body. If your body is more than 100 feet away from you or if your body is dead when you attempt to return to it, you die. If another creature's soul is in the container when it is destroyed, the creature's soul returns to its body if the body is alive and within 100 feet. Otherwise, that creature dies.\n\nWhen the spell ends, the container is destroyed."},
  ["spell.magic-jar.xphb2024"]={title="Magic Jar",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 294\n\nYour body falls into a catatonic state as your soul leaves it and enters the container you used for the spell's Material component. While your soul inhabits the container, you are aware of your surroundings as if you were in the container's space. You can't move or take Reactions. The only action you can take is to project your soul up to 100 feet out of the container, either returning to your living body (and ending the spell) or attempting to possess a Humanoid's body.\n\nYou can attempt to possess any Humanoid within 100 feet of you that you can see (creatures warded by a XPHB or XPHB spell can't be possessed). The target makes a Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, your soul enters the target's body, and the target's soul becomes trapped in the container. On a successful save, the target resists your efforts to possess it, and you can't attempt to possess it again for 24 hours.\n\nOnce you possess a creature's body, you control it. Your XPHB, XPHB, Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, XPHB, and senses are replaced by the creature's. You otherwise keep your game statistics.\n\nMeanwhile, the possessed creature's soul can perceive from the container using its own senses, but it can't move and it is XPHB.\n\nWhile possessing a body, you can take a XPHB action to return from the host body to the container if it is within 100 feet of you, returning the host creature's soul to its body. If the host body dies while you're in it, the creature dies, and you make a Charisma saving throw against your own spellcasting DC. On a success, you return to the container if it is within 100 feet of you. Otherwise, you die.\n\nIf the container is destroyed or the spell ends, your soul returns to your body. If your body is more than 100 feet away from you or if your body is dead, you die. If another creature's soul is in the container when it is destroyed, the creature's soul returns to its body if the body is alive and within 100 feet. Otherwise, that creature dies.\n\nWhen the spell ends, the container is destroyed."},
  ["spell.magic-missile.phb2014"]={title="Magic Missile",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 257\n\nYou create three glowing darts of magical force. Each dart hits a creature of your choice that you can see within range. A dart deals 1d4 + 1 force damage to its target. The darts all strike simultaneously, and you can direct them to hit one creature or several."},
  ["spell.magic-missile.xphb2024"]={title="Magic Missile",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 295\n\nYou create three glowing darts of magical force. Each dart strikes a creature of your choice that you can see within range. A dart deals 1d4 + 1 Force damage to its target. The darts all strike simultaneously, and you can direct them to hit one creature or several."},
  ["spell.magic-mouth.phb2014"]={title="Magic Mouth",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 257\n\nYou implant a message within an object in range, a message that is uttered when a trigger condition is met. Choose an object that you can see and that isn't being worn or carried by another creature. Then speak the message, which must be 25 words or less, though it can be delivered over as long as 10 minutes. Finally, determine the circumstance that will trigger the spell to deliver your message.\n\nWhen that circumstance occurs, a magical mouth appears on the object and recites the message in your voice and at the same volume you spoke. If the object you chose has a mouth or something that looks like a mouth (for example, the mouth of a statue), the magical mouth appears there so that the words appear to come from the object's mouth. When you cast this spell, you can have the spell end after it delivers its message, or it can remain and repeat its message whenever the trigger occurs.\n\nThe triggering circumstance can be as general or as detailed as you like, though it must be based on visual or audible conditions that occur within 30 feet of the object. For example, you could instruct the mouth to speak when any creature moves within 30 feet of the object or when a silver bell rings within 30 feet of it."},
  ["spell.magic-mouth.xphb2024"]={title="Magic Mouth",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 295\n\nYou implant a message within an object in range—a message that is uttered when a trigger condition is met. Choose an object that you can see and that isn't being worn or carried by another creature. Then speak the message, which must be 25 words or fewer, though it can be delivered over as long as 10 minutes. Finally, determine the circumstance that will trigger the spell to deliver your message.\n\nWhen that trigger occurs, a magical mouth appears on the object and recites the message in your voice and at the same volume you spoke. If the object you chose has a mouth or something that looks like a mouth (for example, the mouth of a statue), the magical mouth appears there, so the words appear to come from the object's mouth. When you cast this spell, you can have the spell end after it delivers its message, or it can remain and repeat its message whenever the trigger occurs.\n\nThe trigger can be as general or as detailed as you like, though it must be based on visual or audible conditions that occur within 30 feet of the object. For example, you could instruct the mouth to speak when any creature moves within 30 feet of the object or when a silver bell rings within 30 feet of it."},
  ["spell.magic-stone.xge2024"]={title="Magic Stone",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 160\n\nYou touch one to three pebbles and imbue them with magic. You or someone else can make a ranged spell attack with one of the pebbles by throwing it or hurling it with a phb. If thrown, a pebble has a range of 60 feet. If someone else attacks with a pebble, that attacker adds your spellcasting ability modifier, not the attacker's, to the attack roll. On a hit, the target takes bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + your spellcasting ability modifier. Whether the attack hits or misses, the spell then ends on the stone.\n\nIf you cast this spell again, the spell ends on any pebbles still affected by your previous casting."},
  ["spell.magic-weapon.phb2014"]={title="Magic Weapon",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 257\n\nYou touch a nonmagical weapon. Until the spell ends, that weapon becomes a magic weapon with a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls."},
  ["spell.magic-weapon.xphb2024"]={title="Magic Weapon",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 295\n\nYou touch a nonmagical weapon. Until the spell ends, that weapon becomes a magic weapon with a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls. The spell ends early if you cast it again."},
  ["feature.magic-user-s-nemesis.xge2024.ranger.monster-slayer.11"]={title="Magic-User's Nemesis",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.magical-ambush.phb2014.rogue.arcane-trickster.9"]={title="Magical Ambush",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\nStarting at 9th level, if you are hidden from a creature when you cast a spell on it, the creature has disadvantage on any saving throw it makes against the spell this turn."},
  ["feature.magical-ambush.xphb2024.rogue.arcane-trickster.9"]={title="Magical Ambush",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 133\n\nIf you have the XPHB condition when you cast a spell on a creature, it has XPHB on any saving throw it makes against the spell on the same turn."},
  ["feature.magical-ammunition.au2014.fighter.arcane-archer.7"]={title="Magical Ammunition",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.magical-cunning.xphb2024.warlock.base.2"]={title="Magical Cunning",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.magical-discoveries.xphb2024.bard.lore.6"]={title="Magical Discoveries",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 66\n\nYou learn two spells of your choice. These spells can come from the spells, spells, or spells or any combination thereof (see a class's section for its spell list). A spell you choose must be a cantrip or a spell for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Bard Features table.\n\nYou always have the chosen spells prepared, and whenever you gain a Bard level, you can replace one of the spells with another spell that meets these requirements."},
  ["feature.magical-guidance.tce2014.sorcerer.base.5"]={title="Magical Guidance",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 65\n\n{@i 5th-level sorcerer tce\n\nYou can tap into your inner wellspring of magic to try to conjure success from failure. When you make an ability check that fails, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll the d20, and you must use the new roll, potentially turning the failure into a success."},
  ["feature.magical-inspiration.tce2014.bard.base.2"]={title="Magical Inspiration",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n{@i 2nd-level bard tce\n\nIf a creature has a Bardic Inspiration die from you and casts a spell that restores hit points or deals damage, the creature can roll that die and choose a target affected by the spell. Add the number rolled as a bonus to the hit points regained or the damage dealt. The Bardic Inspiration die is then lost."},
  ["feature.magical-mastery.au2014.cleric.arcana.17"]={title="Magical Mastery",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nYou learn four spells, one from each of levels 6, 7, 8, and 9. You thereafter always have those spells prepared. Whenever you gain a Cleric level, you can replace one of these spells with another spells of the same level."},
  ["traphazard.magical-mirage.fraif2014"]={title="Magical Mirage",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nMagical mirages are created by ambient magic. Such a mirage seems real, including sounds and smells appropriate to the thing depicted, but it can't deal damage or cause conditions. Physical inspection of the mirage reveals it to be an illusion, for things can pass through it.\n\nFor example, a magical mirage might depict an oasis complete with local flora and fauna, but a creature wading into the oasis's pond would find only a sandy pit.\n\nExamples of magical mirages include lively oases, and pristine ancient temples.\n\nSeeing through a Mirage\n\nAs a XPHB action, a creature can inspect the image and make a 15 Intelligence (XPHB). If a creature discerns the mirage's nature, the mirage becomes faint to the creature."},
  ["feature.magical-secrets.phb2014.bard.base.10"]={title="Magical Secrets",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nBy 10th level, you have plundered magical knowledge from a wide spectrum of disciplines. Choose two spells from any classes, including this one. A spell you choose must be of a level you can cast, as shown on the Bard table, or a cantrip.\n\nThe chosen spells count as bard spells for you and are included in the number in the Spells Known column of the Bard table.\n\nYou learn two additional spells from any classes at 14th level and again at 18th level."},
  ["feature.magical-secrets.phb2014.bard.base.14"]={title="Magical Secrets",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nAt 14th level, choose two additional spells from any classes, including this one. A spell you choose must be of a level you can cast, as shown on the Bard table, or a cantrip.\n\nThe chosen spells count as bard spells for you and are included in the number in the Spells Known column of the Bard table."},
  ["feature.magical-secrets.phb2014.bard.base.18"]={title="Magical Secrets",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nAt 18th level, choose two additional spells from any class, including this one. A spell you choose must be of a level you can cast, as shown on the Bard table, or a cantrip.\n\nThe chosen spells count as bard spells for you and are included in the number in the Spells Known column of the Bard table."},
  ["feature.magical-secrets.xphb2024.bard.base.10"]={title="Magical Secrets",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 61\n\nYou've learned secrets from various magical traditions. Whenever you reach a Bard level (including this level) and the Prepared Spells number in the Bard Features table increases, you can choose any of your new prepared spells from the spells, spells, spells, and spells spells, and the chosen spells count as Bard spells for you (see a class's section for its spell list). In addition, whenever you replace a spell prepared for this class, you can replace it with a spell from those lists."},
  ["feature.magical-tinkering.tce2014.artificer.base.1"]={title="Magical Tinkering",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n1st-level artificer feature\n\nYou've learned how to invest a spark of magic into mundane objects. To use this ability, you must have PHB or PHB in hand. You then touch a Tiny nonmagical object as an action and give it one of the following magical properties of your choice:\n\n• The object sheds bright light in a 5-foot radius and dim light for an additional 5 feet.\n\n• Whenever tapped by a creature, the object emits a recorded message that can be heard up to 10 feet away. You utter the message when you bestow this property on the object, and the recording can be no more than 6 seconds long.\n\n• The object continuously emits your choice of an odor or a nonverbal sound (wind, waves, chirping, or the like). The chosen phenomenon is perceivable up to 10 feet away.\n\n• A static visual effect appears on one of the object's surfaces. This effect can be a picture, up to 25 words of text, lines and shapes, or a mixture of these elements, as you like.\n\nThe chosen property lasts indefinitely. As an action, you can touch the object and end the property early.\n\nYou can bestow magic on multiple objects, touching one object each time you use this feature, though a single object can only bear one property at a time. The maximum number of objects you can affect with this feature at one time is equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of one object). If you try to exceed your maximum, the oldest property immediately ends, and then the new property applies."},
  ["feature.magician.xphb2024.druid.base.1"]={title="Magician",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.magister-umbero-zastro.wdh2014"]={title="Magister Umbero Zastro",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 12 | CON 11 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nUmbero has advantage on saving throws against being charmed and magic can't put him to sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRapier\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe noble adds 2 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the noble must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["deity.maglubiyet.phb2014"]={title="Maglubiyet",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["creature.magma-mephit.mm2014"]={title="Magma Mephit",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 22 (5d6 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 7 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Ignan, Terran\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: cold\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Burst\n\nWhen the mephit dies, it explodes in a burst of lava. Each creature within 5 feet of it must make a 11 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the mephit remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary mound of magma.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (1/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h3 (1d4 + 1) slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge}\n\nThe mephit exhales a 15-foot cone of fire. Each creature in that area must make a 11 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.magma-mephit.xmm2024"]={title="Magma Mephit",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 207\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 18 (4d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 7 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Ignan, Terran)\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: cold\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Burst\n\nThe mephit explodes when it dies. dex 11, each creature in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the mephit. actSaveFail 7 (2d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h3 (1d4 + 1) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge}\n\ndex 11, each creature in a 15-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 7 (2d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.magmin.mm2014"]={title="Magmin",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Ignan\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Burst\n\nWhen the magmin dies, it explodes in a burst of fire and magma. Each creature within 10 feet of it must make a 11 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Flammable objects that aren't being worn or carried in that area are ignited.\n\nIgnited Illumination\n\nAs a bonus action, the magmin can set itself ablaze or extinguish its flames. While ablaze, the magmin sheds bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTouch\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d6) fire damage. If the target is a creature or a flammable object, it ignites. Until a creature takes an action to douse the fire, the target takes 3 (1d6) fire damage at the end of each of its turns."},
  ["creature.magmin.xmm2024"]={title="Magmin",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 200\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 13 (3d6 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Ignan)\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Burst\n\nThe magmin explodes when it dies. dex 11, each creature in a 10-foot XPHB originating from the magmin. actSaveFail 7 (2d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTouch\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h7 (2d4 + 2) Fire damage. If the target is a creature or a flammable object that isn't being worn or carried, it starts XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nIgnited Illumination\n\nThe magmin sets itself ablaze or extinguishes its flames. While ablaze, the magmin sheds XPHB in a 10-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 10 feet."},
  ["creature.magnifico.nrh-coi2014"]={title="Magnifico",subtitle="Criatura - NRH-CoI - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCunning Action\n\nOn each of his turns, Magnifico can use a bonus action to take the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nHand Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["spell.magnify-gravity.egw2014"]={title="Magnify Gravity",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 188\n\nThe gravity in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you can see within range increases for a moment. Each creature in the sphere on the turn when you cast the spell must make a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 2d8 force damage, and its speed is halved until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and suffers no reduction to its speed.\n\nUntil the start of your next turn, any object that isn't being worn or carried in the sphere requires a successful Strength check against your spell save DC to pick up or move."},
  ["item.magnifying-glass.phb2014"]={title="Magnifying Glass",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis lens allows a closer look at small objects. It is also useful as a substitute for flint and steel when starting fires. Lighting a fire with a magnifying glass requires light as bright as sunlight to focus, tinder to ignite, and about 5 minutes for the fire to ignite. A magnifying glass grants advantage on any ability check made to appraise or inspect an item that is small or highly detailed."},
  ["item.magnifying-glass.xphb2024"]={title="Magnifying Glass",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 226\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Magnifying Glass grants XPHB on any ability check made to appraise or inspect a highly detailed item. Lighting a fire with a Magnifying Glass requires light as bright as sunlight to focus, tinder to ignite, and about 5 minutes for the fire to ignite."},
  ["creature.mahadi-the-rakshasa.bgdia2014"]={title="Mahadi the Rakshasa",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 195 (23d8 + 92)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 18 | CON 18 | INT 14 | WIS 18 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all (can read only), Common, Infernal\n\nResistencias: \n\nVulnerabilidades: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLimited Magic Immunity\n\nMahadi can't be affected or detected by spells of 6th level or lower unless he wishes to be. He has advantage on saving throws against all other spells and magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nMahadi's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMahadi makes four claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) slashing damage, and the target is cursed if it's a creature. The curse takes effect whenever the target takes a short or long rest, filling the target's thoughts with horrible images and dreams. The cursed target gains no benefit from finishing a short or long rest. The curse lasts until it is lifted by a remove curse spell or similar magic.\n\nSummon Erinyes (1/Day)\n\nMahadi summons Ilzabet, an erinyes bound to him by an infernal contract. The erinyes appears in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of him, acts as his ally, and can't summon other devils. The erinyes remains for 10 minutes or until Mahadi dismisses it as an action. If the erinyes dies, Mahadi loses this action option."},
  ["deity.majere.dsotdq2014"]={title="Majere",subtitle="Divindade - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nAustere and aloof, Majere is the god of meditation and discipline. Monks, his most devoted followers, honor him by leading lives of quiet contemplation in remote monasteries. Many orphans are raised in the monasteries of Majere; some become monks themselves, while those who leave the monastic life often take the surname Majere out of respect."},
  ["deity.majere.phb2014"]={title="Majere",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["creature.majesto.cos2014"]={title="Majesto",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["spell.major-image.phb2014"]={title="Major Image",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nYou create the image of an object, a creature, or some other visible phenomenon that is no larger than a 20-foot cube. The image appears at a spot that you can see within range and lasts for the duration. It seems completely real, including sounds, smells, and temperature appropriate to the thing depicted. You can't create sufficient heat or cold to cause damage, a sound loud enough to deal thunder damage or deafen a creature, or a smell that might sicken a creature (like a troglodyte stench).\n\nAs long as you are within range of the illusion, you can use your action to cause the image to move to any other spot within range. As the image changes location, you can alter its appearance so that its movements appear natural for the image. For example, if you create an image of a creature and move it, you can alter the image so that it appears to be walking. Similarly, you can cause the illusion to make different sounds at different times, even making it carry on a conversation, for example.\n\nPhysical interaction with the image reveals it to be an illusion, because things can pass through it. A creature that uses its action to examine the image can determine that it is an illusion with a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. If a creature discerns the illusion for what it is, the creature can see through the image, and its other sensory qualities become faint to the creature."},
  ["spell.major-image.xphb2024"]={title="Major Image",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 295\n\nYou create the image of an object, a creature, or some other visible phenomenon that is no larger than a 20-foot XPHB. The image appears at a spot that you can see within range and lasts for the duration. It seems real, including sounds, smells, and temperature appropriate to the thing depicted, but it can't deal damage or cause conditions.\n\nIf you are within range of the illusion, you can take a XPHB action to cause the image to move to any other spot within range. As the image changes location, you can alter its appearance so that its movements appear natural for the image. For example, if you create an image of a creature and move it, you can alter the image so that it appears to be walking. Similarly, you can cause the illusion to make different sounds at different times, even making it carry on a conversation, for example.\n\nPhysical interaction with the image reveals it to be an illusion, for things can pass through it. A creature that takes a XPHB action to examine the image can determine that it is an illusion with a successful Intelligence (XPHB) check against your spell save DC. If a creature discerns the illusion for what it is, the creature can see through the image, and its other sensory qualities become faint to the creature."},
  ["item.malachite.dmg2014"]={title="Malachite",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAn opaque striated light and dark green gemstone."},
  ["item.malachite.xdmg2024"]={title="Malachite",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA striated light and dark green gemstone."},
  ["creature.malaina-van-talstiv.veor2014"]={title="Malaina van Talstiv",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 41\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["deity.malar.frhof2014"]={title="Malar",subtitle="Divindade - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 114\n\nMalar inspires the thrill of adrenaline experienced by a predator chasing its next meal. He epitomizes the bloody, sadistic side of nature, the world that is red in tooth and claw. He is the god of those who delight in the hunt, don't shy from bloodshed, and savor the fear of their prey.\n\nMalar is a bestial deity, depicted in paintings and murals as a feline monster. When he needs to make his will known on the Material Plane, he sends a ferocious predator drenched in blood, such as a XMM, an XMM, or a XMM. Malar's intentions rumble and snarl in the minds of those experiencing the delights of savage violence, urging them on and basking in their bloodlust.\n\nFoolish mortals attempt to propitiate Malar with offerings or prayers, hoping to avoid attacks by wild animals. These efforts are in vain, for Malar shows no mercy. Those who worship him instead attempt to embody his peerless hunting skill. Berserkers scream prayers to Malar as they rage, and hunters whisper a prayer before closing in for the kill. Lycanthropes see themselves in Malar's uncontrollable savagery. Malar's followers wear or carry trinkets from the fearsome creatures they've slain. Teeth, pelts, wings, claws—the more ferocious, the better.\n\nPriests of Malar believe in the survival of the fittest, and none are allowed to enter the priesthood without first demonstrating prowess in hunting and combat. Malar has no temples in Faerûn's major cities, but villages on the edges of the wilderness might house a temple. During the tenday leading up to FRHoF, priests of Malar hunt tirelessly for as much game as they can find. They then invite members of the community to join them at a great feast on Highharvestide called the Feast of the Stags. They keep quiet the dreaded High Hunt ritual, in which priests of Malar choose someone to become their prey for a day and a night. If the prey survives, they gain a favor from the priests of Malar, but death is a far more likely outcome.\n\nMalar's Chosen are gifted trackers, sometimes blessed with lycanthropy. It is said that the Chosen of Malar can smell their quarry from miles away."},
  ["deity.malar.phb2014"]={title="Malar",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 294"},
  ["deity.malar.scag2014"]={title="Malar",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nMalar epitomizes the dark side of nature, the world that is red in tooth and claw. His faithful believe the hunt is the center point between life and death - the facing off of hunter and prey, forcing the issue of who lives and who dies. People believe that Malar can't be propitiated and knows no mercy, so he receives prayers only from those engaging in a hunt. Such supplicants pray to Malar for two reasons: to beg the aid of his peerless skill as a hunter, or to adopt his fearsome mantle and thus ward off other predators. Malar is the god of those who delight in the hunt, don't shy from bloodshed, and savor the fear of their prey.\n\nMany lycanthropes consider Malar to be their divine father, as do some other intelligent predators. He has many devotees who are druids and rangers of particularly savage inclination, and many barbarians take Malar as a patron for his ferocity and cruelty. His priests use claw bracers, impressive gauntlets bedecked with stylized claws that jut out from the ends of the fists, as ceremonial weapons."},
  ["creature.malaxxix.bmt2014"]={title="Malaxxix",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / H\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 312 (25d12 + 150)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 60\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 16 | CON 22 | INT 22 | WIS 20 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Malaxxix fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nMalaxxix has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMalaxxix makes two Forge Hammer or Whip attacks in any combination.\n\nForge Hammer\n\nmw,rw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft. or range 60/180 ft., one target. h28 (4d10 + 6) bludgeoning damage, and the target can't take reactions until the end of Malaxxix's next turn. homThe hammer then magically returns to Malaxxix's hand.\n\nWhip\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 30 ft., one creature. h15 (2d8 + 6) slashing damage, and the target has the restrained condition for 1 minute. The restrained target can make a 20 Strength saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Only one creature can be restrained by the whip at a time.\n\nMezzoloth Vortex {@recharge 5}\n\nMalaxxix summons a vortex of whirling mezzoloths at a point it can see within 90 feet of itself. The vortex is a 30-foot-radius, 100-foot-high cylinder centered on that point. Each creature other than Malaxxix in that area must make a 20 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 35 (10d6) force damage and has the restrained condition while within the cylinder. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and is pushed to the nearest unoccupied space outside the cylinder. The vortex lasts until the start of Malaxxix's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFiendish Stride\n\nMalaxxix moves up to its speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks. When Malaxxix moves within 5 feet of a creature during this movement, that creature takes 5 (1d10) lightning damage. A creature can take this damage only once per turn.\n\nAttack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nMalaxxix makes one Forge Hammer or Whip attack."},
  ["creature.male-steeder.mpmm2014"]={title="Male Steeder",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 231\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 13 (2d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nExtraordinary Leap\n\nThe distance of the steeder's long jumps is tripled; every foot of its walking speed that it spends on the jump allows it to jump 3 feet.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe steeder can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) poison damage.\n\nSticky Leg\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Small or Tiny creature. hThe target is stuck to the steeder's leg and grappled (escape 12). The steeder can have only one creature grappled at a time."},
  ["creature.male-steeder.mtf2014"]={title="Male Steeder",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 238\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 13 (2d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe steeder can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nExtraordinary Leap\n\nThe distance of the steeder's long jumps is tripled; every foot of its walking speed that it spends on the jump allows it to jump 3 feet.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) poison damage.\n\nSticky Leg\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Small or Tiny creature. hThe target is stuck to the steeder's leg and is grappled until it escapes (escape 12). The steeder can have only one creature grappled at a time."},
  ["creature.male-steeder.oota2014"]={title="Male Steeder",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 231\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 13 (2d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe steeder can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nLeap\n\nThe steeder can expend all its movement on its turn to jump up to 60 feet vertically or horizontally, provided that its speed is at least 30 feet.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h7 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage, and the target must make a 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 4 (1d8) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nSticky Leg (Recharges when the Steeder Has No Creatures Grappled)\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Small or Tiny creature. hThe target is stuck to the steeder's leg and grappled until it escapes (escape 12)."},
  ["creature.malformed-kraken.tftyp2014"]={title="Malformed Kraken",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 239\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 172 (15d12 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 40\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 11 | CON 20 | INT 11 | WIS 15 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, paralyzed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe kraken can breathe air and water.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe kraken deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe kraken makes three tentacle attacks. One of them can be replaced with a bite attack, and any of them can be replaced with Fling.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d8 + 7) piercing damage.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 16). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained. The kraken has ten tentacles, each of which can grapple one target.\n\nFling\n\nOne Medium or smaller object held or creature grappled by the kraken's tentacles is thrown up to 60 feet in a random direction and knocked prone. If a thrown target strikes a solid surface, the target takes 3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage for every 10 feet it was thrown. If the target is thrown at another creature, that creature must succeed on a 16 Dexterity saving throw or take the same damage and be knocked prone.\n\nLightning Storm\n\nThe kraken creates three bolts of lightning, each of which can strike a target the kraken can see within 150 feet of it. A target must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 16 (3d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["traphazard.malfunctioning-phase-transference-emitter.azfyt2014"]={title="Malfunctioning Phase Transference Emitter",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - AZfyT - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nThe malfunctioning Phase Transference Emitter consists of two primary components. The power battery is a 10-foot circular matrix of conduction coils wired directly to a generator via a secure power cable. The coils have ten nodes that connect to a large eight-foot tall cylindrical steel emitter rigged on a swivel."},
  ["item.malice.dmg2014"]={title="Malice",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned for 1 hour. The poisoned creature is blinded."},
  ["item.malice.xdmg2024"]={title="Malice",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 91\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature subjected to Malice must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or have the XPHB condition for 1 hour. The creature also has the XPHB condition while XPHB in this way."},
  ["creature.malinia.pabtso2014"]={title="Malinia",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.malivar.aitfr-isf2014"]={title="Malivar",subtitle="Criatura - AitFR-ISF - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Ignan, Infernal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBenign Transportation (Recharges after Malivar Casts a Conjuration Spell of 1st Level or Higher)\n\nAs a bonus action, Malivar teleports up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space that he can see.\n\nIf he instead chooses a space within range that is occupied by a willing Small or Medium creature, they both teleport, swapping places.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["feature.malleable-illusions.phb2014.wizard.illusion.6"]={title="Malleable Illusions",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\nStarting at 6th level, when you cast an illusion spell that has a duration of 1 minute or longer, you can use your action to change the nature of that illusion (using the spell's normal parameters for the illusion), provided that you can see the illusion."},
  ["traphazard.malnutrition.xphb2024"]={title="Malnutrition",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 371\n\nA creature needs an amount of food per day based on its size, as shown in the Food Needs per Day table. A creature that eats but consumes less than half the required food for a day must succeed on a 10 Constitution XPHB or gain 1 XPHB level at the day's end. A creature that eats nothing for 5 days automatically gains 1 XPHB level at the end of the fifth day as well as an additional level at the end of each subsequent day without food.\n\nXPHB caused by malnutrition can't be removed until the creature eats the full amount of food required for a day.\n\nSize | Food\n\nTiny | 1/4 pound\n\nSmall | 1 pound\n\nMedium | 1 pound\n\nLarge | 4 pounds\n\nHuge | 16 pounds\n\nGargantuan | 64 pounds"},
  ["deity.malyk.mtf2014"]={title="Malyk",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 54\n\nMalyk embodies rebellion and chaos. Drow know of his influence from the appearance of wild mages among their number. Such an individual, possessed of sorcerous powers seemingly bestowed at random, is often seen as a threat to the established order. Many drow, especially males and even females of low station, try to attract Malyk's attention by secretly making sacrifices to him. Meanwhile, house matrons and others steeped in the faith of Lolth attempt to purge Malyk's worship from drow society-at the same time that some of them pray to him for power.\n\nMalyk is associated with rebellion because when a wild mage's true nature is revealed, the individual often has no recourse but to openly attack others and create chaos. Most other drow vie to receive Lolth's blessing by being the one to bring such a blasphemer to justice. In order to survive, a wild mage must defeat or elude all attackers and forge an alliance with those who can be threatened or bribed to provide a safe haven. Most wild mages who are discovered are put to death, some survive as outcasts, and a rare few rise to positions of status, declaring their allegiance to Lolth-or at least pretending to."},
  ["creature.mammon.coa2014"]={title="Mammon",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 230\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / H\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 464 (32d12 + 256)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 17 | CON 26 | INT 22 | WIS 25 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft., truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede Mammon's darkvision.\n\nFiendish Regeneration\n\nMammon regains 20 hit points at the start of his turn. If he takes radiant damage this trait doesn't function at the start of his next turn. Mammon only dies if he starts his turn with 0 hit points and is unable to regenerate.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Mammon fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nMammon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMammon uses Fearful Gaze, then makes four attacks using Tail Swipe, Constrict, or a combination of the two.\n\nTail Swipe\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h31 (4d10 + 9) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the grappled condition (escape 21). While grappled, the creature also has the restrained condition, and Mammon can't make Tail Swipe attacks.\n\nFearful Gaze\n\nMammon focuses his gaze in a 90-foot cone in front of him. Each creature of his choice within the cone must make a 23 Wisdom saving throw, taking 19 (3d12) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Creatures that fail the save have the frightened condition until the end of their next turn.\n\nConstrict\n\nMammon tightens his grip around a creature he has grappled. The target takes 35 (4d12 + 9) bludgeoning damage.\n\nGolden Gaze {@recharge}\n\nMammon attempts to turn one creature he can see within 60 feet of him into solid gold. The target must make a 23 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target's flesh begins to harden, and it has the restrained condition. A restrained creature must repeat the saving throw at the end of each turn. If it successfully saves three times, the effect ends. If it fails three times, it turns to gold and now has the petrified condition. Successes and failures don't need to be consecutive.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nPain Tax\n\nAs a reaction to taking damage, Mammon causes the attacker's valuables to glow red hot. This deals 3 (1d6) fire damage to the attacker for every 100 gold (or equivalent in gems, jewelry, and other coinage) that it currently carries.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nChange Form\n\nMammon changes his form into that of a pit fiend, maintaining his statistics but losing his actions. He gains the actions and mobility of a pit fiend, including its weapon, and maintains his legendary actions and lair actions. Mammon's serpentine abilities can still recharge while he is in pit fiend form. If Mammon is already a pit fiend, this action changes him back into his serpentine form.\n\nGolden Touch (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nMammon recharges Golden Gaze.\n\nCall Underling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nMammon summons an allied horned devil in an unoccupied space that he can see."},
  ["creature.mammoth.mm2014"]={title="Mammoth",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 332\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 126 (11d12 + 55)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 9 | CON 21 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTrampling Charge\n\nIf the mammoth moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the mammoth can make one stomp attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h25 (4d8 + 7) piercing damage.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one prone creature. h29 (4d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.mammoth.xmm2024"]={title="Mammoth",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 365\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 126 (11d12 + 55)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 9 | CON 21 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\nSalvamentos: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe mammoth makes two Gore attacks.\n\nGore\n\nm 10, reach 10 ft. h18 (2d10 + 7) Piercing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature and the mammoth moved 20+ feet straight toward it immediately before the hit, the target has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTrample\n\ndex 18, one creature within 5 feet that has the XPHB condition. actSaveFail 29 (4d10 + 7) Bludgeoning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["item.manacles.phb2014"]={title="Manacles",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThese metal restraints can bind a Small or Medium creature. Escaping the manacles requires a successful 20 Dexterity check. Breaking them requires a successful 20 Strength check. Each set of manacles comes with one key. Without the key, a creature proficient with PHB can pick the manacles' lock with a successful 15 Dexterity check. Manacles have 15 hit points."},
  ["item.manacles.xphb2024"]={title="Manacles",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 226\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can use Manacles to bind an unwilling Small or Medium creature within 5 feet of yourself that has the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB condition if you succeed on a 13 Dexterity (XPHB) check. While bound, a creature has XPHB on attack rolls, and the creature is XPHB if the Manacles are attached to a chain or hook that is fixed in place. Escaping the Manacles requires a successful 20 Dexterity (XPHB) check as an action. Bursting them requires a successful 25 Strength (XPHB) check as an action.\n\nEach set of Manacles comes with a key. Without the key, a creature can use XPHB to pick the Manacles' lock with a successful 15 Dexterity (XPHB) check."},
  ["creature.manafret-cherryport.wdh2014"]={title="Manafret Cherryport",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 31 (9d6)\n\nIdiomas: Common, Halfling"},
  ["deity.manannan-mac-lir.phb2014"]={title="Manannan mac Lir",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["creature.manes.mm2014"]={title="Manes",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 9\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 9 | CON 13 | INT 3 | WIS 8 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (2d4) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.manes.xmm2024"]={title="Manes",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 9\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 9 | CON 13 | INT 3 | WIS 8 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nm 2, reach 5 ft. h5 (2d4) Slashing damage."},
  ["creature.manes-vaporspawn.xmm2024"]={title="Manes Vaporspawn",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, poisoned, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nContortionist\n\nThe manes can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra movement to do so.\n\nSickening Vapors\n\ncon 12, each creature in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the manes at the end of the manes's turn. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccess The target is immune to this manes's Sickening Vapors for 24 hours.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage plus 5 (2d4) Necrotic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShadow Stealth\n\nWhile in XPHB or XPHB, the manes takes the XPHB action."},
  ["feature.maneuver-options.tce2014.fighter.battle-master.3"]={title="Maneuver Options",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.maneuver-options.xphb2024.fighter.battle-master.3"]={title="Maneuver Options",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.maneuvering-attack.phb2014"]={title="Maneuvering Attack",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 74\n\nWhen you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to maneuver one of your comrades into a more advantageous position. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and you choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you. That creature can use its reaction to move up to half its speed without provoking opportunity attacks from the target of your attack."},
  ["optionalfeature.maneuvering-attack.xphb2024"]={title="Maneuvering Attack",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 95\n\nWhen you hit a creature with an attack roll, you can expend one Superiority Die to maneuver one of your comrades into another position. Add the Superiority Die roll to the attack's damage roll, and choose a willing creature who can see or hear you. That creature can use its XPHB to move up to half its XPHB without provoking an XPHB from the target of your attack."},
  ["feature.maneuvers.phb2014.fighter.battle-master.3"]={title="Maneuvers",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["object.mangonel.dmg2014"]={title="Mangonel",subtitle="Objeto - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 255\n\nA mangonel is a type of catapult that hurls heavy projectiles in a high arc. This payload can hit targets behind cover. Before the mangonel can be fired, it must be loaded and aimed. It takes two actions to load the weapon, two actions to aim it, and one action to fire it.\n\nA mangonel typically hurls a heavy stone, although it can hurl other kinds of projectiles, with different effects."},
  ["object.mangonel.xdmg2024"]={title="Mangonel",subtitle="Objeto - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 97\n\nA Mangonel is a catapult that hurls heavy projectiles in a high arc, so it can hit targets behind walls. Loading a Mangonel requires two XPHB actions, and aiming it requires two more XPHB actions. Then a crew member can take the Mangonel Stone action."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-daanvi-the-perfect-order.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Daanvi, the Perfect Order",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nYou can expend the Charm (no action required) to end the XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB condition on yourself."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-dolurrh-the-realm-of-the-dead.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Dolurrh, the Realm of the Dead",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhen you use a spell slot to cast a spell from the Necromancy school, you can expend the Charm (no action required) to treat the spell as if it were cast using a spell slot 1 level above the slot expended."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-fernia-the-sea-of-fire.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Fernia, the Sea of Fire",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhen you use a spell slot to cast a spell that deals Fire damage, you can expend the Charm (no action required) to treat the spell as if it were cast using a spell slot 1 level above the slot expended."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-irian-the-eternal-dawn.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Irian, the Eternal Dawn",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhen you use a spell slot to cast a spell that restores Hit Points or deals Radiant damage, you can expend the Charm (no action required) to treat the spell as if it were cast using a spell slot 1 level above the slot expended."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-lamannia-the-twilight-forest.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Lamannia, the Twilight Forest",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhen you use a spell slot to cast a spell that conjures or summons a Beast, an Elemental, or a Fey (including XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB), you can expend the Charm (no action required) to treat the spell as if it were cast using a spell slot 1 level above the slot expended."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-mabar-the-endless-night.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Mabar, the Endless Night",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhen you use a spell slot to cast a spell that animates or summons an Undead (including XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB), you can expend the Charm (no action required) to treat the spell as if it were cast using a spell slot 1 level above the slot expended."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-risia-the-plain-of-ice.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Risia, the Plain of Ice",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhen you use a spell slot to cast a spell that deals Cold damage, you can expend the Charm (no action required) to treat the spell as if it were cast using a spell slot 1 level above the slot expended."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-shavarath-the-battleground.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Shavarath, the Battleground",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhen you score a Critical Hit, you can expend the Charm (no action required) to deal an extra 10 damage of one of the types dealt by the attack."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-syrania-the-azure-sky.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Syrania, the Azure Sky",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nYou can expend the Charm as a Bonus Action to gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed for 1 minute."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-thelanis-the-faerie-court.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Thelanis, the Faerie Court",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhen you cast a spell from the Enchantment or Illusion school, you can expend the Charm (no action required) to give one target of the spell Disadvantage on its saving throw against the spell."},
  ["reward.manifest-charm-of-xoriat-the-realm-of-delirium.efa2014"]={title="Manifest Charm of Xoriat, the Realm of Delirium",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nWhen you use a spell slot to cast a spell, you can expend the Charm (no action required) to roll on the XPHB in the XPHB."},
  ["feature.manifest-echo.egw2014.fighter.echo-knight.3"]={title="Manifest Echo",subtitle="Caracteristica - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 183\n\n3rd-level Echo Knight feature\n\nYou can use a bonus action to magically manifest an echo of yourself in an unoccupied space you can see within 15 feet of you. This echo is a magical, translucent, gray image of you that lasts until it is destroyed, until you dismiss it as a bonus action, until you manifest another echo, or until you're incapacitated.\n\nYour echo has AC 14 + your proficiency bonus, 1 hit point, and immunity to all conditions. If it has to make a saving throw, it uses your saving throw bonus for the roll. It is the same size as you, and it occupies its space. On your turn, you can mentally command the echo to move up to 30 feet in any direction (no action required). If your echo is ever more than 30 feet from you at the end of your turn, it is destroyed.\n\nYou can use the echo in the following ways:\n\n• As a bonus action, you can teleport, magically swapping places with your echo at a cost of 15 feet of your movement, regardless of the distance between the two of you.\n\n• When you take the Attack action on your turn, any attack you make with that action can originate from your space or the echo's space. You make this choice for each attack.\n\n• When a creature that you can see within 5 feet of your echo moves at least 5 feet away from it, you can use your reaction to make an opportunity attack against that creature as if you were in the echo's space."},
  ["feature.manifest-mind.tce2014.wizard.scribes.6"]={title="Manifest Mind",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 78\n\n6th-level Order of Scribes feature\n\nYou can conjure forth the mind of your Awakened Spellbook. As a bonus action while the book is on your person, you can cause the mind to manifest as a Tiny spectral object, hovering in an unoccupied space of your choice within 60 feet of you. The spectral mind is intangible and doesn't occupy its space, and it sheds dim light in a 10-foot radius. It looks like a ghostly tome, a cascade of text, or a scholar from the past (your choice).\n\nWhile manifested, the spectral mind can hear and see, and it has darkvision with a range of 60 feet. The mind can telepathically share with you what it sees and hears (no action required).\n\nWhenever you cast a wizard spell on your turn, you can cast it as if you were in the spectral mind's space, instead of your own, using its senses. You can do so a number of times per day equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nAs a bonus action, you can cause the spectral mind to hover up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space that you or it can see. It can pass through creatures but not objects.\n\nThe spectral mind stops manifesting if it is ever more than 300 feet away from you, if someone casts dispel magic on it, if the Awakened Spellbook is destroyed, if you die, or if you dismiss the spectral mind as a bonus action.\n\nOnce you conjure the mind, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend a spell slot of any level to conjure it again."},
  ["magicitem.manifold-tool.efa2014"]={title="Manifold Tool",subtitle="Item Magico - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis tool takes the form of a wrench, a screwdriver, or another basic tool. As a XPHB action, you can touch the item and transform it into a type of XPHB of your choice. Whatever form the tool takes, you have proficiency with it when you use it.\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["feature.manipulate-elements.xphb2024.monk.elements.3"]={title="Manipulate Elements",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 106\n\nYou know the XPHB spell. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for it."},
  ["creature.manshoon.fraif2014"]={title="Manshoon",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 265\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 214 (33d8 + 66)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 23 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Infernal, Undercommon\n\nImunidades: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nManshoon has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nMisty Step\n\nProtective Magic\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nManshoon makes three Arcane Burst attacks. He can replace two attacks with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nm,r 11, reach 5 ft., or range 120 ft. h32 (4d12 + 6) Force damage."},
  ["creature.manshoon.wdh2014"]={title="Manshoon",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 126 (23d8 + 23)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 23 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Goblin, Infernal, Orc, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nManshoon wears a black robe of the archmagi and wields a staff of power (both accounted for in his statistics). Roll 2d10 to determine how many charges the staff has remaining.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nWhile wearing his robe of the archmagi, Manshoon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMetal Fist\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nStaff of Power\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage when used with two hands. Manshoon can expend 1 of the staff's charges to deal an extra 3 (1d6) force damage on a hit."},
  ["creature.manshoon-simulacrum.wdh2014"]={title="Manshoon Simulacrum",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 126 (23d8 + 23)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 23 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Goblin, Infernal, Orc, Undercommon\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMetal Fist\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.manticore.mm2014"]={title="Manticore",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 68 (8d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 50\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTail Spike Regrowth\n\nThe manticore has twenty-four tail spikes. Used spikes regrow when the manticore finishes a long rest.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe manticore makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws or three with its tail spikes.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nTail Spike\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 100/200 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.manticore.xmm2024"]={title="Manticore",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 202\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 68 (8d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 50\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe manticore makes three attacks, using Rend or Tail Spike in any combination.\n\nRend\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage.\n\nTail Spike\n\nr 5, range 100/200 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.manticore-heart-piercer.psa2014"]={title="Manticore, Heart-Piercer",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 136 (16d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe manticore makes two attacks, one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nStinger\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage. The target must make a 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 24 (7d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["psionic.mantle-of-awe.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mantle of Awe",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nYou learn to use psionic energy to manipulate others with a subtle combination of psi and your own, natural charm."},
  ["psionic.mantle-of-command.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mantle of Command",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nYou exert an aura of trust and authority, enhancing the coordination among your allies."},
  ["psionic.mantle-of-courage.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mantle of Courage",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nYou focus your mind on courage, radiating confidence and bravado to your allies."},
  ["psionic.mantle-of-fear.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mantle of Fear",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nYou tap into a well of primal fear and turn yourself into a beacon of terror to your enemies."},
  ["psionic.mantle-of-fury.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mantle of Fury",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nYou allow the primal fury lurking deep within your mind to burst forth, catching you and you allies in an implacable bloodthirst."},
  ["feature.mantle-of-inspiration.xge2024.bard.glamour.3"]={title="Mantle of Inspiration",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 14\n\nWhen you join the College of Glamour at 3rd level, you gain the ability to weave a song of fey magic that imbues your allies with vigor and speed.\n\nAs a bonus action, you can expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration to grant yourself a wondrous appearance. When you do so, choose a number of creatures you can see and that can see you within 60 feet of you, up to a number equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). Each of them gains 5 temporary hit points. When a creature gains these temporary hit points, it can immediately use its reaction to move up to its speed, without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nThe number of temporary hit points increases when you reach certain levels in this class, increasing to 8 at 5th level, 11 at 10th level, and 14 at 15th level."},
  ["feature.mantle-of-inspiration.xphb2024.bard.glamour.3"]={title="Mantle of Inspiration",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["psionic.mantle-of-joy.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mantle of Joy",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nYou tap into the joy within you, radiating it outward in soothing, psychic energy that brings hope and comfort to creatures around you."},
  ["feature.mantle-of-majesty.xge2024.bard.glamour.6"]={title="Mantle of Majesty",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 14\n\nAt 6th level, you gain the ability to cloak yourself in a fey magic that makes others want to serve you. As a bonus action, you cast command, without expending a spell slot, and you take on an appearance of unearthly beauty for 1 minute or until your concentration ends (as if you were concentration on a spell). During this time, you can cast command as a bonus action on each of your turns, without expending a spell slot.\n\nAny creature charmed by you automatically fails its saving throw against the command you cast with this feature.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.mantle-of-majesty.xphb2024.bard.glamour.6"]={title="Mantle of Majesty",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["magicitem.mantle-of-spell-resistance.dmg2014"]={title="Mantle of Spell Resistance",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against spells while you wear this cloak."},
  ["magicitem.mantle-of-spell-resistance.xdmg2024"]={title="Mantle of Spell Resistance",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 276\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou have XPHB on saving throws against spells while you wear this cloak."},
  ["feature.mantle-of-whispers.xge2024.bard.whispers.6"]={title="Mantle of Whispers",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.mantrap.toa2014"]={title="Mantrap",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 227\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 45 (7d10 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 2\n\nSentidos: tremorsense 30 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened, exhaustion, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAttractive Pollen (1/Day)\n\nWhen the mantrap detects any creatures nearby, it can use its reaction to release pollen out to a radius of 30 feet. Any beast or humanoid within the area must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or be forced to use all its movement on its turns to get as close to the the mantrap as possible. An affected target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the mantrap remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary tropical plant.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nEngulf\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller creature. hThe target is trapped inside the mantrap's leafy jaws. While trapped in this way, the target is blinded and restrained, has Cover from an attacks and other effects outside the mantrap, and takes 14 (4d6) acid damage at the start of each of the target's turns. If the mantrap dies, the creature inside it is no longer restrained by it. A mantrap can engulf only one creature at a time."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-bodily-health.dmg2014"]={title="Manual of Bodily Health",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains health and diet tips, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Constitution score increases by 2, as does your maximum for that score. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-bodily-health.xdmg2024"]={title="Manual of Bodily Health",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 277\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains health and diet tips, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-clay-golems.dmg2014"]={title="Manual of Clay Golems",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis tome contains information and incantations necessary to make a particular type of golem. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two 5th-level spell slots. A creature that can't use a manual of golems and attempts to read it takes 6d6 psychic damage.\n\nTo create a clay golem, you must spend 30 days, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay 65,000 gp to purchase supplies. Once you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the ashes of the manual are sprinkled on it. It is under your control, and it understands and obeys your spoken commands."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-clay-golems.xdmg2024"]={title="Manual of Clay Golems",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 277\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis tome contains information and incantations necessary to make a XMM. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two 5th-level spell slots. A creature that can't use a manual of golems and attempts to read it takes 6d6 psychic damage.\n\nTo create a clay golem, you must spend 30 days, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay 65,000 gp to purchase supplies.\n\nOnce you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the ashes of the manual are sprinkled on it. It is under your control, and it understands and obeys your spoken commands."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-flesh-golems.dmg2014"]={title="Manual of Flesh Golems",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis tome contains information and incantations necessary to make a particular type of golem. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two 5th-level spell slots. A creature that can't use a manual of golems and attempts to read it takes 6d6 psychic damage.\n\nTo create a flesh golem, you must spend 60 days, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay 50,000 gp to purchase supplies. Once you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the ashes of the manual are sprinkled on it. It is under your control, and it understands and obeys your spoken commands."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-flesh-golems.xdmg2024"]={title="Manual of Flesh Golems",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 277\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis tome contains information and incantations necessary to make a XMM. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two 5th-level spell slots. A creature that can't use a manual of golems and attempts to read it takes 6d6 psychic damage.\n\nTo create a flesh golem, you must spend 60 days, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay 50,000 gp to purchase supplies.\n\nOnce you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the ashes of the manual are sprinkled on it. It is under your control, and it understands and obeys your spoken commands."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-gainful-exercise.dmg2014"]={title="Manual of Gainful Exercise",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book describes fitness exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Strength score increases by 2, as does your maximum for that score. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-gainful-exercise.xdmg2024"]={title="Manual of Gainful Exercise",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 277\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book describes fitness exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Strength increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-iron-golems.dmg2014"]={title="Manual of Iron Golems",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis tome contains information and incantations necessary to make a particular type of golem. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two 5th-level spell slots. A creature that can't use a manual of golems and attempts to read it takes 6d6 psychic damage.\n\nTo create an iron golem, you must spend 120 days, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay 100,000 gp to purchase supplies. Once you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the ashes of the manual are sprinkled on it. It is under your control, and it understands and obeys your spoken commands."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-iron-golems.xdmg2024"]={title="Manual of Iron Golems",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 277\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis tome contains information and incantations necessary to make a XMM. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two 5th-level spell slots. A creature that can't use a manual of golems and attempts to read it takes 6d6 psychic damage.\n\nTo create an iron golem, you must spend 120 days, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay 100,000 gp to purchase supplies.\n\nOnce you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the ashes of the manual are sprinkled on it. It is under your control, and it understands and obeys your spoken commands."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-quickness-of-action.dmg2014"]={title="Manual of Quickness of Action",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 181\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains coordination and balance exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Dexterity score increases by 2, as does your maximum for that score. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-quickness-of-action.xdmg2024"]={title="Manual of Quickness of Action",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 278\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains coordination and balance exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Dexterity increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-stone-golems.dmg2014"]={title="Manual of Stone Golems",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis tome contains information and incantations necessary to make a particular type of golem. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two 5th-level spell slots. A creature that can't use a manual of golems and attempts to read it takes 6d6 psychic damage.\n\nTo create a stone golem, you must spend 90 days, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay 80,000 gp to purchase supplies. Once you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the ashes of the manual are sprinkled on it. It is under your control, and it understands and obeys your spoken commands."},
  ["magicitem.manual-of-stone-golems.xdmg2024"]={title="Manual of Stone Golems",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 277\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis tome contains information and incantations necessary to make a XMM. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two 5th-level spell slots. A creature that can't use a manual of golems and attempts to read it takes 6d6 psychic damage.\n\nTo create a stone golem, you must spend 90 days, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay 80,000 gp to purchase supplies.\n\nOnce you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the ashes of the manual are sprinkled on it. It is under your control, and it understands and obeys your spoken commands."},
  ["magicitem.many-keyholes-dagger.au2014"]={title="Many Keyholes Dagger",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 128\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias"},
  ["item.map.xphb2024"]={title="Map",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 227\n\nRaridade: none\n\nIf you consult an accurate Map, you gain a +5 bonus to Wisdom (XPHB) checks you make to find your way in the place represented on it."},
  ["item.map-or-scroll-case.phb2014"]={title="Map or Scroll Case",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis cylindrical leather case can hold up to ten rolled-up phb or five rolled-up phb."},
  ["item.map-or-scroll-case.xphb2024"]={title="Map or Scroll Case",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA XPHB holds up to 10 sheets of paper or 5 sheets of parchment."},
  ["feature.mapping-magic.efa2014.artificer.cartographer.3"]={title="Mapping Magic",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nIlluminated Cartography\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot, outlining the affected creatures as if in ink. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nPortal Jump\n\nOn your turn, you can spend an amount of movement equal to half your XPHB (round down) to teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of yourself or within 5 feet of a creature that is within 30 feet of you and holding one of your Adventurer's Atlas maps. You can't use this benefit if your XPHB is 0."},
  ["item.marble-font-with-gold-inlay-legion-of-dusk.psx2014"]={title="Marble font with gold inlay (Legion of Dusk)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.marfulb.rot2014"]={title="Marfulb",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 13"},
  ["creature.marid.mm2014"]={title="Marid",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 146\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 229 (17d10 + 136)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 90\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 12 | CON 26 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aquan\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe marid can breathe air and water.\n\nElemental Demise\n\nIf the marid dies, its body disintegrates into a burst of water and foam, leaving behind only equipment the marid was wearing or carrying.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe marid makes two trident attacks.\n\nTrident\n\nmw,rw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) piercing damage, or 15 (2d8 + 6) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nWater Jet\n\nThe marid magically shoots water in a 60-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, a target takes 21 (6d6) bludgeoning damage and, if it is Huge or smaller, is pushed up to 20 feet away from the marid and knocked prone. On a success, a target takes half the bludgeoning damage, but is neither pushed nor knocked prone."},
  ["creature.marid.xmm2024"]={title="Marid",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 203\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 229 (17d10 + 136)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 90\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 12 | CON 26 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Aquan)\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe marid can breathe air and water.\n\nElemental Restoration\n\nIf the marid dies outside the Elemental Plane of Water, its body dissolves into brine, and it gains a new body in 1d4 days, reviving with all its XPHB somewhere on the Plane of Water.\n\nWishes\n\nThe marid has a 30 percent chance of knowing the XPHB spell. If the marid knows it, the marid can cast it only on behalf of a non-genie creature who communicates a wish in a way the marid can understand. If the marid casts the spell for the creature, the marid suffers none of the spell's stress. Once the marid has cast it three times, the marid can't do so again for 365 days.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nMisty Veil {@recharge 5}\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe marid makes three Aquatic Lash attacks.\n\nAquatic Lash\n\nm 10, reach 15 ft. h15 (2d8 + 6) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Cold damage.\n\nWater Jet\n\ndex 18, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 10-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 31 (9d6) Cold damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is pushed up to 20 feet straight away from the marid and has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["feature.marid-s-surge.frhof2014.paladin.noble-genies.3"]={title="Marid's Surge",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nThe target of your Divine Smite and each creature of your choice in a 10-foot XPHB originating from you make a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, a creature is pushed 15 feet straight away from you and has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.marilith.mm2014"]={title="Marilith",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 189 (18d10 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 20 | CON 20 | INT 18 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe marilith has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe marilith's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nReactive\n\nThe marilith can take one reaction on every turn in combat.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe marilith can make seven attacks: six with its longswords and one with its tail.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h15 (2d10 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape 19). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, the marilith can automatically hit the target with its tail, and the marilith can't make tail attacks against other targets.\n\nTeleport\n\nThe marilith magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe marilith adds 5 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the marilith must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.marilith.xmm2024"]={title="Marilith",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 204\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 220 (21d10 + 105)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 20 | CON 20 | INT 18 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDemonic Restoration\n\nIf the marilith dies outside the Abyss, its body dissolves into ichor, and it gains a new body instantly, reviving with all its XPHB somewhere in the Abyss.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe marilith has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nReactive\n\nThe marilith can take one XPHB on every turn of combat.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe marilith makes six Pact Blade attacks and uses Constrict.\n\nPact Blade\n\nm 10, reach 5 ft. h10 (1d10 + 5) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage.\n\nConstrict\n\nstr 17, one Medium or smaller creature the marilith can see within 5 feet. actSaveFail 15 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. The target has the XPHB condition (escape 14), and it has the XPHB condition until the grapple ends.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTeleport {@recharge 5}\n\nThe marilith teleports up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nactTrigger The marilith is hit by a melee attack roll while holding a weapon. actResponse The marilith adds 5 to its AC against that attack, possibly causing it to miss."},
  ["background.marine.gos2014"]={title="Marine",subtitle="Background - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Steady\n\nYou can move twice the normal amount of time (up to 16 hours) each day before being subject to the effect of a forced march (see \"Travel Pace\" in chapter 8 of the Player's Handbook). Additionally, you can automatically find a safe route to land a boat on shore, provided such a route exists.\n\nHardship Endured\n\nHardship in your past has forged you into an unstoppable living weapon. This hardship is essential to you and is at the heart of a personal philosophy or ethos that often guides your actions. You can roll on the following table to determine this hardship or choose one that best fits your character.\n\nd6 | Hardship\n\n1 | Nearly Drowned. You hid underwater to avoid detection by enemies and held your breath for an extremely long time. Just before you would have died, you had a revelation about your existence.\n\n2 | Captured. You spent months enduring thirst, starvation, and torture at the hands of your enemy, but you never broke.\n\n3 | Sacrifice. You enabled the escape of your fellow soldiers, but at great cost to yourself. Some of your past comrades may think you're dead.\n\n4 | Juggernaut. No reasonable explanation can explain how you survived a particular battle. Every arrow and bolt missed you. You slew scores of enemies single-handedly and led your comrades to victory.\n\n5 | Stowaway. For days, you hid in the bilge of an enemy ship, surviving on brackish water and foolhardy rats. At the right moment, you crept up to the deck and took over the ship on your own.\n\n6 | Leave None Behind. You carried an injured marine for miles to avoid capture and death.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nMarines are looked up to by other soldiers and respected by their superiors. They are veteran warriors who rarely lose composure on the battlefield. Marines who leave the service tend to work as mercenaries, but their combat experience also makes them excellent adventurers. Though they are self-reliant, marines tend to operate best in groups, valuing camaraderie and the companionship of like-minded individuals.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I speak rarely but mean every word I say.\n\n2 | I laugh loudly and see the humor in stressful situations.\n\n3 | I prefer to solve problems without violence, but I finish fights decisively.\n\n4 | I enjoy being out in nature; poor weather never sours my mood.\n\n5 | I am dependable.\n\n6 | I am always working on some project or other.\n\n7 | I become cantankerous and quiet in the rain.\n\n8 | When the sea is within my sight, my mood is jovial and optimistic.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Teamwork. Success depends on cooperation and communication. (Good)\n\n2 | Code. The marines' code provides a solution for every problem, and following it is imperative. (Lawful)\n\n3 | Embracing. Life is messy. Throwing yourself into the worst of it is necessary to get the job done. (Chaotic)\n\n4 | Might. The strong train so that they might rule those who are weak. (Evil)\n\n5 | Bravery. To act when others quake in fear—this is the essence of the warrior. (Any)\n\n6 | Perseverance. No injury or obstacle can turn me from my goal. (Any)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | I face danger and evil to offset an unredeemable act in my past.\n\n2 | I. Will. Finish. The. Job.\n\n3 | I must set an example of hope for those who have given up.\n\n4 | I'm searching for a fellow marine captured by an elusive enemy.\n\n5 | Fear leads to tyranny, and both must be eradicated.\n\n6 | My commander betrayed my unit, and I will have revenge.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | I grow combative and unpredictable when I drink.\n\n2 | I find civilian life difficult and struggle to say the right thing in social situations.\n\n3 | My intensity can drive others away.\n\n4 | I hold grudges and have difficulty forgiving others.\n\n5 | I become irrational when innocent people are hurt.\n\n6 | I sometimes stay up all night listening to the ghosts of my fallen enemies."},
  ["creature.marisa.crcotn2014"]={title="Marisa",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["actionref.mark.dmg2014"]={title="Mark",subtitle="Acao - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 271\n\nThis option makes it easier for melee combatants to harry each other with opportunity attacks.\n\nWhen a creature makes a melee attack, it can also mark its target. Until the end of the attacker's next turn, any opportunity attack it makes against the marked target has advantage. The opportunity attack doesn't expend the attacker's reaction, but the attacker can't make the attack if anything, such as the incapacitated condition or the shocking grasp spell, is preventing it from taking reactions. The attacker is limited to one opportunity attack per turn."},
  ["feat.mark-of-detection.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Detection",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nDeductive Intuition\n\nWhen you make an Intelligence (XPHB) or Wisdom (XPHB) check, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nMagical Detection\n\nYou always have the XPHB and XPHB spells prepared. You can cast each spell once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast these spells using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this feat).\n\nWhen you reach character level 3, you also always have the XPHB spell prepared and can cast it the same way.\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Detection Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-finding.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Finding",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nHunter's Intuition\n\nWhen you make a Wisdom (XPHB or XPHB) check, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nFinder's Magic\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nWhen you reach character level 3, you also always have the XPHB spell prepared and can cast it the same way.\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Finding Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-handling.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Handling",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nWild Intuition\n\nWhen you make an Intelligence (XPHB) or Wisdom (XPHB) check, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nPrimal Connection\n\nYou always have the XPHB and XPHB spells prepared. You can cast each spell once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast these spells using any spell slots you have. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this feat).\n\nMonstrous Connections\n\nWhen you reach character level 3, you can target a Monstrosity when you cast XPHB or XPHB if the creature's Intelligence score is 3 or lower.\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Handling Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-healing.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Healing",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nMedical Intuition\n\nWhen you make a Wisdom (XPHB) check or an ability check using a XPHB, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nHealing Touch\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nWhen you reach character level 3, you also always have the XPHB spell prepared and can cast it the same way.\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Healing Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-hospitality.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Hospitality",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nEver Hospitable\n\nWhen you make a Charisma (XPHB) check or an ability check using XPHB or XPHB, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nInnkeeper's Magic\n\nYou always have the XPHB and XPHB spells prepared. You can cast each spell once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast these spells using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this feat).\n\nWhen you reach character level 3, you also always have the XPHB spell prepared and can cast it the same way.\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Hospitality Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-making.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Making",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nArtisan's Intuition\n\nWhen you make an Intelligence (XPHB) check or an ability check using XPHB, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nSpellsmith\n\nYou know the XPHB cantrip. You also always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this feat).\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Making Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-passage.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Passage",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 41\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCourier's Speed\n\nYour XPHB increases by 5 feet.\n\nIntuitive Motion\n\nWhen you make a Strength (XPHB) or Dexterity (XPHB) check, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nMagical Passage\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Passage Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-scribing.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Scribing",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 41\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nGifted Scribe\n\nWhen you make an Intelligence (XPHB) check or an ability check using XPHB, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nScribe's Insight\n\nYou know the XPHB cantrip. You also always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nWhen you reach character level 3, you also always have the XPHB spell prepared and can cast it the same way.\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Scribing Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-sentinel.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Sentinel",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 41\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nSentinel's Intuition\n\nWhen you make a Wisdom (XPHB or XPHB) check, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nGuardian's Shield\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nVigilant Guardian\n\nWhen a creature you can see within 5 feet of you is hit by an attack roll, you can take a XPHB to swap places with that creature, and you are hit by the attack instead. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your XPHB and regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Sentinel Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-shadow.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Shadow",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCunning Intuition\n\nWhen you make a Dexterity (XPHB) or Charisma (XPHB) check, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nShape Shadows\n\nYou know the XPHB cantrip. You also always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this feat).\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Shadow Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-storm.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Storm",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nWindwright's Intuition\n\nWhen you make a Dexterity (XPHB) check or an ability check using XPHB, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nStorm's Boon\n\nYou have XPHB to Lightning damage.\n\nStorm Magic\n\nYou know the XPHB cantrip. When you reach character level 3, you also always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this feat).\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Storm Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feat.mark-of-warding.efa2014"]={title="Mark of Warding",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nWarder's Intuition\n\nWhen you make an Intelligence (XPHB) check or an ability check using XPHB, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nWards and Seals\n\nYou always have the XPHB and XPHB spells prepared. You can cast each spell once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB.\n\nYou can also cast these spells using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this feat).\n\nWhen you reach character level 3, you also always have the XPHB spell prepared and can cast it the same way.\n\nSpells of the Mark\n\nIf you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature, the spells on the Mark of Warding Spells table are added to that feature's spell list.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["creature.markham-southwell.skt2014"]={title="Markham Southwell",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 248\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRoleplaying Information\n\nSheriff Markham of Bryn Shander is a brawny, likable man of few words. Nothing is more important to him than protecting Icewind Dale. He judges others by their actions, not their words.\n\nIdeal: \"All people deserve to be treated with dignity.\"\n\nBond: \"Duvessa is a natural leader, but she needs help. That's my job.\"\n\nFlaw: \"I bury my emotions and have no interest in small talk.\"\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMarkham makes two melee attacks.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage, or 7 (1d10 + 2) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 3 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h6 (1d10 + 1) piercing damage. Markham carries twenty crossbow bolts."},
  ["creature.markos-delphi.kftgv2014"]={title="Markos Delphi",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 53\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 44 (8d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 17 | WIS 13 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Deep Speech\n\nImunidades: psychic\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMarkos makes two Ceremonial Blade attacks, two Psychic Orb attacks, or one of each.\n\nCeremonial Blade\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) poison damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned for 1 minute. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nPsychic Orb\n\nrs 5 to hit, range 60 ft., one creature. h10 (2d6 + 3) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSwap Space\n\nMarkos targets one Medium or Small creature he can see within 30 feet of himself. The target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or it teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, exchanging positions with Markos."},
  ["creature.marlos-urnrayle.pota2014"]={title="Marlos Urnrayle",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 199\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 136 (16d8 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Terran\n\nResistencias: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEarthen Defeat\n\nWhen Marlos drops to 0 hit points, his body transforms into mud and collapses into a pool. Anything he is wearing or carrying is left behind.\n\nEarth Passage\n\nMarlos can move in difficult terrain composed of anything made from earth or stone as if it were normal terrain. He can move through solid earth and rock as if it were difficult terrain. If he ends his turn there, he is shunted into the nearest space he last occupied.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf Marlos fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nPetrifying Gaze\n\nWhen a creature that can see Marlos's eyes starts its turn within 30 feet of him, Marlos can force it to make a 14 Constitution saving throw if Marlos isn't incapacitated and can see the creature. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the creature is instantly petrified. Otherwise, a creature that fails the save begins to turn to stone and is restrained. The restrained creature must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn, becoming petrified on a failure or ending the effect on a success. The petrification lasts until the creature is freed by the greater restoration spell or other magic.\n\nUnless surprised, a creature can avert its eyes to avoid the saving throw at the start of its turn. If the creature does so, it can't see Marlos until the start of its next turn, when it can decide to avert its eyes again. If the creature looks at Marlos in the meantime, it must immediately make the save.\n\nIf Marlos sees himself reflected on a polished surface within 30 feet of him and in an area of bright light, Marlos is, due to his curse, affected by his own gaze.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMarlos makes three melee attacks, one with his snake hair and two with PotA.\n\nSnake Hair\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) poison damage.\n\nIronfang\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) thunder damage."},
  ["language.marquesian.egw2014"]={title="Marquesian",subtitle="Idioma - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nThe Menagerie Coast was settled by colonists from the arid land of Marquet, and their language now holds an unusual position in the Clovis Concord. It is the language of high society, as many Clovis elite are descended from Marquesians, but it is also the language of piracy, since countless lower-class Marquesians defected from the Concord and formed the Revelry pirates."},
  ["creature.marta-moonshadow.wdmm2014"]={title="Marta Moonshadow",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 46\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Dwarvish, Elvish, Undercommon"},
  ["deity.marthammor-duin.mtf2014"]={title="Marthammor Duin",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 73"},
  ["deity.marthammor-duin.scag2014"]={title="Marthammor Duin",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 22"},
  ["feat.martial-adept.phb2014"]={title="Martial Adept",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\nYou have martial training that allows you to perform special combat maneuvers. You gain the following benefits:\n\n• You learn two optionalfeatures of your choice from among those available to the phb archetype in the fighter class. If a maneuver you use requires your target to make a saving throw to resist the maneuver's effects, the saving throw DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice).\n\n• You gain one superiority die, which is a d6 (this die is added to any superiority dice you have from another source). This die is used to fuel your maneuvers. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain your expended superiority dice when you finish a short or long rest."},
  ["feature.martial-archetype.phb2014.fighter.base.3"]={title="Martial Archetype",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nAt 3rd level, you choose an archetype from the list available that you strive to emulate in your combat styles and techniques. The archetype you choose grants you features at 3rd level and again at 7th, 10th, 15th, and 18th level."},
  ["feature.martial-archetype-feature.phb2014.fighter.base.7"]={title="Martial Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nAt 7th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype."},
  ["feature.martial-archetype-feature.phb2014.fighter.base.10"]={title="Martial Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nAt 10th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype."},
  ["feature.martial-archetype-feature.phb2014.fighter.base.15"]={title="Martial Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nAt 15th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype."},
  ["feature.martial-archetype-feature.phb2014.fighter.base.18"]={title="Martial Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nAt 18th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype."},
  ["feature.martial-arts.phb2014.monk.base.1"]={title="Martial Arts",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.martial-arts.xphb2024.monk.base.1"]={title="Martial Arts",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.martial-arts-adept.mpmm2014"]={title="Martial Arts Adept",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 60 (11d8 + 11)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 17 | CON 13 | INT 11 | WIS 16 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnarmored Defense\n\nWhile the adept is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe adept makes three Unarmed Strike attacks or five Dart attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage. Once per turn, the adept can cause one of the following additional effects (choose one or roll a d4):\n\n• 1–2: Knock Down.\n\n• 3–4: Push.\n\nDart\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeflect Missile\n\nIn response to being hit by a ranged weapon attack, the adept deflects the missile. The damage it takes from the attack is reduced by 1d10 + 3. If the damage is reduced to 0, the adept catches the missile if it's small enough to hold in one hand and the adept has a hand free."},
  ["creature.martial-arts-adept.vgm2014"]={title="Martial Arts Adept",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 60 (11d8 + 11)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 17 | CON 13 | INT 11 | WIS 16 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnarmored Defense\n\nWhile the adept is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe adept makes three unarmed strikes or three dart attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, the adept can choose one of the following additional effects:\n\n• The target must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or drop one item it is holding (adept's choice).\n\n• The target must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n• The target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the end of the adept's next turn.\n\nDart\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeflect Missile\n\nIn response to being hit by a ranged weapon attack, the adept deflects the missile. The damage it takes from the attack is reduced by 1d10 + 3. If the damage is reduced to 0, the adept catches the missile if it's small enough to hold in one hand and the adept has a hand free."},
  ["feature.martial-arts-die.xphb2024.monk.base.1"]={title="Martial Arts Die",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 101\n\nYou can roll 1d6 in place of the normal damage of your XPHB or Monk weapons. This die changes as you gain Monk levels, as shown in the Martial Arts column of the Monk Features table."},
  ["feature.martial-role.tce2014.warrior-sidekick.base.1"]={title="Martial Role",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 146\n\n1st-level Warrior feature\n\nEach warrior focuses on offense or defense in their training. Choose one of the following options:\n\n• Attacker\n\n• Defender"},
  ["feature.martial-training.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.soul-knife.1"]={title="Martial Training",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\nAt 1st level, you gain proficiency with medium armor and martial weapons."},
  ["feature.martial-training.xphb2024.bard.valor.3"]={title="Martial Training",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.martial-versatility.tce2014.fighter.base.4"]={title="Martial Versatility",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 41\n\n{@i 4th-level fighter tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can do one of the following, as you shift the focus of your martial practice:\n\n• Replace a optionalfeatures you know with another fighting style available to fighters.\n\n• If you know any optionalfeatures from the phb archetype, you can replace one maneuver you know with a different maneuver."},
  ["feature.martial-versatility.tce2014.paladin.base.4"]={title="Martial Versatility",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 52\n\n{@i 4th-level paladin tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can replace a optionalfeatures you know with another fighting style available to paladins. This replacement represents a shift of focus in your martial practice."},
  ["feature.martial-versatility.tce2014.ranger.base.4"]={title="Martial Versatility",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\n{@i 4th-level ranger tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can replace a fighting style you know with another fighting style available to rangers. This replacement represents a shift of focus in your martial practice."},
  ["feat.martial-weapon-training.xphb2024"]={title="Martial Weapon Training",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 205\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nWeapon Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency with items."},
  ["magicitem.martialist-s-quarterstaff.au2014"]={title="Martialist's Quarterstaff",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 120\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis magic XPHB has 4 charges and regains 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn. It has the following additional properties.\n\nSearing Smite\n\nYou can expend 2 charges to cast the XPHB spell (13).\n\nThrow\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action, you can expend 1 charge to imbue the staff with magical velocity. Until the end of your next turn, the staff gains the XPHB property, with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet, and immediately after you make a ranged attack with the weapon, it flies back to your hand.\n\nTrip\n\nWhen you make a melee attack with this weapon, you can expend 1 charge to give yourself XPHB on the attack roll. If the attack hits, the target makes a 13 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, the target has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.marut.mpmm2014"]={title="Marut",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 432 (32d10 + 256)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 30\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 12 | CON 26 | INT 19 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all but rarely speaks\n\nResistencias: thunder\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe marut is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the marut fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe marut has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe marut doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nPlane Shift (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe marut makes two Unerring Slam attacks.\n\nUnerring Slam\n\nmw automatic hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h60 force damage, and the target is pushed up to 5 feet away from the marut if it is Huge or smaller.\n\nBlazing Edict {@recharge 5}\n\nArcane energy emanates from the marut's chest in a 60-foot cube. Every creature in that area takes 45 radiant damage. Each creature that takes any of this damage must succeed on a 20 Wisdom saving throw or be stunned until the end of the marut's next turn."},
  ["creature.marut.mtf2014"]={title="Marut",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 432 (32d10 + 256)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 30\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 12 | CON 26 | INT 19 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all but rarely speaks\n\nResistencias: thunder\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe marut is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the marut fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe marut has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe marut makes two slam attacks.\n\nUnerring Slam\n\nmw automatic hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h60 force damage, and the target is pushed up to 5 feet away from the marut if it is Huge or smaller.\n\nBlazing Edict {@recharge 5}\n\nArcane energy emanates from the marut's chest in a 60-foot cube. Every creature in that area takes 45 radiant damage. Each creature that takes any of this damage must succeed on a 20 Wisdom saving throw or be stunned until the end of the marut's next turn.\n\nJustify\n\nThe marut targets up to two creatures it can see within 60 feet of it. Each target must succeed on a 20 Charisma saving throw or be teleported to a teleportation circle in the Hall of Concordance in Sigil. A target fails automatically if it is incapacitated. If either target is teleported in this way, the marut teleports with it to the circle.\n\nAfter teleporting in this way, the marut can't use this action again until it finishes a short or long rest."},
  ["creature.mary-greymalkin.llk2014"]={title="Mary Greymalkin",subtitle="Criatura - LLK - 2014",body="Pagina: 41\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 10 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Celestial, Common, Elvish, Infernal, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nMary wears Bracers of Defense and a Ring of Protection, and carries a LLK\n\nFey Presence (Recharges after a Short Rest)\n\nMary can cause each creature within 10 feet of her to succeed on a 12 Wisdom saving throw or become charmed or frightened by her (Mary's choice) until the end of her next turn.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nMary has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put her to sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.marzena-belview.cos2014"]={title="Marzena Belview",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 40"},
  ["creature.maschin-i-bozorg.qftis2014"]={title="Maschin-i-Bozorg",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 207\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 94 (9d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 20 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Gnomish but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nOverheat\n\nWhen the maschin-i-bozorg is reduced to 0 hit points, its power source overloads, briefly superheating its outer shell. Each creature within 10 feet of the maschin-i-bozorg must make a 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe maschin-i-bozorg makes two Poison Jab attacks.\n\nPoison Jab\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h13 (4d4 + 3) piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or have the poisoned condition for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nSteam Jet {@recharge 5}\n\nThe maschin-i-bozorg emits scalding steam in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nCrushing Stride\n\nThe maschin-i-bozorg moves up to its speed in a straight line. During this movement, it can enter Medium and smaller creatures' spaces. A creature whose space the maschin-i-bozorg enters must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw. On a successful save, the creature is pushed to the nearest unoccupied space out of the maschin-i-bozorg's path. On a failed save, the creature takes 10 (3d6) bludgeoning damage and has the prone condition.\n\nIf the maschin-i-bozorg remains in the prone creature's space, the creature also has the restrained condition until it's no longer in the same space as the maschin-i-bozorg. While restrained in this way, the creature, or another creature within 5 feet of it, can use its action to make a 15 Strength (Athletics) check. On a successful check, the creature is shunted to an unoccupied space of its choice within 5 feet of the maschin-i-bozorg."},
  ["deity.mask.frhof2014"]={title="Mask",subtitle="Divindade - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\nMask is a trickster god, the patron of ne'er-do-wells, spies, and thieves. All that occurs within shadow is in the purview of Mask. People whisper a prayer to Mask whenever stealth is required or intrigue is afoot. Courtiers and diplomats invoke Mask's name in hope of a smooth negotiation.\n\nMask takes the form of a quick masculine being wielding two shadowy blades, his identity hidden by a mask. Sometimes he takes the form of masks that others might wear. When he speaks to his followers, he does so by claiming a mask as his temporary face, or he sends a living shadow (Neutral Evil XMM).\n\nThose who favor Mask practice thievery and try to acquire what belongs to others, engaging in pickpocketing, burglary, mugging, and con games. Ordinary folk pray to him so he'll avert his eyes from their valuables, but cautious individuals employ \"Mask's purse,\" a small, cheap cloth pouch worn in plain sight containing a small offering of coin. By convention, a pickpocket pilfers Mask's purse when encountering another person wearing one and considers it a gift from the god, while the one who lost the purse is grateful to Mask for accepting this respectful sacrifice. Of course, nothing prevents another pickpocket from targeting someone who has lost Mask's purse, and anyone with the ill luck to attract multiple pickpockets in a single outing has probably earned Mask's ire anyway.\n\nPriests of Mask are thieves by profession and serve as higher-ups in the local underworld or a criminal syndicate. They go by the title of demarche and wear veil-masks when acting in their priestly capacity.\n\nThe foremost organization serving Mask is the Shadowmasters of Telflamm, a criminal syndicate in the land of FRHoF. The Shadowmasters are based at Mask's largest temple, the House of Shadow, in Telflamm, but they also maintain safe houses throughout Thesk.\n\nChosen of Mask are master thieves, manipulative spies, and assassins who rarely walk in the light."},
  ["deity.mask.phb2014"]={title="Mask",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 294"},
  ["deity.mask.scag2014"]={title="Mask",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nMask is a trickster god, the patron of ne'er-do-wells, spies, and thieves. All that occurs within shadow is in the purview of Mask. People whisper a prayer to Mask whenever stealth is required or intrigue is afoot. Courtiers and diplomats invoke the god's name in hopes of a smooth negotiation.\n\nThose who favor Mask usually pursue thievery and other forms of acquisition of what belongs to others, such as pickpocketing, burglary, mugging, and con games. Ordinary folk pray to him to avert his eyes from their valuables, but the cautious sometimes employ \"Mask's purse,\" a small, cheap cloth pouch worn in plain sight (thus easily cut or lifted) containing a small offering of coin. By convention, a pickpocket pilfers Mask's purse when encountering another person wearing one, and considers the gain a gift from the god, while the one who lost the purse is grateful to the Lord of Shadows for accepting a respectful sacrifice of a small portion of his goods. Of course, nothing prevents another pickpocket from targeting someone who has lost Mask's purse, but anyone with the ill luck to attract multiple pickpockets in a single outing has probably earned Mask's ire anyway.\n\nPriests of Mask are usually thieves by profession, and often serve as higher-ups in the local underworld or criminal syndicate. They go by the title of demarche or demarchess, and wear veil-masks when acting in their priestly capacity."},
  ["magicitem.mask-of-changed-appearance.nf2014"]={title="Mask of Changed Appearance",subtitle="Item Magico - NF - 2014",body="Raridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis jeweled mask has 3 charges. As a XPHB action, you can expend 1 charge and change your face's appearance. You can't make yourself look like a different person, but you can smooth or deepen your wrinkles, whiten your teeth, hide or accentuate bags under your eyes, or perform other minor cosmetic changes. While your appearance is changed, the mask has the XPHB condition. Your changed appearance lasts 1 hour.\n\nRegaining Charges\n\nThe mask regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the mask explodes in a harmless cloud of sweet-swelling powder and is destroyed."},
  ["optionalfeature.mask-of-many-faces.phb2014"]={title="Mask of Many Faces",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nYou can cast disguise self at will, without expending a spell slot."},
  ["optionalfeature.mask-of-many-faces.xphb2024"]={title="Mask of Many Faces",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 156\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot."},
  ["magicitem.mask-of-the-beast.toa2014"]={title="Mask of the Beast",subtitle="Item Magico - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 207\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis wooden mask is shaped in the likeness of a beast's visage and has 3 charges. While wearing the mask you can expend 1 charge and use the mask to cast the animal friendship spell as an action. The mask regains all expended charges at dawn."},
  ["magicitem.mask-of-the-dragon-queen.rot2014"]={title="Mask of the Dragon Queen",subtitle="Item Magico - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nIndividually, the five dragon masks resemble the dragons they are named for. When two or more of the dragon masks are assembled, however, they transform magically into the Mask of the Dragon Queen. Each mask shrinks to become the modeled head of a chromatic dragon, appearing to roar its devotion to RoT where all the masks brought together are arranged crown-like on the wearer's head. Below the five masks, a new mask shapes itself, granting the wearer a draconic visage that covers the face, neck, and shoulders.\n\nWhile you are attuned to and wear this mask, you can have any of the properties from any one mask. Additionally, you gain the Damage Absorption from each of the five dragon masks, and you gain five uses of the Legendary Resistance property."},
  ["item.mason-s-tools.phb2014"]={title="Mason's Tools",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nMason's tools allow you to craft stone structures, including walls and buildings crafted from brick.\n\nComponents\n\nMason's tools consist of a trowel, a hammer, a chisel, brushes, and a square.\n\nHistory\n\nYour expertise aids you in identifying a stone building's date of construction and purpose, along with insight into who might have built it.\n\nInvestigation\n\nYou gain additional insight when inspecting areas within stone structures.\n\nPerception\n\nYou can spot irregularities in stone walls or floors, making it easier to find trap doors and secret passages.\n\nDemolition\n\nYour knowledge of masonry allows you to spot weak points in brick walls. You deal double damage to such structures with your weapon attacks.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nChisel a small hole in a stone wall | 10\n\nFind a weak point in a stone wall | 15"},
  ["item.mason-s-tools.xphb2024"]={title="Mason's Tools",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Strength\n\n• Utilize: Chisel a symbol or hole in stone (10)\n\n• Craft: XPHB"},
  ["magicitem.masque-charm.scc2014"]={title="Masque Charm",subtitle="Item Magico - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nA masque charm is a small silver pin. While wearing this charm, you can use an action to cast the disguise self spell (13 to discern the disguise). Once the spell is cast, it can't be cast from the charm again until the next sunset. When casting the spell, you can have the spell last for its normal 1 hour duration or for 6 hours. If you choose the 6-hour duration, the charm becomes nonmagical when the spell ends. In either case, the spell ends if the charm is removed from you."},
  ["magicitem.masquerade-tattoo.tce2014"]={title="Masquerade Tattoo",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 131\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nProduced by a special needle, this magic tattoo appears on your body as whatever you desire.\n\nTattoo Attunement\n\nTo attune to this item, you hold the needle to your skin where you want the tattoo to appear, pressing the needle there throughout the attunement process. When the attunement is complete, the needle turns into the ink that becomes the tattoo, which appears on the skin.\n\nIf your attunement to the tattoo ends, the tattoo vanishes, and the needle reappears in your space.\n\nFluid Ink\n\nAs a bonus action, you can shape the tattoo into any color or pattern and move it to any area of your skin. Whatever form it takes, it is always obviously a tattoo. It can range in size from no smaller than a copper piece to an intricate work of art that covers all your skin.\n\nDisguise Self\n\nAs an action, you can use the tattoo to cast the disguise self spell (13 to discern the disguise). Once the spell is cast from the tattoo, it can't be cast from the tattoo again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.masquerader-s-brooch.aud2014"]={title="Masquerader's Brooch",subtitle="Item Magico - AUD - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA Masquerader's Brooch comes in various shapes and sizes but always looks slightly tarnished.\n\nYou gain the following benefits while wearing the brooch.\n\nIllusory Fashion\n\nAs a XPHB while wearing or holding the brooch, you can project a magical illusion over your clothing, armor, weapons, equipment, and other belongings on your person. The illusion lasts for 1 hour and ends early if the brooch is removed. Each time you use this benefit, you determine the extent and nature of the illusion. It could be as minor as changing the color of your garments or as extensive as making a suit of armor appear as an evening gown and a sheathed weapon appear as a satin sash.\n\nThe changes wrought by this illusion fail to hold up to physical inspection. A creature that takes the XPHB action to examine your appearance discerns the illusion with a successful 13 Intelligence (XPHB) check.\n\nShifting Guise\n\nAs a XPHB action while wearing or holding the brooch, you can cast XPHB from it (Change Appearance option only; no XPHB required)."},
  ["spell.mass-cure-wounds.phb2014"]={title="Mass Cure Wounds",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nA wave of healing energy washes out from a point of your choice within range. Choose up to six creatures in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on that point. Each target regains hit points equal to 3d8 + your spellcasting ability modifier. This spell has no effect on undead or constructs."},
  ["spell.mass-cure-wounds.xphb2024"]={title="Mass Cure Wounds",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 296\n\nA wave of healing energy washes out from a point you can see within range. Choose up to six creatures in a 30-foot-radius XPHB centered on that point. Each target regains XPHB equal to 5d8 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."},
  ["spell.mass-heal.phb2014"]={title="Mass Heal",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 9 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nA flood of healing energy flows from you into injured creatures around you. You restore up to 700 hit points, divided as you choose among any number of creatures that you can see within range. Creatures healed by this spell are also cured of all diseases and any effect making them blinded or deafened. This spell has no effect on undead or constructs."},
  ["spell.mass-heal.xphb2024"]={title="Mass Heal",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 9 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 296\n\nA flood of healing energy flows from you into creatures around you. You restore up to 700 XPHB, divided as you choose among any number of creatures that you can see within range. Creatures healed by this spell also have the XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB conditions removed from them."},
  ["spell.mass-healing-word.phb2014"]={title="Mass Healing Word",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nAs you call out words of restoration, up to six creatures of your choice that you can see within range regain hit points equal to 1d4 + your spellcasting ability modifier. This spell has no effect on undead or constructs."},
  ["spell.mass-healing-word.xphb2024"]={title="Mass Healing Word",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 296\n\nUp to six creatures of your choice that you can see within range regain XPHB equal to 2d4 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."},
  ["spell.mass-polymorph.xge2024"]={title="Mass Polymorph",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 9 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 160\n\nYou transform up to ten creatures of your choice that you can see within range. An unwilling target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw to resist the transformation. An unwilling shapechanger automatically succeeds on the save.\n\nEach target assumes a beast form of your choice, and you can choose the same form or different ones for each target. The new form can be bestiary you have seen whose challenge rating is equal to or less than the target's (or half the target's level, if the target doesn't have a challenge rating). The target's game statistics, including mental ability scores, are replaced by the statistics of the chosen beast, but the target retains its hit points, alignment, and personality.\n\nEach target gains a number of temporary hit points equal to the hit points of its new form. These temporary hit points can't be replaced by temporary hit points from another source. A target reverts to its normal form when it has no more temporary hit points or it dies. If the spell ends before then, the creature loses all its temporary hit points and reverts to its normal form.\n\nThe creature is limited in the actions it can perform by the nature of its new form. It can't speak, cast spells, or do anything else that requires hands or speech.\n\nThe target's gear melds into the new form. The target can't activate, use, wield, or otherwise benefit from any of its equipment."},
  ["spell.mass-suggestion.phb2014"]={title="Mass Suggestion",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nYou suggest a course of activity (limited to a sentence or two) and magically influence up to twelve creatures of your choice that you can see within range and that can hear and understand you. Creatures that can't be charmed are immune to this effect. The suggestion must be worded in such a manner as to make the course of action sound reasonable. Asking the creature to stab itself, throw itself onto a spear, immolate itself, or do some other obviously harmful act automatically negates the effect of the spell.\n\nEach target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it pursues the course of action you described to the best of its ability. The suggested course of action can continue for the entire duration. If the suggested activity can be completed in a shorter time, the spell ends when the subject finishes what it was asked to do.\n\nYou can also specify conditions that will trigger a special activity during the duration. For example, you might suggest that a group of soldiers give all their money to the first beggar they meet. If the condition isn't met before the spell ends, the activity isn't performed.\n\nIf you or any of your companions damage a creature affected by this spell, the spell ends for that creature."},
  ["spell.mass-suggestion.xphb2024"]={title="Mass Suggestion",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 296\n\nYou suggest a course of activity—described in no more than 25 words—to twelve or fewer creatures you can see within range that can hear and understand you. The suggestion must sound achievable and not involve anything that would obviously deal damage to any of the targets or their allies. For example, you could say, \"Walk to the village down that road, and help the villagers there harvest crops until sunset.\" Or you could say, \"Now is not the time for violence. Drop your weapons, and dance! Stop in an hour.\"\n\nEach target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition for the duration or until you or your allies deal damage to the target. Each XPHB target pursues the suggestion to the best of its ability. The suggested activity can continue for the entire duration, but if the suggested activity can be completed in a shorter time, the spell ends for a target upon completing it."},
  ["feature.master-duelist.xge2024.rogue.swashbuckler.17"]={title="Master Duelist",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 48\n\nBeginning at 17th level, your mastery of the blade lets you turn failure into success in combat. If you miss with an attack roll, you can roll it again with advantage. Once you do so, you can't use this feature again until you finish a short or long rest."},
  ["creature.master-of-cruelties.ggr2014"]={title="Master of Cruelties",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 196\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 127 (15d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 19 | WIS 16 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Blood Lust\n\nWhen any other creature starts its turn within 30 feet of the master, that creature must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw, or it must immediately take the Attack action, making one melee attack against a random creature within reach. If no creatures are within reach, it makes a ranged attack against a random creature within range, throwing its weapon if necessary.\n\nFeed on the Crowd\n\nWhenever a creature within 60 feet of the master dies, the master gains 15 temporary hit points and has advantage on all attack rolls, ability checks, and saving throws until the end of its next turn.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe master has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe master makes two melee attacks with its spear.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack, plus 13 (3d8) psychic damage.\n\nCaptivating Presence {@recharge}\n\nEach creature within 120 feet of the master must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by the master for 1 hour. While charmed in this way, a creature's speed is 0. If the charmed creature takes damage, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. A target that succeeds on the saving throw is immune to the Captivating Presence of all masters of cruelties for the next 24 hours."},
  ["feature.master-of-hexes.xge2024.warlock.hexblade.14"]={title="Master of Hexes",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 55\n\nStarting at 14th level, you can spread your Hexblade's Curse from a slain creature to another creature. When the creature cursed by your Hexblade's Curse dies, you can apply the curse to a different creature you can see within 30 feet of you, provided you aren't incapacitated. When you apply the curse in this way, you don't regain hit points from the death of the previously cursed creature."},
  ["feature.master-of-intrigue.xge2024.rogue.mastermind.3"]={title="Master of Intrigue",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.master-of-myriad-forms.phb2014"]={title="Master of Myriad Forms",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nYou can cast alter self at will, without expending a spell slot."},
  ["optionalfeature.master-of-myriad-forms.xphb2024"]={title="Master of Myriad Forms",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 156\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot."},
  ["feature.master-of-nature.phb2014.cleric.nature.17"]={title="Master of Nature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\nAt 17th level, you gain the ability to command animals and plant creatures. While creatures are charmed by your Charm Animals and Plants feature, you can take a bonus action on your turn to verbally command what each of those creatures will do on its next turn."},
  ["feature.master-of-runes.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.15"]={title="Master of Runes",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n15th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou can invoke each rune you know from your Rune Carver feature twice, rather than once, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest."},
  ["creature.master-of-souls.bgdia2014"]={title="Master of Souls",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 19 | WIS 14 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGrave Magic\n\nWhen the master of souls cast a spell that deals damage, it can change the spell's damage type to necrotic.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe master of souls attacks twice with its flail.\n\nSilvered Skull Flail\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d8) bludgeoning damage plus 14 (4d6) necrotic damage, and the target has disadvantage on all saving throws until the end of the master of souls' next turn.\n\nChill Touch (Cantrip)\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature. h13 (2d8) necrotic damage, and the target can't regain hit points until the start of the master of souls' next turn. If the target is undead, it has disadvantage on attack rolls against the master of souls for the same duration.\n\nRay of Sickness (1st-Level Spell; Requires a Spell Slot)\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 60 ft., one creature. h9 (2d8) poison damage, and the target must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the end of the master of souls' next turn. If the master of souls casts this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, the damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 1st.\n\nScorching Ray (2nd-Level Spell; Requires a Spell Slot)\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 120 ft., one target per ray (3 rays if a 2nd-level spell slot is used, 4 rays if a 3rd-level spell slot is used). h7 (2d6) fire damage per ray."},
  ["feature.master-of-tactics.xge2024.rogue.mastermind.3"]={title="Master of Tactics",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.master-refrum.gos2014"]={title="Master Refrum",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.master-sage.cm2014"]={title="Master Sage",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 54 (12d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 20 | WIS 18 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any five languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShocking Grasp (Cantrip)\n\nms 8 to hit (with advantage if the target is wearing armor made of metal), reach 5 ft., one creature. h13 (3d8) lightning damage, and the target can't take reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\nLightning Eruption (3/Day)\n\nThe sage creates an eruption of magical lightning centered on a point it can see within 150 feet of it. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nShield (1st-Level Spell; 3/Day)\n\nWhen the sage is hit by an attack or targeted by a magic missile spell, it calls forth an invisible barrier of magical force that protects it. Until the start of its next turn, the sage has a +5 bonus to AC, including against the triggering attack, and it takes no damage from magic missile."},
  ["feature.master-scrivener.tce2014.wizard.scribes.10"]={title="Master Scrivener",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 78\n\n10th-level Order of Scribes feature\n\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can create one magic scroll by touching your Wizardly Quill to a blank piece of paper or parchment and causing one spell from your Awakened Spellbook to be copied onto the scroll. The spellbook must be within 5 feet of you when you make the scroll.\n\nThe chosen spell must be of 1st or 2nd level and must have a casting time of 1 action. Once in the scroll, the spell's power is enhanced, counting as one level higher than normal. You can cast the spell from the scroll by reading it as an action. The scroll is unintelligible to anyone else, and the spell vanishes from the scroll when you cast it or when you finish your next long rest.\n\nYou are also adept at crafting spell scrolls, which are described in the treasure chapter of the Dungeon Master's Guide. The gold and time you must spend to make such a scroll are halved if you use your Wizardly Quill."},
  ["creature.master-thief.mpmm2014"]={title="Master Thief",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 174\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 84 (13d8 + 26)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common) plus thieves' cant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEvasion\n\nIf the thief is subjected to an effect that allows it to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, the thief instead takes no damage if it succeeds on the saving throw and only half damage if it fails, provided the thief isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thief makes three Shortsword or Shortbow attacks.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) poison damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nCunning Action\n\nThe thief takes the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nThe thief halves the damage that it takes from an attack that hits it. The thief must be able to see the attacker."},
  ["creature.master-thief.vgm2014"]={title="Master Thief",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 83 (13d8 + 26)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common) plus Thieves' cant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCunning Action\n\nOn each of its turns, the thief can use a bonus action to take the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action.\n\nEvasion\n\nIf the thief is subjected to an effect that allows it to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, the thief instead takes no damage if it succeeds on the saving throw, and only half damage if it fails.\n\nSneak Attack (1/Turn)\n\nThe thief deals an extra 14 (4d6) damage when it hits a target with a weapon attack and has advantage on the attack roll, or when the target is within 5 feet of an ally of the thief that isn't incapacitated and the thief doesn't have disadvantage on the attack roll.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thief makes three attacks with its shortsword.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nLight Crossbow\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nThe thief halves the damage that it takes from an attack that hits it. The thief must be able to see the attacker."},
  ["feature.master-transmuter.au2014.wizard.transmuter.14"]={title="Master Transmuter",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.master-transmuter.phb2014.wizard.transmutation.14"]={title="Master Transmuter",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nStarting at 14th level, you can use your action to consume the reserve of transmutation magic stored within your transmuter's stone in a single burst. When you do so, choose one of the following effects. Your transmuter's stone is destroyed and can't be remade until you finish a long rest.\n\nMajor Transformation\n\nYou can transmute one nonmagical object—no larger than a 5-foot cube—into another nonmagical object of similar size and mass and of equal or lesser value. You must spend 10 minutes handling the object to transform it.\n\nPanacea\n\nYou remove all curses, diseases, and poisons affecting a creature that you touch with the transmuter's stone. The creature also regains all its hit points.\n\nRestore Life\n\nYou cast the raise dead spell on a creature you touch with the transmuter's stone, without expending a spell slot or needing to have the spell in your spellbook.\n\nRestore Youth\n\nYou touch the transmuter's stone to a willing creature, and that creature's apparent age is reduced by 3d10 years, to a minimum of 13 years. This effect doesn't extend the creature's lifespan."},
  ["magicitem.master-s-amulet.mm2014"]={title="Master's Amulet",subtitle="Item Magico - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 271\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nEvery shield guardian has an amulet magically linked to it. A shield guardian can have only one corresponding amulet, and if that amulet is destroyed, the shield guardian is incapacitated until a replacement amulet is created. A shield guardian's amulet is subject to direct attack if it isn't being worn or carried. It has AC 10, 10 hit points, and immunity to poison and psychic damage. Crafting an amulet requires 1 week and costs 1,000 gp in components.\n\nA shield guardian's solitary focus is to protect the amulet's wearer. The amulet's wearer can command the guardian to attack its enemies or to guard the wielder against attack. If an attack threatens to injure the wearer, the construct can magically absorb the blow into its own body, even at a distance.\n\nA spellcaster can store a single spell within a shield guardian, which can then cast the spell on command or under specific conditions. Many a wizard has been rendered helpless by enemies, only to surprise those foes when its shield guardian unleashes potent magical power."},
  ["feature.master-s-flourish.xge2024.bard.swords.14"]={title="Master's Flourish",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 15\n\nStarting at 14th level, whenever you use a Blade Flourish option, you can roll a d6 and use it instead of expending a Bardic Inspiration die."},
  ["feature.masterful-shots.au2014.fighter.arcane-archer.18"]={title="Masterful Shots",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.mastermind.xge2024.rogue.mastermind.0"]={title="Mastermind",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Master of Intrigue\n\nPagina: 46\n\nWhen you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain proficiency with the phb, the phb, and one PHB of your choice. You also learn two languages of your choice.\n\nAdditionally, you can unerringly mimic the speech patterns and accent of a creature that you hear speak for at least 1 minute, enabling you to pass yourself off as a native speaker of a particular land, provided that you know the language.\n\nNivel 3 - Master of Intrigue\n\nNivel 3 - Master of Tactics\n\nPagina: 46\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you can use the Help action as a bonus action. Additionally, when you use the Help action to aid an ally in attacking a creature, the target of that attack can be within 30 feet of you, rather than within 5 feet of you, if the target can see or hear you.\n\nNivel 3 - Master of Tactics\n\nNivel 3 - Mastermind\n\nPagina: 46\n\nYour focus is on people and on the influence and secrets they have. Many spies, courtiers, and schemers follow this archetype, leading lives of intrigue. Words are your weapons as often as knives or poison, and secrets and favors are some of your favorite treasures.\n\nNivel 9 - Insightful Manipulator\n\nPagina: 46\n\nStarting at 9th level, if you spend at least 1 minute observing or interacting with another creature outside combat, you can learn certain information about its capabilities compared to your own. The DM tells you if the creature is your equal, superior, or inferior in regard to two of the following characteristics of your choice:\n\n• Intelligence score\n\n• Wisdom score\n\n• Charisma score\n\n• Class levels (if any)\n\nAt the DM's option, you might also realize you know a piece of the creature's history or one of its personality traits, if it has any.\n\nNivel 13 - Misdirection\n\nPagina: 46\n\nBeginning at 13th level, you can sometimes cause another creature to suffer an attack meant for you. When you are targeted by an attack while a creature within 5 feet of you is granting you cover against that attack, you can use your reaction to have the attack target that creature instead of you.\n\nNivel 17 - Soul of Deceit\n\nPagina: 46\n\nStarting at 17th level, your thoughts can't be read by telepathy or other means, unless you allow it. You can present false thoughts by succeeding on a Charisma (Deception) check contested by the mind reader's Wisdom (Insight) check.\n\nAdditionally, no matter what you say, magic that would determine if you are telling the truth indicates you are being truthful if you so choose, and you can't be compelled to tell the truth by magic."},
  ["feature.mastermind.xge2024.rogue.mastermind.3"]={title="Mastermind",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 46\n\nYour focus is on people and on the influence and secrets they have. Many spies, courtiers, and schemers follow this archetype, leading lives of intrigue. Words are your weapons as often as knives or poison, and secrets and favors are some of your favorite treasures."},
  ["item.masterpiece-painting-in-mahogany-frame-with-gold-inlay-legion-of-dusk.psx2014"]={title="Masterpiece painting in mahogany frame with gold inlay (Legion of Dusk)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["psionic.mastery-of-air.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mastery of Air",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nYou become one with the power of elemental air."},
  ["feature.mastery-of-death.scag2014.monk.long-death.11"]={title="Mastery of Death",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\nBeginning at 11th level, you use your familiarity with death to escape its grasp. When you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can expend 1 ki point (no action required) to have 1 hit point instead."},
  ["psionic.mastery-of-fire.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mastery of Fire",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nYou align your mind with the energy of elemental fire."},
  ["psionic.mastery-of-force.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mastery of Force",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 18\n\nAs a student of psionic power, you perceive the potential energy that flows through all things. You reach out with your mind, transforming the potential into the actual. Objects and creatures move at your command."},
  ["psionic.mastery-of-ice.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mastery of Ice",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nYou master the power of ice, shaping it to meet you demands."},
  ["psionic.mastery-of-light-and-darkness.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mastery of Light and Darkness",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nYou claim dominion over light and darkness with your mind."},
  ["psionic.mastery-of-water.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mastery of Water",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nYour mind becomes one with elemental water, attuning your thoughts to its ebb and flow."},
  ["psionic.mastery-of-weather.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mastery of Weather",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nYour mind reaches into the sky, reshaping the stuff of storms to serve your needs."},
  ["psionic.mastery-of-wood-and-earth.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Mastery of Wood and Earth",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nYou attune your mind to seize control of wood and earth."},
  ["creature.mastiff.mm2014"]={title="Mastiff",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 332\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 5 (1d8 + 1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe mastiff has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 11 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["item.mastiff.phb2014"]={title="Mastiff",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.mastiff.xmm2024"]={title="Mastiff",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 365\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 5 (1d8 + 1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition."},
  ["item.mastiff.xphb2024"]={title="Mastiff",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.mastix-whip-of-erebos.mot2014"]={title="Mastix, Whip of Erebos",subtitle="Item Magico - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nErebos wields Mastix, a whip capable of extending like an impossibly long shadow. In the hands of the god of the dead, the whip snares the reluctant dead and drags them into his realm. When Erebos grants his weapon to a mortal follower, it's typically to reclaim a powerful soul or to humiliate Heliod.\n\nWhip of the Dead\n\nErebos's whip seethes with the enervating energy of the Underworld. This magic whip grants a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. When you hit with an attack using this whip, the target takes an extra 2d8 necrotic damage and you regain hit points equal to half the amount of necrotic damage dealt.\n\nAdditionally, when you make an attack with the whip on your turn, you can increase the range of the attack to 300 feet. This property of the weapon can't be used again until the next dusk.\n\nBlessing of the Dead\n\nIf you are a worshiper of Erebos, you gain all the following benefits for which you have the required piety:\n\n• Piety 1+\n\n• Piety 25+\n\n• Piety 50+\n\nIf you aren't a worshiper of Erebos, the whip has 2 randomly determined dmg properties.\n\nSee \"Artifacts\" in chapter 7 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for details on randomly determined properties.\n\nErebos's Claim\n\nWhile carrying the whip, you can use an action to cast either circle of death or dominate monster (targeting only undead) from the whip. The save DC for these spells is 18. Once you use the whip to cast a spell, that spell can't be cast from it again until the next dusk.\n\nDestroying the Whip\n\nTo destroy the whip, it must be taken to the heights of Mount Hiastos in Nyx, unraveled by a Returned, and left to bask in continual daylight for one month."},
  ["magicitem.matalotok.bgdia2014"]={title="Matalotok",subtitle="Item Magico - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nMatalotok, the Frost Father, is an ancient hammer fashioned by Thrym, the god of frost giants. The favored weapon of the demon lord BGDIA, Matalotok is frigid to the touch and wreathed in mist.\n\nYou are immune to cold damage while holding Matalotok. Whenever it deals damage to a creature, the hammer radiates a burst of intense cold in a 30-foot-radius sphere. Each creature in that area takes 10 (3d6) cold damage."},
  ["item.matchless-pipe.wdh2014"]={title="Matchless Pipe",subtitle="Item - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 47\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nA switch made of flint is built into the bowl of this fine wooden smoking pipe. With a few flicks of the switch, the pipe lights itself."},
  ["deity.math-mathonwy.phb2014"]={title="Math Mathonwy",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["creature.mattrim-threestrings-mereg.wdh2014"]={title="Mattrim \"Threestrings\" Mereg",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.maude.nrh-at2014"]={title="Maude",subtitle="Criatura - NRH-AT - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.maul.phb2014"]={title="Maul",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.maul.xphb2024"]={title="Maul",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.maurezhi.mpmm2014"]={title="Maurezhi",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 175\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 88 (16d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 17 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Elvish, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAssume Form\n\nThe maurezhi can assume the appearance of any Medium Humanoid it eats. It remains in this form for 1d6 days, during which time the form gradually decays until, when the effect ends, the form sloughs from the demon's body.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe maurezhi has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe maurezhi makes one Bite attack and one Claw attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d10 + 3) piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, its Charisma score is reduced by 1d4. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a short or long rest. The target dies if this reduces its Charisma to 0. It rises 24 hours later as a ghoul  unless it has been revived or its corpse has been destroyed.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) slashing damage. If the target is a creature other than an Undead, it must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nRaise Ghoul {@recharge 5}\n\nThe maurezhi targets one dead ghoul or ghast it can see within 30 feet of it. The target is revived with all its hit points."},
  ["creature.maurezhi.mtf2014"]={title="Maurezhi",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 133\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 88 (16d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 17 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Elvish, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAssume Form\n\nThe maurezhi can assume the appearance of any Medium humanoid it has eaten. It remains in this form for 1d6 days, during which time the form gradually decays until, when the effect ends, the form sloughs from the demon's body.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe maurezhi has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe maurezhi makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d10 + 3) piercing damage. If the target is a humanoid, its Charisma score is reduced by 1d4. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a short or long rest. The target dies if this reduces its Charisma to 0. It rises 24 hours later as a ghoul, unless it has been revived or its corpse has been destroyed.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) slashing damage. If the target is a creature other than an undead, it must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nRaise Ghoul {@recharge 5}\n\nThe maurezhi targets one dead ghoul or ghast it can see within 30 feet of it. The target is revived with all its hit points."},
  ["creature.maw-demon.mpmm2014"]={title="Maw Demon",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 176\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 8 | CON 13 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nDisgorge {@recharge}\n\nThe demon vomits in a 15-foot cube. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 11 Dexterity saving throw or take 11 (2d10) acid damage and fall prone in the spew."},
  ["creature.maw-demon.vgm2014"]={title="Maw Demon",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 137\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 8 | CON 13 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRampage\n\nWhen it reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the maw demon can take a bonus action to move up to half its speed and make a bite attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.maw-of-sekolah.gos2014"]={title="Maw of Sekolah",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 244\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 114 (12d12 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, swim: 50\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 14 | CHA 7\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin, telepathy 100 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf the maw of Sekolah fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nWater Breathing\n\nThe maw of Sekolah can breathe only underwater.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe maw of Sekolah makes one attack with its bite and one attack with its tail smash.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nTail Smash\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe maw of Sekolah makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nSpeed of Sekolah\n\nThe maw of Sekolah moves up to its speed.\n\nFeed (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe ferocious spirit of Sekolah flashes through the water, tearing through the foes of the maw of Sekolah. Each creature of the maw's choosing within 60 feet of it must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) slashing damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.maw-of-yeenoghu.bgg2014"]={title="Maw of Yeenoghu",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 159\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / H\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 161 (14d12 + 70)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Giant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe maw has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe maw makes two Bite or Fang Fling attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (2d12 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nFang Fling\n\nrw 10 to hit, range 30/90 ft., one target. h11 (1d10 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nGorging Charge {@recharge 5}\n\nThe maw moves up to its speed without provoking opportunity attacks and can move through the spaces of Large or smaller creatures. Each time the maw enters a creature's space for the first time during this move, that creature must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or take 25 (3d12 + 6) piercing damage and have the grappled condition (escape 16); if a creature is already grappled this way, it has the prone condition. Until this grapple ends, the target has the restrained condition. The maw can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFanged Rebuke\n\nIn response to taking damage, the maw makes one Bite attack against a random creature within 10 feet of itself. If no creature is within reach, the maw can make two Fang Fling attacks."},
  ["creature.maxeene.wdh2014"]={title="Maxeene",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 19 (3d10 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 7\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHooves\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["spell.maximilian-s-earthen-grasp.xge2024"]={title="Maximilian's Earthen Grasp",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 161\n\nYou choose a 5-foot-square unoccupied space on the ground that you can see within range. A Medium hand made from compacted soil rises there and reaches for one creature you can see within 5 feet of it. The target must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage and is restrained for the spell's duration.\n\nAs an action, you can cause the hand to crush the restrained target, which must make a Strength saving throw. The target takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nTo break out, the restrained target can use its action to make a Strength check against your spell save DC. On a success, the target escapes and is no longer restrained by the hand.\n\nAs an action, you can cause the hand to reach for a different creature or to move to a different unoccupied space within range. The hand releases a restrained target if you do either."},
  ["spell.maze.phb2014"]={title="Maze",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nYou banish a creature that you can see within range into a labyrinthine demiplane. The target remains there for the duration or until it escapes the maze.\n\nThe target can use its action to attempt to escape. When it does so, it makes a 20 Intelligence check. If it succeeds, it escapes, and the spell ends (a minotaur or goristro demon automatically succeeds).\n\nWhen the spell ends, the target reappears in the space it left or, if that space is occupied, in the nearest unoccupied space."},
  ["spell.maze.xphb2024"]={title="Maze",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 296\n\nYou banish a creature that you can see within range into a labyrinthine demiplane. The target remains there for the duration or until it escapes the maze.\n\nThe target can take a XPHB action to try to escape. When it does so, it makes a 20 Intelligence (XPHB) check. If it succeeds, it escapes, and the spell ends.\n\nWhen the spell ends, the target reappears in the space it left or, if that space is occupied, in the nearest unoccupied space."},
  ["creature.meazel.mpmm2014"]={title="Meazel",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 177\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 35 (10d8 - 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 17 | CON 9 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGarrote\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target of the meazel's size or smaller. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 13 with disadvantage). Until the grapple ends, the target takes 10 (2d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage at the start of each of the meazel's turns. The meazel can't make weapon attacks while grappling a creature in this way.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) necrotic damage.\n\nShadow Teleport {@recharge 5}\n\nThe meazel, any equipment it is wearing or carrying, and any creature it is grappling teleport to an unoccupied space within 500 feet of it, provided that the starting space and the destination are in dim light or darkness. The destination must be a place the meazel has seen before, but it need not be within line of sight. If the destination space is occupied, the teleportation leads to the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nAny other creature the meazel teleports becomes cursed for 1 hour or until the curse is ended by remove curse or greater restoration. Until this curse ends, every Undead and every creature native to the Shadowfell within 300 feet of the cursed creature can sense it, which prevents that creature from hiding from them.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShadow Stealth\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, the meazel takes the Hide action."},
  ["creature.meazel.mtf2014"]={title="Meazel",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 35 (10d8 - 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 17 | CON 9 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShadow Stealth\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, the meazel can take the Hide action as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGarrote\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target of the meazel's size or smaller. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 13 with disadvantage). Until the grapple ends, the target takes 10 (2d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage at the start of each of the meazel's turns. The meazel can't make weapon attacks while grappling a creature in this way.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage, plus 3 (1d6) necrotic damage.\n\nShadow Teleport {@recharge 5}\n\nThe meazel, any equipment it is wearing or carrying, and any creature it is grappling teleport to an unoccupied space within 500 feet of it, provided that the starting space and the destination are in dim light or darkness. The destination must be a place the meazel has seen before, but it need not be within line of sight. If the destination space is occupied, the teleportation leads to the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nAny other creature the meazel teleports becomes cursed by shadow for 1 hour. Until this curse ends, every undead and every creature native to the Shadowfell within 300 feet of the cursed creature can sense it, which prevents that creature from hiding from them."},
  ["creature.mechachimera.oow2014"]={title="Mechachimera",subtitle="Criatura - OoW - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic"},
  ["vehicle.mechanical-beholder.ai2014"]={title="Mechanical Beholder",subtitle="Veiculo - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\nOn its turn the mechanical beholder can take 1 action. It cannot take any actions if it has no crew.\n\n• Eye Rays\n\n• Move"},
  ["creature.mechanical-bird.wdh2014"]={title="Mechanical Bird",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 46\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / T\n\nCR: Unknown\n\nCA: 15\n\nDeslocamento: fly: 60\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 0 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d3) piercing damage, and the bird is destroyed by the impact."},
  ["magicitem.mechanical-wonder-domestic.fraif2014"]={title="Mechanical Wonder (Domestic)",subtitle="Item Magico - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nA Mechanical Wonder is a semi-autonomous object imbued with magical power. Mechanical Wonders vary greatly in size and form depending on their function.\n\nA Mechanical Wonder is a dormant object until activated. To activate a Mechanical Wonder, you must wind the wonder with a handheld key unique to that wonder. It takes 1 minute to wind a Mechanical Wonder. While you wind it, you must take the XPHB action each turn.\n\nOnce wound, a Mechanical Wonder remains activated for the duration specified in the wonder's description.\n\nThis bipedal wonder is designed to assist with household duties. It vaguely resembles whatever species its creator used as inspiration. An activated domestic wonder uses the FRAiF stat block. The wonder is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, the wonder shares your XPHB count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you). If you don't issue any, it takes the XPHB action and uses its movement to avoid danger. The domestic wonder is destroyed if it drops to 0 XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.mechanical-wonder-flying.fraif2014"]={title="Mechanical Wonder (Flying)",subtitle="Item Magico - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nA Mechanical Wonder is a semi-autonomous object imbued with magical power. Mechanical Wonders vary greatly in size and form depending on their function.\n\nA Mechanical Wonder is a dormant object until activated. To activate a Mechanical Wonder, you must wind the wonder with a handheld key unique to that wonder. It takes 1 minute to wind a Mechanical Wonder. While you wind it, you must take the XPHB action each turn.\n\nOnce wound, a Mechanical Wonder remains activated for the duration specified in the wonder's description.\n\nAn activated flying wonder uses the FRAiF stat block. The wonder is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, the wonder shares your XPHB count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you). If you don't issue any, it takes the XPHB action and uses its movement to avoid danger. The flying wonder is destroyed if it drops to 0 XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.mechanical-wonder-gyrocopter.fraif2014"]={title="Mechanical Wonder (Gyrocopter)",subtitle="Item Magico - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA Mechanical Wonder is a semi-autonomous object imbued with magical power. Mechanical Wonders vary greatly in size and form depending on their function.\n\nA Mechanical Wonder is a dormant object until activated. To activate a Mechanical Wonder, you must wind the wonder with a handheld key unique to that wonder. It takes 1 minute to wind a Mechanical Wonder. While you wind it, you must take the XPHB action each turn.\n\nThis wagon-sized vehicle is made of brassy metal and has a spiral-shaped propeller atop it. Its midsection is open on two sides. Once wound, the gyrocopter wonder remains active for 8 hours. While active, the gyrocopter can be used as a vehicle; it requires one pilot.\n\nThe gyrocopter wonder is a Huge object that weighs 500 pounds and has the following statistics: AC 14, HP 50, XPHB 5 ft., and XPHB 20 ft. The gyrocopter can bear up to 2,000 pounds of cargo; if it bears any more than this, it deactivates.\n\nEight spectral cords are mounted to the inside of the cargo bay. A creature riding in the gyrocopter wonder can take a XPHB action to attach itself to or detach itself from one of these cords. A creature attached to a cord can leap from the gyrocopter wonder and glide, moving up to 5 feet horizontally for every 1 foot it descends in the air. If a creature attached to a cord is ever more than 500 feet away from the gyrocopter, the cord immediately disappears and returns to the wonder."},
  ["magicitem.mechanical-wonder-mobility.fraif2014"]={title="Mechanical Wonder (Mobility)",subtitle="Item Magico - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 246\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nA Mechanical Wonder is a semi-autonomous object imbued with magical power. Mechanical Wonders vary greatly in size and form depending on their function.\n\nA Mechanical Wonder is a dormant object until activated. To activate a Mechanical Wonder, you must wind the wonder with a handheld key unique to that wonder. It takes 1 minute to wind a Mechanical Wonder. While you wind it, you must take the XPHB action each turn.\n\nWhile inactive, the mobility wonder resembles a metal turtle shell with straps. It is designed to be worn on your back or flank, depending on your anatomy. Once wound, the mobility wonder transforms into a personal transport device and remains active for 24 hours. While active, the mobility wonder increases your XPHB to 30 feet. Other creatures can't remove your mobility wonder from you unless you allow it."},
  ["magicitem.medal-of-muscle.crcotn2014"]={title="Medal of Muscle",subtitle="Item Magico - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nYou can squeeze this medal tightly in the palm of your hand as an action. Doing so gives you advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws for 1 hour. Once this property has been used, it can't be used again, and the medal becomes nonmagical."},
  ["magicitem.medal-of-the-conch.crcotn2014"]={title="Medal of the Conch",subtitle="Item Magico - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhen you use an action to rub this medal, you gain a swimming speed equal to your walking speed for 1 hour. Once this property has been used, it can't be used again, and the medal becomes nonmagical."},
  ["magicitem.medal-of-the-horizonback.crcotn2014"]={title="Medal of the Horizonback",subtitle="Item Magico - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhen you would be hit by an attack, you can use your reaction to increase your AC by 5 until the start of your next turn, including against the triggering attack. You must be wearing the medal and able to see the creature that made the triggering attack to use this property. Once this property has been used, it can't be used again, and the medal becomes nonmagical."},
  ["magicitem.medal-of-the-maze.crcotn2014"]={title="Medal of the Maze",subtitle="Item Magico - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhen you use an action to trace the maze inscribed on this medal, you gain advantage on Wisdom checks and know the quickest route to the end of any nonmagical path or maze for 1 hour. Once this property has been used, it can't be used again, and the medal becomes nonmagical."},
  ["magicitem.medal-of-the-meat-pie.crcotn2014"]={title="Medal of the Meat Pie",subtitle="Item Magico - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nYou gain 2d4 + 2 temporary hit points when you use an action to press this medal to your mouth. Once this property has been used, it can't be used again, and the medal becomes nonmagical.\n\nWhile magical, this medal is slightly warm to the touch (as if it's fresh from the oven) and smells faintly of baked pie crust."},
  ["magicitem.medal-of-the-wetlands.crcotn2014"]={title="Medal of the Wetlands",subtitle="Item Magico - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhen you use an action to trace the edge of this medal, difficult terrain doesn't cost you extra movement for 1 hour. Once this property has been used, it can't be used again, and the medal becomes nonmagical."},
  ["magicitem.medal-of-wit.crcotn2014"]={title="Medal of Wit",subtitle="Item Magico - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nYou can press this medal to your temple as an action. Doing so gives you advantage on Intelligence checks and Intelligence saving throws for 1 hour. Once this property has been used, it can't be used again, and the medal becomes nonmagical."},
  ["magicitem.medallion-of-thoughts.dmg2014"]={title="Medallion of Thoughts",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 181\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThe medallion has 3 charges. While wearing it, you can use an action and expend 1 charge to cast the detect thoughts spell (save 13) from it. The medallion regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."},
  ["magicitem.medallion-of-thoughts.xdmg2024"]={title="Medallion of Thoughts",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 278\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThe medallion has 5 charges. While wearing it, you can expend 1 charge to cast XPHB (save 13) from it. The medallion regains 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn."},
  ["creature.medani-inquisitive.efa2014"]={title="Medani Inquisitive",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe inquisitive makes three Crooked Staff attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Inquisitive Eye.\n\nCrooked Staff\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition. If the target already has the XPHB condition, the attack deals an extra 7 (2d6) Radiant damage.\n\nInquisitive Eye\n\nwis 13, one creature the inquisitive can see within 60 feet. actSaveFail 10 (3d6) Psychic damage, and the target is marked. The inquisitive has XPHB on attack rolls against a target it has marked. While marked, the target can't become hidden from the inquisitive, and if it has the XPHB condition, it gains no benefit from that condition against the inquisitive. The mark disappears after 1 minute or when the inquisitive uses this action again. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSpontaneous Barrier {@recharge 4}\n\nactTrigger The inquisitive or an ally it can see is hit with an attack roll. actResponse The inquisitive adds 2 to its or the ally's AC against that attack, possibly causing it to miss."},
  ["feat.medium-armor-master.phb2014"]={title="Medium Armor Master",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\nYou have practiced moving in medium armor to gain the following benefits:\n\n• Wearing medium armor doesn't impose disadvantage on your Dexterity (Stealth) checks.\n\n• When you wear medium armor, you can add 3, rather than 2, to your AC if you have a Dexterity of 16 or higher."},
  ["feat.medium-armor-master.xphb2024"]={title="Medium Armor Master",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 205\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nDexterous Wearer\n\nWhile you're wearing Medium armor, you can add 3, rather than 2 to your AC if you have a Dexterity score of 16 or higher."},
  ["creature.medusa.mm2014"]={title="Medusa",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 127 (17d8 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPetrifying Gaze\n\nWhen a creature that can see the medusa's eyes starts its turn within 30 feet of the medusa, the medusa can force it to make a 14 Constitution saving throw if the medusa isn't incapacitated and can see the creature. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the creature is instantly petrified. Otherwise, a creature that fails the save begins to turn to stone and is restrained. The restrained creature must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn, becoming petrified on a failure or ending the effect on a success. The petrification lasts until the creature is freed by the greater restoration spell or other magic.\n\nUnless surprised, a creature can avert its eyes to avoid the saving throw at the start of its turn. If the creature does so, it can't see the medusa until the start of its next turn, when it can avert its eyes again. If the creature looks at the medusa in the meantime, it must immediately make the save.\n\nIf the medusa sees itself reflected on a polished surface within 30 feet of it and in an area of bright light, the medusa is, due to its curse, affected by its own gaze.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe medusa makes either three melee attacks—one with its snake hair and two with its shortsword—or two ranged attacks with its longbow.\n\nSnake Hair\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) poison damage.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage."},
  ["creature.medusa.mot2014"]={title="Medusa",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.medusa.wtthc2014"]={title="Medusa",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.medusa.xmm2024"]={title="Medusa",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 205\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 127 (17d8 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 150 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe medusa makes two Claw attacks and one Snake Hair attack, or it makes three Poison Ray attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage.\n\nSnake Hair\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) Poison damage.\n\nPoison Ray\n\nr 5, range 150 ft. h11 (2d8 + 2) Poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nPetrifying Gaze {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 13, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. If the medusa sees its reflection in the XPHB, the medusa must make this save. 1 The target has the XPHB condition and repeats the save at the end of its next turn if it is still XPHB, ending the effect on itself on a success. 2 The target has the XPHB condition instead of the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.meenlock.mpmm2014"]={title="Meenlock",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 178\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 31 (7d6 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFear Aura\n\nAny Beast or Humanoid that starts its turn within 10 feet of the meenlock must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the start of the creature's next turn.\n\nLight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in bright light, the meenlock has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d4 + 2) slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShadow Teleport {@recharge 5}\n\nThe meenlock teleports to an unoccupied space within 30 feet of it, provided that both the space it's teleporting from and its destination are in dim light or darkness. The destination need not be within line of sight."},
  ["creature.meenlock.vgm2014"]={title="Meenlock",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 170\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 31 (7d6 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFear Aura\n\nAny beast or humanoid that starts its turn within 10 feet of the meenlock must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the start of the creature's next turn.\n\nLight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in bright light, the meenlock has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nShadow Teleport {@recharge 5}\n\nAs a bonus action, the meenlock can teleport to an unoccupied space within 30 feet of it, provided that both the space it's teleporting from and its destination are in dim light or darkness. The destination need not be within line of sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d4 + 2) slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.meera-raheer.kftgv2014"]={title="Meera Raheer",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.meeseeks.rmbre2014"]={title="Meeseeks",subtitle="Criatura - RMBRE - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.megapede.bam2014"]={title="Megapede",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / G\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 175 (13d20 + 39)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe megapede makes one Bite attack and uses either Life Drain or Psychic Bomb.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h22 (3d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 22 (5d8) poison damage.\n\nLife Drain\n\nThe megapede magically drains life energy from other creatures nearby. Each creature within 15 feet of the megapede must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 16 (3d10) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nPsychic Bomb\n\nThe megapede targets one creature it can see within 60 feet of itself. The target must make a 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 22 (5d8) psychic damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage and isn't incapacitated."},
  ["creature.melannor-fellbranch.wdh2014"]={title="Melannor Fellbranch",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 11/16\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 15 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nMelannor has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put him to sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 2 to hit or Melee Weapon Attack 4 to hit with shillelagh, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage with shillelagh or if wielded with two hands."},
  ["spell.meld-into-stone.phb2014"]={title="Meld into Stone",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 259\n\nYou step into a stone object or surface large enough to fully contain your body, melding yourself and all the equipment you carry with the stone for the duration. Using your movement, you step into the stone at a point you can touch. Nothing of your presence remains visible or otherwise detectable by nonmagical senses.\n\nWhile merged with the stone, you can't see what occurs outside it, and any Wisdom (Perception) checks you make to hear sounds outside it are made with disadvantage. You remain aware of the passage of time and can cast spells on yourself while merged in the stone. You can use your movement to leave the stone where you entered it, which ends the spell. You otherwise can't move.\n\nMinor physical damage to the stone doesn't harm you, but its partial destruction or a change in its shape (to the extent that you no longer fit within it) expels you and deals 6d6 bludgeoning damage to you. The stone's complete destruction (or transmutation into a different substance) expels you and deals 50 bludgeoning damage to you. If expelled, you fall prone in an unoccupied space closest to where you first entered."},
  ["spell.meld-into-stone.xphb2024"]={title="Meld into Stone",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 296\n\nYou step into a stone object or surface large enough to fully contain your body, merging yourself and your equipment with the stone for the duration. You must touch the stone to do so. Nothing of your presence remains visible or otherwise detectable by nonmagical senses.\n\nWhile merged with the stone, you can't see what occurs outside it, and any Wisdom (XPHB) checks you make to hear sounds outside it are made with XPHB. You remain aware of the passage of time and can cast spells on yourself while merged in the stone. You can use 5 feet of movement to leave the stone where you entered it, which ends the spell. You otherwise can't move.\n\nMinor physical damage to the stone doesn't harm you, but its partial destruction or a change in its shape (to the extent that you no longer fit within it) expels you and deals 6d6 Force damage to you. The stone's complete destruction (or transmutation into a different substance) expels you and deals 50 Force damage to you. If expelled, you move into an unoccupied space closest to where you first entered and have the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.meletian-hoplite.mot2014"]={title="Meletian Hoplite",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 229\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 49 (9d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe hoplite makes three weapon attacks. It can replace one weapon attack with ray of frost.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage, or 7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nShield Bash\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nRay of Frost (Cantrip)\n\nrs 5 to hit, range 60 ft., one creature. h4 (1d8) cold damage, and the target's speed is reduced by 10 feet until the start of the hoplite's next turn."},
  ["spell.melf-s-acid-arrow.phb2014"]={title="Melf's Acid Arrow",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 259\n\nA shimmering green arrow streaks toward a target within range and bursts in a spray of acid. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 4d4 acid damage immediately and 2d4 acid damage at the end of its next turn. On a miss, the arrow splashes the target with acid for half as much of the initial damage and no damage at the end of its next turn."},
  ["spell.melf-s-acid-arrow.xphb2024"]={title="Melf's Acid Arrow",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 297\n\nA shimmering green arrow streaks toward a target within range and bursts in a spray of acid. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 4d4 Acid damage and 2d4 Acid damage at the end of its next turn. On a miss, the arrow splashes the target with acid for half as much of the initial damage only."},
  ["spell.melf-s-minute-meteors.xge2024"]={title="Melf's Minute Meteors",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 161\n\nYou create six tiny meteors in your space. They float in the air and orbit you for the spell's duration. When you cast the spell—and as a bonus action on each of your turns thereafter—you can expend one or two of the meteors, sending them streaking toward a point or points you choose within 120 feet of you. Once a meteor reaches its destination or impacts against a solid surface, the meteor explodes. Each creature within 5 feet of the point where the meteor explodes must make a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 2d6 fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["deity.melira-taralen.mtf2014"]={title="Melira Taralen",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["creature.melissara-shadowdusk.wdmm2014"]={title="Melissara Shadowdusk",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 281\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nIdiomas: Common, Deep Speech, Draconic, Dwarvish"},
  ["creature.meloon-wardragon.wdh2014"]={title="Meloon Wardragon",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 143 (22d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Deep Speech, telepathy 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nMeloon wields wdh but can't attune to it, and thus gains none of its benefits.\n\nIndomitable (2/Day)\n\nMeloon can reroll a saving throw that he fails. He must use the new roll.\n\nSecond Wind (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nAs a bonus action, Meloon can regain 20 hit points.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMeloon makes four attacks with Azuredge.\n\nAzuredge\n\nm 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (1d12 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["deity.melora.dmg2014"]={title="Melora",subtitle="Divindade - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 10"},
  ["deity.melora.egw2014"]={title="Melora",subtitle="Divindade - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\nThe realm of Melora extends to wherever the seas shift and the land grows wild. As the keeper of the wilderness, Melora represents the wild creatures of nature, the rush of the angry rapids, and the heat-heavy stillness of the desert. Elves worship her, as do hunters, accepting her guidance to exist harmoniously within savage lands. Those seeking safe passage across dangerous waters pray to her to guide them.\n\nFollowers of the Raven Queen also show respect to the Wild Mother as the caretaker of what remains when the Matron of Death's work is done. Those of Ki'Nau descent often make offerings to Melora, considering her a collective entity that represents their ancient nature gods within a singular feminine form. Druids of Melora the Wild Mother and clerics of her lover, Erathis the Law Bearer, work together to preserve the balance of nature and civilization. However, worship of Melora was outlawed in the Dwendalian Empire, causing disagreement between clerics of Erathis within Western Wynandir, where many blame poor weather and natural disasters on the ire of their deity's partner.\n\nEschewing a permanent realm, Melora prefers to wander the planes to oversee natural life. She is often found among the unearthly beauty of Arvandor's infinite expanse of deep woods, hunting unnatural things that corrupt the wilds.\n\nDepiction\n\nImmortalized through wooden reliefs and carved idols in hidden, overgrown groves and rural shrines, the Wild Mother is shown as a beautiful woman with green skin nearly swallowed by a wild, tangled wreath of hair, leaves, and vines that dwarf her lithe form.\n\nHoly Day\n\nMelora's holy day is Wild's Grandeur, which is celebrated on the vernal equinox, usually the twentieth day of the third month. The people of the Menagerie Coast set aside this day to sail for no reason other than the pleasure of observing the natural beauty of their surroundings. Those who still partake in elements of Ki'Nau culture take this day to appreciate the fruits and foods granted by the sea, leaving offerings of delicacies and small handmade crafts at temporary altars of twisted roots and grasses.\n\nCommandments of Melora\n\n• Protect the untamed wilderness from exploitation and destruction.\n\n• Slay abominations and other mockeries of nature.\n\n• Embrace and respect the savage nature of the world. Exist in harmony with it."},
  ["feature.memorize-spell.xphb2024.wizard.base.5"]={title="Memorize Spell",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 167\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can study your spellbook and replace one of the level 1+ Wizard spells you have prepared for your Spellcasting feature with another level 1+ spell from the book."},
  ["feature.memory-of-one-thousand-steps.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.nomad.3"]={title="Memory of One Thousand Steps",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\nAt 3rd level, you gain the ability to use psionics to recall your steps. As a reaction when you are hit by an attack, you can teleport to an unoccupied space that you occupied since the start of your last turn, and the attack misses you. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."},
  ["creature.memory-web.qftis2014"]={title="Memory Web",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 39 (6d10 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 18 | CON 13 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (can't see beyond this radius)\n\nResistencias: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDamage Transfer\n\nWhile it is grappling a creature, the memory web takes only half the damage dealt to it, and the creature grappled by the web takes the other half.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the memory web is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the memory web move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the memory web is animate.\n\nMemory Flood\n\nWhen the memory web is reduced to 0 hit points, it discharges any memories it consumed over the past 24 hours in a telepathic deluge. Hazy, dreamlike visions of these discharged memories lodge in the minds of creatures up to 120 feet from the memory web.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nEnsnare\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Large or smaller creature. hThe target has the grappled condition (escape 13). Until this grapple ends, the target has the restrained condition and takes 7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage at the start of each of its turns. The memory web can grapple only one creature at a time.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDrain Memories\n\nThe memory web targets one creature grappled by it. The target must make a 12 Intelligence saving throw. Constructs, Oozes, Plants, and Undead succeed on the save automatically. On a failed save, the target takes 5 (2d4) psychic damage and becomes memory drained until it finishes a long rest or the memory web is destroyed.\n\nWhile memory drained, the target must roll a d4 each time it makes an ability check or attack roll, subtracting the d4 roll from it. Each time the target is memory drained beyond the first, the die size increases by one: the d4 becomes a d6, the d6 becomes a d8, and so on until the die becomes a d20, at which point the target has the unconscious condition for 1 hour. If a memory drained creature is the target of the Greater Restoration or Heal spell, the memory drained effect ends on it. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only."},
  ["optionalfeature.menacing-attack.phb2014"]={title="Menacing Attack",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 74\n\nWhen you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to frighten the target. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it is frightened of you until the end of your next turn."},
  ["optionalfeature.menacing-attack.xphb2024"]={title="Menacing Attack",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 95\n\nWhen you hit a creature with an attack roll, you can expend one Superiority Die to attempt to frighten the target. Add the Superiority Die to the attack's damage roll. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition until the end of your next turn."},
  ["creature.mend-nets.rot2014"]={title="Mend-nets",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["spell.mending.phb2014"]={title="Mending",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 259\n\nThis spell repairs a single break or tear in an object you touch, such as broken chain link, two halves of a broken key, a torn cloak, or a leaking wineskin. As long as the break or tear is no larger than 1 foot in any dimension, you mend it, leaving no trace of the former damage.\n\nThis spell can physically repair a magic item or construct, but the spell can't restore magic to such an object."},
  ["spell.mending.xphb2024"]={title="Mending",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 297\n\nThis spell repairs a single break or tear in an object you touch, such as a broken chain link, two halves of a broken key, a torn cloak, or a leaking wineskin. As long as the break or tear is no larger than 1 foot in any dimension, you mend it, leaving no trace of the former damage.\n\nThis spell can physically repair a magic item, but it can't restore magic to such an object."},
  ["item.menga-leaves-1-ounce.toa2014"]={title="Menga leaves (1 ounce)",subtitle="Item - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nThe dried leaves of a menga bush can be ground, dissolved in a liquid, heated, and ingested. A creature that ingests 1 ounce of menga leaves in this fashion regains 1 hit point. A creature that ingests more than 5 ounces of menga leaves in a 24-hour period gains no additional benefit and must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or fall unconscious for 1 hour. The unconscious creature awakens if it takes at least 5 damage on one turn.\n\nA healthy menga bush usually has 2d6 ounces of leaves. Once picked, the leaves require 1 day to dry out before they can confer any benefit."},
  ["creature.mennek-ariz.tftyp2014"]={title="Mennek Ariz",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["spell.mental-prison.xge2024"]={title="Mental Prison",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 161\n\nYou attempt to bind a creature within an illusory cell that only it perceives. One creature you can see within range must make an Intelligence saving throw. The target succeeds automatically if it is immune to being charmed. On a successful save, the target takes 5d10 psychic damage, and the spell ends. On a failed save, the target takes 5d10 psychic damage, and you make the area immediately around the target's space appear dangerous to it in some way. You might cause the target to perceive itself as being surrounded by fire, floating razors, or hideous maws filled with dripping teeth. Whatever form the illusion takes, the target can't see or hear anything beyond it and is restrained for the spell's duration. If the target is moved out of the illusion, makes a melee attack through it, or reaches any part of its body through it, the target takes 10d10 psychic damage, and the spell ends."},
  ["creature.mephistopheles.coa2014"]={title="Mephistopheles",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 27\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 460 (40d10 + 240)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 100\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 23 | CON 22 | INT 30 | WIS 28 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede Mephistopheles' darkvision.\n\nFiendish Regeneration\n\nMephistopheles regains 20 hit points at the start of his turn. If he takes radiant damage this trait doesn't function at the start of his next turn. Mephistopheles only dies if he starts his turn with 0 hit points and is unable to regenerate.\n\nFlyby\n\nMephistopheles doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when he flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nHellfire Mastery\n\nFire damage that Mephistopheles inflicts ignores resistances and immunities. Mephistopheles is immune to this effect.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Mephistopheles fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nMephistopheles has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMephistopheles makes three Ranseur attacks. He can replace one of the attacks with Hellfire Lash (if available).\n\nRanseur +3\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) piercing damage plus 18 (4d8) fire or cold damage (Mephistopheles' choice).\n\nHellfire Implosion {@recharge 4}\n\nA bright streak of Hellfire appears at a point that Mephistopheles can see within 150 feet of him. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw. Targets take 31 (9d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nHellfire Lash {@recharge 5}\n\nMephistopheles unleashes a 60-foot-long, 5-foot-wide lash of Hellfire that ignites a 5-foot- radius sphere around where it strikes. Any targets in the area of effect must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAshen Teleport\n\nMephistopheles' body and any equipment he is wearing or carrying turns to ash, then he magically teleports up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space he can see and reforms.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nHellfire Wings\n\nMephistopheles uses his wings to generate a burst of heat. Each creature within 10 feet of him must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or take 9 (2d8) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) fire damage. Creatures that failed the save also have the prone condition.\n\nHellfire Storm (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nMephistopheles creates a rain of Hellfire at a point he can see within 150 feet. Each creature within a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 24 Dexterity saving throw. Targets take 38 (7d10) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nCall Underling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nMephistopheles summons an allied horned devil in an unoccupied space that he can see."},
  ["creature.mephistopheles.mabjov2014"]={title="Mephistopheles",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 101\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 27\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 460 (40d10 + 240)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 100\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 23 | CON 22 | INT 30 | WIS 28 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede Mephistopheles' darkvision.\n\nFiendish Regeneration\n\nMephistopheles regains 20 hit points at the start of his turn. If he takes radiant damage this trait doesn't function at the start of his next turn. Mephistopheles only dies if he starts his turn with 0 hit points and is unable to regenerate.\n\nFlyby\n\nMephistopheles doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when he flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nHellfire Mastery\n\nFire damage that Mephistopheles inflicts ignores resistances and immunities. Mephistopheles is immune to this effect.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Mephistopheles fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nMephistopheles has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMephistopheles makes three Ranseur attacks. He can replace one of the attacks with Hellfire Lash (if available).\n\nRanseur, +3\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) piercing plus 18 (4d8) fire or cold damage (Mephistopheles' choice).\n\nHellfire Implosion {@recharge 4}\n\nA bright streak of Hellfire appears at a point that Mephistopheles can see within 150 feet of him. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw. Targets take 31 (9d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nHellfire Lash {@recharge 5}\n\nMephistopheles unleashes a 60-foot-long, 5-foot-wide lash of Hellfire that ignites a 5-foot-radius sphere around where it strikes. Any targets in the area of effect must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAshen Teleport\n\nMephistopheles' body and any equipment he is wearing or carrying turns to ash, then he magically teleports up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space he can see and reforms.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nHellfire Wings\n\nMephistopheles uses his wings to generate a burst of heat. Each creature within 10 feet of him must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or take 9 (2d8) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) fire damage. Creatures that failed the save also have the prone condition.\n\nHellfire Storm (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nMephistopheles creates a rain of Hellfire at a point he can see within 150 feet. Each creature within a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 24 Dexterity saving throw. Targets take 38 (7d10) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nCall Underling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nMephistopheles summons an allied horned devil in an unoccupied space that he can see."},
  ["creature.mercane.bam2014"]={title="Mercane",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 75 (10d10 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 18 | WIS 16 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant, telepathy 60 ft. (see also Mercane telepathy)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMercane Telepathy\n\nThe mercane can communicate telepathically with any other mercane it knows, regardless of the distance between them.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe mercane makes three Psi-Imbued Blade attacks.\n\nPsi-Imbued Blade\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened of the mercane until the end of the target's next turn."},
  ["creature.mercenary-envoy.aitfr-fcd2014"]={title="Mercenary Envoy",subtitle="Criatura - AitFR-FCD - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 26 (4d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 15 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nInspired Courage\n\nThe mercenary has advantage on savings throws against being charmed, frightened, grappled, or restrained while within 5 feet of at least one ally.\n\nMartial Advantage\n\nOnce per turn, the mercenary can deal an extra 7 (2d6) damage to a creature it hits with a weapon attack if that creature is within 5 feet of an ally of the mercenary that isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe mercenary makes two longsword attacks.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range\n\n100/400 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["background.mercenary-veteran.scag2014"]={title="Mercenary Veteran",subtitle="Background - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Mercenary Life\n\nYou know the mercenary life as only someone who has experienced it can. You are able to identify mercenary companies by their emblems, and you know a little about any such company, including who has hired them recently. You can find the taverns and festhalls where mercenaries abide in any area, as long as you speak the language. You can find mercenary work between adventures sufficient to maintain a comfortable lifestyle (see \"PHB\" under \"Downtime Activities\" in chapter 8 of the Player's Handbook).\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nUse the tables for the soldier background in the Player's Handbook as the basis for your traits and motivations, modifying the entries when appropriate to suit your identity as a mercenary.\n\nYour bond could be associated with the company you traveled with previously, or with some of the comrades you served with. The ideal you embrace largely depends on your worldview and your motivation for fighting."},
  ["background.merchant.xphb2024"]={title="Merchant",subtitle="Background - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 182\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiency:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["item.merchant-s-scale.phb2014"]={title="Merchant's Scale",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA scale includes a small balance, pans, and a suitable assortment of weights up to 2 pounds. With it, you can measure the exact weight of small objects, such as raw precious metals or trade goods, to help determine their worth."},
  ["creature.mercion.wbtw2014"]={title="Mercion",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 31 (9d8 - 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 10 | CON 9 | INT 12 | WIS 17 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nMercion wields a +1 quarterstaff.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMercion makes one Divine Radiance attack and one +1 Quarterstaff attack. She can replace one of these attacks with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nDivine Radiance\n\nms,rs 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h13 (3d8) radiant damage.\n\n+1 Quarterstaff\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage, or 7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage when used with two hands.\n\nRadiant Fire {@recharge 5}\n\nMercion creates a magical explosion of fiery radiance centered on a point she can see within 120 feet of her. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.mercykiller-bloodhound.mpp2014"]={title="Mercykiller Bloodhound",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 104 (16d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 15 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one more language\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPortal Sense\n\nThe bloodhound can sense the presence of portals within 30 feet of itself, including inactive portals, and instinctively knows the destination of each portal.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bloodhound makes three Clawed Gauntlet attacks.\n\nClawed Gauntlet\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) necrotic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nMarked for Pursuit (3/Day)\n\nThe bloodhound attempts to place a magical mark on a creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 13 Charisma saving throw or become cursed for 24 hours. A creature missing any of its hit points has disadvantage on this saving throw. While cursed in this way, the bloodhound can sense the direction and distance to the target as long as the two are on the same plane of existence. If the target isn't on the same plane, the bloodhound knows what plane the target is on."},
  ["species.merfolk.dmg2014"]={title="Merfolk",subtitle="Especie - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nAmphibious\n\nYou can breathe air and water.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Aquan."},
  ["language.merfolk.ggr2014"]={title="Merfolk",subtitle="Idioma - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["creature.merfolk.mm2014"]={title="Merfolk",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 40\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 13 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe merfolk can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) piercing damage, or 4 (1d8) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack."},
  ["language.merfolk.psx2014"]={title="Merfolk",subtitle="Idioma - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 6"},
  ["species.merfolk.psz2014"]={title="Merfolk",subtitle="Especie - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\nAge\n\nMerfolk mature at the same rate humans do and reach adulthood around the age of 20. They live considerably longer than humans, though, often reaching well over 100 years.\n\nAlignment\n\nMost merfolk are neutral, though merfolk of the Emeria and Cosi creeds have chaotic leanings.\n\nAmphibious\n\nYou can breathe air and water.\n\nSize\n\nMerfolk are about the same size and build as humans. Your size is Medium.\n\nSwimming\n\nYou have a swimming speed of 30 feet.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common, Merfolk, and one extra language of your choice."},
  ["creature.merfolk-salvager.gos2014"]={title="Merfolk Salvager",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 244\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe salvager can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe salvager makes two attacks with its coral rapier.\n\nCoral Rapier\n\nm 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nInject Toxin (2/Day)\n\nm 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage, and the creature must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.merfolk-scout.gos2014"]={title="Merfolk Scout",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.merfolk-skirmisher.xmm2024"]={title="Merfolk Skirmisher",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 40\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 13 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nIdiomas: Common, Primordial (Aquan)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe merfolk can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nOcean Spear\n\nm,r 2, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h3 (1d6) Piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) Cold damage. If the target is a creature, its XPHB decreases by 10 feet until the end of its next turn. homThe spear magically returns to the merfolk's hand immediately after a ranged attack."},
  ["creature.merfolk-wavebender.xmm2024"]={title="Merfolk Wavebender",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 97 (15d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 40\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 19 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Primordial (Aquan)\n\nResistencias: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe merfolk can breathe air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merfolk makes two Aquatic Burst attacks.\n\nAquatic Burst\n\nm,r 7, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. h20 (3d10 + 4) Cold damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nWatery Rebuke\n\nactTrigger An enemy the merfolk can see enters a space within 5 feet of the merfolk. dstr 15, the triggering enemy. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Cold damage. If the target is Large or smaller, it is pushed up to 30 feet straight away from the merfolk by conjured water."},
  ["creature.meri.crcotn2014"]={title="Meri",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.merregon.mpmm2014"]={title="Merregon",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 179\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Infernal but can't speak, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the merregon's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe merregon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merregon makes three Halberd attacks.\n\nHalberd\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nLoyal Bodyguard\n\nWhen another Fiend within 5 feet of the merregon is hit by an attack roll, the merregon causes itself to be hit instead."},
  ["creature.merregon.mtf2014"]={title="Merregon",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 166\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Infernal but can't speak, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the merregon's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe merregon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merregon makes two halberd attacks, or if an allied fiend of challenge rating 6 or higher is within 60 feet of it, the merregon makes three halberd attacks.\n\nHalberd\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nLoyal Bodyguard\n\nWhen another fiend within 5 feet of the merregon is hit by an attack, the merregon causes itself to be hit instead."},
  ["creature.merrenoloth.mpmm2014"]={title="Merrenoloth",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 17 | CON 10 | INT 17 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Infernal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe merrenoloth has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merrenoloth makes one Oar attack and uses Fear Gaze.\n\nOar\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (2d4 + 3) fire damage.\n\nFear Gaze\n\nThe merrenoloth targets one creature it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of the merrenoloth for 1 minute. The frightened target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTeleport\n\nThe merrenoloth teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.merrenoloth.mtf2014"]={title="Merrenoloth",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 250\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 17 | CON 10 | INT 17 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Infernal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe merrenoloth has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe merrenoloth's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nTeleport\n\nAs a bonus action, the merrenoloth magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merrenoloth uses Fear Gaze once and makes one oar attack.\n\nOar\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (2d4 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nFear Gaze\n\nThe merrenoloth targets one creature it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. The frightened target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.merrow.mm2014"]={title="Merrow",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Aquan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe merrow can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merrow makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws or harpoon.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d4 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nHarpoon\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it must succeed on a Strength contest against the merrow or be pulled up to 20 feet toward the merrow."},
  ["creature.merrow.xmm2024"]={title="Merrow",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Primordial (Aquan)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe merrow can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merrow makes two attacks, using Bite, Claw, or Harpoon in any combination.\n\nBite\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d4 + 4) Piercing damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the merrow's next turn.\n\nClaw\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage.\n\nHarpoon\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, the merrow pulls the target up to 15 feet straight toward itself."},
  ["creature.merrow-doublespeaker.lfl2014"]={title="Merrow Doublespeaker",subtitle="Criatura - LFL - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 67 (9d8 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Primordial (Aquan)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe merrow can breathe air and water.\n\nMimicry\n\nThe merrow can mimic voices and animal sounds. A creature that hears the mimicries can tell they are imitations with a successful 15 Wisdom (XPHB) check.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merrow makes three Spined Tail attacks. It can replace one of these attacks with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nSpined Tail\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h14 (3d6 + 4) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.merrow-extortionist.dosi2014"]={title="Merrow Extortionist",subtitle="Criatura - DoSI - 2014",body="Pagina: 0\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 30 (4d10 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Aquan, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe merrow can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merrow makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (2d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.merrow-haranguer.lfl2014"]={title="Merrow Haranguer",subtitle="Criatura - LFL - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 90 (12d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Primordial (Aquan)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe merrow can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe merrow makes three attacks, using Coral Scepter and Poisoned Longbow in any combination.\n\nCoral Scepter\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h14 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nPoisoned Longbow\n\nr 7, range 150/600 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage.\n\nInvective\n\nwis 15, up to three creatures the merrow can see within 60 feet. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Psychic damage, and the creature has XPHB on its next attack roll before the end of the merrow's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["creature.merrow-shallowpriest.egw2014"]={title="Merrow Shallowpriest",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 294\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 75 (10d10 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 11 | WIS 16 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Aquan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe merrow can breathe air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHarpoon\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, the merrow can pull it 10 feet closer.\n\nLightning Bolt (3rd-Level Spell; Requires a Spell Slot)\n\nThe merrow unleashes a stroke of lightning in a line 100 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in the line must make a 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["deity.merrshaulk.vgm2014"]={title="Merrshaulk",subtitle="Divindade - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nThough the Master of the Pit is not conscious, neither is he entirely dormant. Mirroring the fate of yuan-ti in the world, Merrshaulk entered a deep slumber when the serpent folk left the surface and went into hiding in ages past. It is unclear if declining worship caused him to fall asleep, or if his prolonged torpor caused his worshipers to abandon him. Even in his compromised state, Merrshaulk grants spells to his clergy in response to their invocations. Rousing him for advice or direct intervention is possible, but requires many ritual murders to be performed in his name, and his return to consciousness lasts only a short time.\n\nThe leaders of Merrshaulk's worshipers, called pit masters, are malison warlocks that uphold and advance the age-old yuan-ti traditions. They sense that it has become easier to wake him in recent decades, and believe this to be a sign that he will soon fully awaken, shed his skin, and-renewed by transformation-restore the yuan-ti to their rightful place as masters of the mortal world."},
  ["item.mess-kit.phb2014"]={title="Mess Kit",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis tin box contains a cup and simple cutlery. The box clamps together, and one side can be used as a cooking pan and the other as a plate or shallow bowl."},
  ["spell.message.phb2014"]={title="Message",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 259\n\nYou point your finger toward a creature within range and whisper a message. The target (and only the target) hears the message and can reply in a whisper that only you can hear.\n\nYou can cast this spell through solid objects if you are familiar with the target and know it is beyond the barrier. Magical silence, 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, a thin sheet of lead, or 3 feet of wood blocks the spell. The spell doesn't have to follow a straight line and can travel freely around corners or through openings."},
  ["spell.message.xphb2024"]={title="Message",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 298\n\nYou point toward a creature within range and whisper a message. The target (and only the target) hears the message and can reply in a whisper that only you can hear.\n\nYou can cast this spell through solid objects if you are familiar with the target and know it is beyond the barrier. Magical silence; 1 foot of stone, metal, or wood; or a thin sheet of lead blocks the spell."},
  ["creature.metal-wasp.wdmm2014"]={title="Metal Wasp",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 174\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 24 (3d8)\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned"},
}
